(864, '2a94d39c-2cf0-4217-a7b1-a565afd8e04e', 134, 3, 'What does the Arabic word \"Tawhid\" linguistically mean?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"To divide\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"To make one \\\\\\/ to unify\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"To worship\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"To submit\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Tawhid comes from the Arabic word \"wahhada\" meaning \"to make one\" or \"to unify\". It refers to the Oneness of Allah.', 'Think about the root word \"wahid\" (one) in Arabic.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"tawhid\\\",\\\"definition\\\",\\\"basics\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(865, 'e0a3239b-c99b-4d09-b5ba-7ee637a2dc98', 134, 3, 'Which Surah of the Quran is most associated with the concept of Tawhid?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Surah Al-Fatiha\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Surah Al-Baqarah\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Surah Al-Ikhlas\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Surah An-Nisa\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Surah Al-Ikhlas (112) states \"Say: He is Allah, the One,\" making it the most direct declaration of Tawhid in the Quran.', 'This Surah is known as the chapter of Sincerity/Purity.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"tawhid\\\",\\\"quran\\\",\\\"surah\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(866, '10aeb9b3-b895-4d2c-87a6-37a0e8759bdf', 134, 3, 'How many types of Tawhid are there according to Islamic theology?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"2\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"4\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"5\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'There are three types of Tawhid: Tawhid ar-Rububiyyah (Lordship), Tawhid al-Uluhiyyah (Worship), and Tawhid al-Asma wa as-Sifat (Names & Attributes).', 'Count: Lordship, Worship, Names & Attributes.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"tawhid\\\",\\\"types\\\",\\\"basics\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(867, 'e0b6ba36-c2a7-43c9-819a-b30d37fd7587', 134, 3, 'Tawhid is considered which pillar of Iman (faith)?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Second\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Third\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Fourth\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"First\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'Tawhid (belief in the Oneness of Allah) is the first and most fundamental pillar of Iman (faith).', 'It is the foundation upon which all other pillars rest.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"tawhid\\\",\\\"iman\\\",\\\"pillars\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(868, '24fcfadc-4c3f-4bc6-bea2-83680627f350', 134, 3, 'What does Tawhid ar-Rububiyyah refer to?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Oneness of Names & Attributes\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Oneness of Worship\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Oneness of Lordship\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Oneness of Prophethood\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Tawhid ar-Rububiyyah refers to believing that Allah alone is the Creator, Owner, Sustainer, and Manager of everything in the universe.', 'Rabb means Lord in Arabic.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"tawhid\\\",\\\"rububiyyah\\\",\\\"lordship\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(869, 'b01e7cc9-9063-4cb6-b2e8-a0ac95c0c850', 134, 3, 'Which type of Tawhid involves believing that only Allah deserves to be worshipped?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Tawhid ar-Rububiyyah\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Tawhid al-Uluhiyyah\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Tawhid al-Asma wa as-Sifat\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"None of the above\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Tawhid al-Uluhiyyah refers to believing that only Allah deserves worship. All acts of worship (prayer, fasting, supplication) must be for Allah alone.', 'Ilah means deity/god in Arabic.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"tawhid\\\",\\\"uluhiyyah\\\",\\\"worship\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(870, 'a61830eb-fcdb-48bf-8dbc-c18f7f380d09', 134, 3, 'Which type of Tawhid did even the polytheists of Makkah believe in?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Tawhid al-Uluhiyyah\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Tawhid al-Asma wa as-Sifat\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Tawhid ar-Rububiyyah\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"All three types\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The polytheists of Makkah believed in Tawhid ar-Rububiyyah (that Allah created the heavens and earth), but they committed shirk in worship by directing some acts of worship to idols.', 'The Quran confirms: \"If you ask them who created the heavens and earth, they will say: Allah.\" (31:25)', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"tawhid\\\",\\\"rububiyyah\\\",\\\"mushrikeen\\\",\\\"makkah\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(871, 'f9fbfa1e-fecd-4e07-a76f-04512e4a4b6e', 134, 3, 'Which type of Tawhid is considered the most important because it distinguishes a Muslim from a disbeliever?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Tawhid ar-Rububiyyah\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Tawhid al-Asma wa as-Sifat\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Tawhid al-Uluhiyyah\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"All are equally important\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Tawhid al-Uluhiyyah is the most important type because it is the basis of Islamic declaration of faith (Shahadah) and distinguishes a true Muslim from a disbeliever.', 'The polytheists were fought over which type of Tawhid they violated?', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"tawhid\\\",\\\"uluhiyyah\\\",\\\"importance\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(872, '3eebe586-d483-47d6-b5e0-d82f1e3b3413', 134, 3, 'What does Tawhid al-Asma wa as-Sifat require a believer to avoid regarding Allah\'s attributes?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Affirming them\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Distorting, denying, comparing or questioning how\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Translating them\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Memorizing them\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Regarding Allah\'s Names and Attributes, one must avoid: Tahreef (distortion), Ta\'teel (denial), Takyeef (asking how), and Tashbih (comparison to creation).', 'The four forbidden acts start with T in Arabic: Tahreef, Ta\'teel, Takyeef, Tashbih.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"tawhid\\\",\\\"asma\\\",\\\"sifat\\\",\\\"attributes\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(873, '09fd4c0f-1343-48c1-a955-8b905d4cbaba', 134, 3, 'Which Surah (verse 42:11) states \"There is nothing like unto Him, and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Seeing\"?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Surah Al-Ikhlas\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Surah Ash-Shura\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Surah Al-Baqarah\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Surah Al-A\'raf\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Surah Ash-Shura (42:11) is the Quranic evidence for Tawhid al-Asma wa as-Sifat, affirming that Allah\'s attributes are unique and nothing resembles Him.', 'Ash-Shura means \"The Consultation.\"', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"tawhid\\\",\\\"quran\\\",\\\"asma\\\",\\\"sifat\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(874, 'f7856e57-379b-4518-99e7-6e8d356bfc97', 134, 3, 'According to Surah Al-A\'raf 7:54, what is the Quranic evidence for Tawhid ar-Rububiyyah?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Allah commands worship\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Allah created the heavens and earth in six days and manages all affairs\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Allah has beautiful names\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Allah sends prophets\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Surah Al-A\'raf 7:54 states: \"Indeed your Lord is Allah who created the heavens and earth in six days...\" This is evidence for Tawhid ar-Rububiyyah — Allah\'s exclusive role as Creator and Manager.', 'This verse from Al-A\'raf describes creation and management of the universe.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"tawhid\\\",\\\"rububiyyah\\\",\\\"quran\\\",\\\"evidence\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(875, 'cba4f006-b0e1-4cd7-b402-32669297b7c0', 134, 3, 'In Tawhid al-Asma wa as-Sifat, what does \"Ta\'teel\" refer to?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Comparing Allah\'s attributes to creation\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Affirming Allah\'s attributes\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Completely denying Allah\'s attributes\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Asking how Allah\'s attributes are\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Ta\'teel means to completely deny Allah\'s attributes (e.g., saying Allah has no hand, no hearing). This is forbidden. We must affirm what Allah affirmed for Himself without denial.', 'Ta\'teel is the opposite of affirmation (Ithbat).', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"tawhid\\\",\\\"tateel\\\",\\\"asma\\\",\\\"sifat\\\",\\\"hard\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(876, '63da7d53-c57f-4c9b-be29-82e1ef490ba4', 134, 3, 'Which statement correctly describes the relationship between Tawhid ar-Rububiyyah and entry into Islam?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"It is sufficient for a person to enter Islam\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"It is not sufficient alone \\\\u2014 one must also have Tawhid al-Uluhiyyah\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"It is the highest form of Tawhid\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"It was unknown to the Arabs before Islam\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Tawhid ar-Rububiyyah alone is NOT sufficient. Even the Makkan polytheists believed in it yet were disbelievers. One must also have Tawhid al-Uluhiyyah — directing all worship exclusively to Allah.', 'The polytheists of Makkah had Rububiyyah but lacked Uluhiyyah.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"tawhid\\\",\\\"rububiyyah\\\",\\\"uluhiyyah\\\",\\\"distinction\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(877, 'c469f0b5-a1c8-4ac9-94e9-2697bd3e346f', 134, 3, 'What is Shirk in Islamic theology?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Believing in prophets\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Associating partners with Allah\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Performing extra prayers\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Fasting voluntarily\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Shirk means associating partners with Allah in His Lordship, Worship, or Names & Attributes. It is the greatest sin in Islam.', 'The word Shirk means \"to associate\" or \"to share\" in Arabic.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"shirk\\\",\\\"definition\\\",\\\"basics\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(878, '2d371217-8552-4de0-8b98-baf0200ae199', 134, 3, 'What is the greatest sin in Islam?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Murder\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Theft\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Major Shirk\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Lying\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Major Shirk (associating partners with Allah) is the greatest sin in Islam. The Quran states: \"Indeed, Allah does not forgive association with Him (Shirk).\" (4:48)', 'Allah forgives all sins except one.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"shirk\\\",\\\"greatest\\\",\\\"sin\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(879, '4ed223ac-cd20-4f1a-a0d2-2c3501a72e44', 134, 3, 'How many main types of Shirk are there?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"4\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"2\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"5\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'There are two main types of Shirk: Major Shirk (Shirk Akbar) which takes a person out of Islam, and Minor Shirk (Shirk Asghar) which does not exit one from Islam.', 'Major and Minor are the two categories.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"shirk\\\",\\\"types\\\",\\\"basics\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(880, '3099c980-bfe5-4104-b16d-2d0e8949cf2d', 134, 3, 'What is Ar-Riya in Islamic terminology?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Sincere worship\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Showing off in acts of worship\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Prostration to Allah\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Seeking forgiveness\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Ar-Riya means showing off or performing acts of worship to gain praise from people rather than seeking Allah\'s pleasure. It is an example of Minor Shirk.', 'The Prophet ﷺ called it the thing he feared most for his companions.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"shirk\\\",\\\"riya\\\",\\\"minor\\\",\\\"showing-off\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(881, '05eb6997-0539-4af6-ae5c-b9d69947cece', 134, 3, 'What is the consequence of Major Shirk (Shirk Akbar) on a person\'s good deeds?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Good deeds are reduced\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Good deeds become null and void\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Good deeds are accepted despite shirk\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Good deeds are doubled\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Major Shirk nullifies all good deeds. The Quran states: \"If they had associated partners with Allah, all that they did would have been worthless.\" (Surah Al-An\'am 6:88)', 'The Quran in Surah Al-An\'am 6:88 addresses this consequence.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"shirk\\\",\\\"major\\\",\\\"deeds\\\",\\\"consequence\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(882, '32017dbe-23c4-431e-a2ae-d0b4426902f5', 134, 3, 'Which of the following is an example of Major Shirk (Shirk Akbar)?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Saying \\\\\\\"What Allah wills and you will\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Praying longer to impress others\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Prostrating and praying to an idol\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Swearing by the Prophet\'s name\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Prostrating or praying to an idol is Major Shirk because it directs an act of worship to other than Allah. Options A, B, and D are examples of Minor Shirk.', 'Major Shirk involves directing core worship acts to other than Allah.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"shirk\\\",\\\"major\\\",\\\"examples\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(883, '27aa9500-9391-43d6-af49-fb7675ac47c6', 134, 3, 'According to a Hadith in Musnad Ahmad, what did the Prophet ﷺ say he feared most for his companions?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Major Shirk\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Minor Shirk \\\\u2014 Ar-Riya (showing off)\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Neglecting prayers\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Backbiting\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The thing I fear most for you is minor shirk — Ar-Riya (showing off).\" (Musnad Ahmad). This shows how dangerous even minor shirk is.', 'This is a Hadith from Musnad Ahmad about a subtle form of shirk.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"shirk\\\",\\\"minor\\\",\\\"riya\\\",\\\"hadith\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(884, 'f5dfedc8-93c3-4bc2-9ceb-3e5dc2e37e80', 134, 3, 'Which Surah and verse says Allah does not forgive Shirk but may forgive lesser sins for whom He wills?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Surah Al-Baqarah 2:255\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Surah An-Nisa 4:48\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Surah Al-Ikhlas 112:1\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Surah Al-An\'am 6:88\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Surah An-Nisa 4:48 states: \"Indeed, Allah does not forgive association with Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills.\" This is a key verse on Shirk.', 'An-Nisa means \"The Women\" — the fourth chapter of the Quran.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"shirk\\\",\\\"forgiveness\\\",\\\"quran\\\",\\\"nisa\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(885, 'a13c5f23-59fc-4967-b0d6-9a6ea692f7ab', 134, 3, 'What is the correct Islamic way to say a conditional statement involving Allah\'s will and another person\'s will?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"What Allah and you will\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"What you will and Allah wills\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"What Allah wills, then what you will\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Both Allah and you will the same thing\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The correct form is \"What Allah wills, THEN what you will\" — using \"then\" (thumma) instead of \"and\" (wa) to show the sequence that Allah\'s will comes first and is supreme.', 'The key word is \"then\" (thumma) vs \"and\" (wa) — which shows proper ranking?', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"shirk\\\",\\\"minor\\\",\\\"language\\\",\\\"will\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(886, '2b88fc23-e360-432b-967f-e1a5e52b6d88', 134, 3, 'What is the difference in repentance required for Major Shirk vs Minor Shirk?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Both require renewal of Islam\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Neither requires any repentance\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Major Shirk requires renewing Islam; Minor Shirk requires repentance only\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Minor Shirk requires renewal of Islam; Major Shirk requires repentance only\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'For Major Shirk, one must sincerely repent, regret, stop the act, and RENEW their Islam (as it took them out of Islam). For Minor Shirk, repentance and stopping the act is sufficient — no need to renew Islam.', 'Major Shirk exits one from Islam — what is needed to re-enter?', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"shirk\\\",\\\"major\\\",\\\"minor\\\",\\\"repentance\\\",\\\"distinction\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(887, '87bcaa9e-a41f-42e4-95c0-3fb88106cdc0', 134, 3, 'Which type of shirk involves believing that someone other than Allah knows the unseen (Ghayb)?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Shirk in Worship\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Shirk in Lordship\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Minor Shirk\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Shirk in Names & Attributes\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'Shirk in Names and Attributes includes believing someone has Allah\'s unique attributes, such as knowing the Unseen (Ghayb) — which belongs exclusively to Allah.', 'Knowledge of the unseen is one of Allah\'s unique attributes (Sifat).', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"shirk\\\",\\\"names\\\",\\\"attributes\\\",\\\"unseen\\\",\\\"ghayb\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(888, '51347f92-9a2b-4922-8180-0309319b32f0', 134, 3, 'What does Risalah mean?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Belief in the Hereafter\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The system of sending messengers and prophets from Allah\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The five pillars of Islam\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Prayer and fasting\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Risalah means the system of sending messengers and prophets from Allah to guide humanity to the worship of Allah alone (Tawhid) and to the straight path.', 'Risalah comes from the word \"Rasul\" meaning messenger.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"risalah\\\",\\\"definition\\\",\\\"prophethood\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(889, 'e6fe24b4-d1ab-40bd-b272-f8fa0c369911', 134, 3, 'What is the approximate number of Rasuls (Messengers) sent by Allah?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"25\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"124,000\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"313\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"1000\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Approximately 313 Rasuls (Messengers) were sent by Allah. The total number of Prophets (Anbiya) is approximately 124,000.', 'Messengers are fewer than Prophets — about 313 vs 124,000.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"risalah\\\",\\\"rasul\\\",\\\"number\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(890, '188950bf-c15b-4b42-9a56-6ea2d7da28ca', 134, 3, 'Which of the following is the correct relationship between Nabi and Rasul?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Every Nabi is a Rasul\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Every Rasul is a Nabi, but not every Nabi is a Rasul\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Nabi and Rasul are the same\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Every Nabi is higher in rank than a Rasul\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Every Rasul is a Nabi (since he receives revelation), but not every Nabi is a Rasul. A Rasul brings a new scripture/law, while a Nabi follows a previous Shariah. Rasul is a higher rank.', 'Think of it as: all squares are rectangles, but not all rectangles are squares.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"risalah\\\",\\\"nabi\\\",\\\"rasul\\\",\\\"difference\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(891, '20bbf74d-22d2-4575-beaa-bd49654d5c6b', 134, 3, 'Which Prophet is an example of a Nabi (not a Rasul) who followed another Prophet\'s law?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Musa (Moses) AS\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Ibrahim (Abraham) AS\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Harun (Aaron) AS\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Isa (Jesus) AS\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Harun (Aaron) AS is an example of a Nabi who followed Musa\'s (Moses\'s) law rather than bringing a new scripture. Musa himself was a Rasul who brought the Torah.', 'He was the brother of Musa and supported him in his mission.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"risalah\\\",\\\"nabi\\\",\\\"harun\\\",\\\"example\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(892, '1903ca7f-dd6d-43bb-912a-ddc350664e97', 134, 3, 'What is the main purpose for which Allah sent Prophets and Messengers to humanity?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"To teach science and technology\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"To call people to worship Allah alone (Tawhid)\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"To establish political empires\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"To compile the Quran\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'All Prophets and Messengers were sent to call humanity to the worship of Allah alone (Tawhid) and to guide them to the straight path. The Quran states: \"We certainly sent into every nation a messenger...\" (16:36)', 'The core message of all prophets was the same.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"risalah\\\",\\\"purpose\\\",\\\"prophets\\\",\\\"tawhid\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(893, '0a4946b2-4321-4632-8abd-b3c06f384ed6', 134, 3, 'What is the key difference between a Rasul and a Nabi regarding scripture?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"A Nabi brings a new book; a Rasul does not\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"A Rasul brings a new book or law; a Nabi follows a previous Shariah\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Both bring new scriptures\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Neither brings new scriptures\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'A Rasul receives a new scripture or law (Shariah) and is sent to a people who have gone astray. A Nabi receives divine revelation (Wahi) but follows the previous Shariah rather than bringing a new one.', 'Which one is sent to disbelieving nations with a new message?', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"risalah\\\",\\\"nabi\\\",\\\"rasul\\\",\\\"scripture\\\",\\\"shariah\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12');
INSERT INTO `mcqs` (`id`, `uuid`, `topic_id`, `subject_id`, `question`, `question_type`, `options`, `correct_answers`, `explanation`, `hint`, `difficulty_level`, `time_limit_seconds`, `marks`, `negative_marks`, `tags`, `reference_book`, `reference_page`, `is_premium`, `is_verified`, `status`, `created_by`, `approved_by`, `approved_at`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(894, '1d9ba020-7297-4c60-99a6-3ad3acd60380', 134, 3, 'Surah Fatir 35:24 states that every nation has received what?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"A holy book\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"A warner (prophet)\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"A miracle\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"A caliph\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Surah Fatir 35:24 states: \"And there is no nation but that a warner (prophet) has passed among them.\" This shows that Allah\'s guidance reached every people through a prophet.', 'This verse emphasizes the universality of Allah\'s guidance.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"risalah\\\",\\\"quran\\\",\\\"fatir\\\",\\\"warner\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(895, 'da0d6f3d-7bdc-49b2-9c12-f94129133d96', 134, 3, 'What is the approximate total number of Prophets (Anbiya) sent by Allah?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"25\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"313\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"1000\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"124,000\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'The approximate total number of Prophets (Anbiya) sent by Allah is 124,000. Out of these, approximately 313 were Messengers (Rusul) who brought new scriptures or laws.', 'The number is very large — tens of thousands.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"risalah\\\",\\\"anbiya\\\",\\\"number\\\",\\\"prophets\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(896, 'ba1db2ef-773f-4e1d-ac89-63f6543f6644', 134, 3, 'Which Quranic verse from Surah Al-Hajj mentions both Nabi and Rasul together?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Surah Al-Hajj 22:52\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Surah An-Nahl 16:36\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Surah Al-Baqarah 2:285\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Surah Al-Ahzab 33:40\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"1\\\"]\"', 'Surah Al-Hajj 22:52 states: \"And We did not send before you any messenger (Rasul) or prophet (Nabi) except that when he spoke...\" — the only verse in the Quran that mentions both terms together.', 'Surah Al-Hajj is associated with the pilgrimage chapter.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"risalah\\\",\\\"quran\\\",\\\"hajj\\\",\\\"nabi\\\",\\\"rasul\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(897, 'deb4e560-5f87-40c9-8010-f168bf6a5c69', 134, 3, 'According to Islamic belief, what is the ruling on a person who denies even one prophet sent by Allah?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"They commit a major sin but remain Muslim\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"They are considered in error but not a disbeliever\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Their denial is considered disbelief (Kufr)\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"They should fast for 60 days in expiation\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'A Muslim must believe in ALL prophets and messengers of Allah. Denying even one prophet constitutes disbelief (Kufr), as the belief in all prophets is a required pillar of faith.', 'Belief in all Prophets is a pillar of Iman — denial of any breaks the pillar.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"risalah\\\",\\\"denial\\\",\\\"kufr\\\",\\\"belief\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(898, 'ebd93b80-5142-417c-9923-e4cb7d73e4f3', 134, 3, 'What does \"Akhirah\" mean?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"The present world\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The life after death\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The time of Judgment only\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"The intermediate world\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Akhirah means the life after death. It includes everything that happens from when a person dies until they enter Paradise or Hell forever — including the grave, resurrection, judgment, and final destination.', 'Akhirah literally means \"the last\" — referring to what comes after this world.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"akhirah\\\",\\\"definition\\\",\\\"hereafter\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(899, '0fe57e01-5d46-4e0a-a2b2-1f99f5587694', 134, 3, 'Belief in Akhirah (Hereafter) is which pillar of Iman?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"First\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Third\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Sixth\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Fifth\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'Belief in Akhirah (the Hereafter) is the fifth pillar of Iman. The six pillars are: Allah, Angels, Books, Messengers, Hereafter, and Divine Decree (Qadr).', 'Count the pillars: Allah, Angels, Books, Messengers, then...?', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"akhirah\\\",\\\"iman\\\",\\\"pillar\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(900, 'dae9443c-257a-4b87-8d17-56abe79bef59', 134, 3, 'Which two angels question the deceased in the grave?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Jibril and Mikail\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Munkar and Nakir\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Israfil and Ridhwan\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Malik and Ridhwan\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The two angels Munkar and Nakir come to the deceased in the grave and ask: Who is your Lord? What is your religion? Who is this man (Muhammad ﷺ)?', 'Their names suggest they bring something unfamiliar and strange.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"akhirah\\\",\\\"grave\\\",\\\"munkar\\\",\\\"nakir\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(901, 'd3f0c244-65fd-4273-b69c-ff42c5c5ba31', 134, 3, 'Which angel will blow the Trumpet (Sur) on the Day of Judgment?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Jibril (AS)\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Mikail (AS)\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Israfil (AS)\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Malik (AS)\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Israfil (AS) will blow the Trumpet (Sur). The first blast will kill all living beings, and the second blast will resurrect them for the Day of Judgment.', 'This angel\'s role is specifically related to the Trumpet (Sur).', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"akhirah\\\",\\\"trumpet\\\",\\\"sur\\\",\\\"israfil\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(902, '1796e84f-0817-4e87-9e1d-1e6d5c1b246f', 134, 3, 'What is the highest level of Paradise called?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Hawiyah\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Firdaws\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Sirat\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Barzakh\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Firdaws is the highest level of Paradise. There are 100 levels of Paradise in total, and the Prophet ﷺ asked believers to ask Allah specifically for Firdaws.', 'The Prophet ﷺ specifically told us to ask for this highest level.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"akhirah\\\",\\\"jannah\\\",\\\"firdaws\\\",\\\"paradise\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(903, 'b6f97e86-f8e8-4b11-a2d8-5a9cd274c8fe', 134, 3, 'What is the lowest level of Hell called?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Firdaws\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Sirat\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Hawiyah\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Barzakh\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Hawiyah is the lowest and worst level of Hell. There are 7 levels of Hell in total. Disbelievers, hypocrites, and those who died without Tawhid remain there forever.', 'It is the opposite extreme from Firdaws (highest Paradise).', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"akhirah\\\",\\\"jahannam\\\",\\\"hawiyah\\\",\\\"hell\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(904, 'a4167eb8-7eab-4968-8f59-9770a991fe20', 134, 3, 'What is Barzakh?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"The Day of Judgment\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The intermediate barrier between death and resurrection\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The bridge over Hell\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"The questioning in the grave\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Barzakh is the intermediate period (barrier) between death and resurrection. The soul lives in this state from the moment of death until the Day of Judgment when resurrection occurs.', 'Barzakh literally means \"barrier\" in Arabic — between two things.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"akhirah\\\",\\\"barzakh\\\",\\\"intermediate\\\",\\\"death\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(905, 'f0eb17e6-d378-4ac4-bb2f-cc8a99e433b1', 134, 3, 'What happens during the FIRST blast of Israfil\'s Trumpet (Sur)?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"All humans are resurrected\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"All living beings die (except whom Allah wills)\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The books of deeds are distributed\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"The bridge Sirat appears\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The first blast of Israfil\'s Trumpet causes all living beings in the heavens and earth to die, except those whom Allah wills to spare. The second blast then resurrects all humans.', 'Two blasts — one destroys, one restores.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"akhirah\\\",\\\"trumpet\\\",\\\"sur\\\",\\\"first-blast\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(906, '77649c65-8ffe-40ed-a2ee-e5a07ebe2e35', 134, 3, 'On the Day of Gathering (Hashr), receiving one\'s Book of Deeds in the right hand indicates what?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Temporary punishment then Paradise\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Entry into Hell\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Success and entry into Paradise\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Requiring intercession first\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Receiving the Book of Deeds in the RIGHT hand indicates success — the person will go to Paradise. Receiving it in the left hand or behind one\'s back indicates failure and going to Hell.', 'In Islamic culture, right = good/blessed, left = the opposite.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"akhirah\\\",\\\"hisab\\\",\\\"book\\\",\\\"right-hand\\\",\\\"paradise\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(907, 'a45d2499-cb7e-4126-b396-2c12ac891100', 134, 3, 'According to Islamic belief, how long will the Day of Judgment last for disbelievers?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"1,000 years\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"10,000 years\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"100,000 years\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"50,000 years\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'The Day of Judgment (the period of Gathering — Hashr) will last 50,000 years for disbelievers. For believers, due to Allah\'s mercy, it will feel much shorter.', 'The number contains \"50\" — 50,000 years.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"akhirah\\\",\\\"day-of-judgment\\\",\\\"duration\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(908, 'dc2363aa-ccb1-4b5b-b529-b813a15417bf', 134, 3, 'What is the Sirat in Islamic eschatology?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"A river in Paradise\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The scale weighing good and bad deeds\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"A bridge stretched over Hell that leads to Paradise\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"The questioning in the grave\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Sirat is a bridge stretched over Hell, described as sharper than a sword and thinner than a hair. Believers will cross it to reach Paradise at speeds ranging from lightning to walking. Sinners will fall into Hell.', 'It connects one place (Gathering) to another (Paradise) — crossing over something dangerous.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"akhirah\\\",\\\"sirat\\\",\\\"bridge\\\",\\\"hell\\\",\\\"paradise\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(909, '3dc9e7bc-ac44-4d34-b567-13faea9048a5', 134, 3, 'What is the greatest blessing for believers in Paradise according to Islamic belief?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Rivers of milk and honey\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Palaces of pearls\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Seeing Allah (the Beatific Vision)\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Never-ending food and drink\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The greatest blessing in Paradise is seeing Allah on Fridays (the Beatific Vision). All other pleasures of Paradise, though immense, are lesser than this supreme blessing.', 'The greatest thing is not physical — it is spiritual and divine.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"akhirah\\\",\\\"jannah\\\",\\\"seeing-allah\\\",\\\"blessing\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(910, '0d353060-a718-4309-860e-1b5715ad65c2', 134, 3, 'Which angel presides over and guards Hell (Jahannam)?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Jibril (AS)\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Israfil (AS)\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Ridhwan (AS)\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Malik (AS)\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'Angel Malik presides over Hell. He oversees the punishment in Jahannam and is accompanied by 19 stern angels. Angel Ridhwan is the guardian of Paradise.', 'Think: Malik guards Jahannam; Ridhwan guards Jannah.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"akhirah\\\",\\\"jahannam\\\",\\\"malik\\\",\\\"angel\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(911, 'a6f3ab05-f404-475f-bcf2-e50a2f22a83c', 134, 3, 'How many levels does Hell (Jahannam) have according to Islamic belief?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"5\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"7\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"10\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"100\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Hell (Jahannam) has 7 levels. The Quran mentions: \"It has seven gates; for every gate is a portion of them assigned.\" (Surah Al-Hijr 15:44). The lowest level is Hawiyah.', 'The Quran in Surah Al-Hijr specifically mentions the number of gates.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"akhirah\\\",\\\"jahannam\\\",\\\"levels\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(912, '734f1553-b8ed-45a3-8f83-9ef5ec449554', 134, 3, 'What are the three questions asked by Munkar and Nakir in the grave?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Who is your father? What is your book? Where is your mosque?\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Who is your Lord? What is your religion? Who is this man (Muhammad \\\\ufdfa)?\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"How many prayers did you pray? Did you fast? Did you perform Hajj?\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"What is your name? Where did you live? How did you die?\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Munkar and Nakir ask three questions: (1) Who is your Lord? (2) What is your religion? (3) Who is this man — referring to Prophet Muhammad ﷺ. Correct answers bring peace; wrong answers bring punishment.', 'The three questions relate to Allah, Islam, and the Prophet ﷺ.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"akhirah\\\",\\\"grave\\\",\\\"munkar\\\",\\\"nakir\\\",\\\"questions\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(913, '9d2d830d-c718-4228-85f0-7590e84ed519', 134, 3, 'What is the Shafa\'ah (Intercession) of Prophet Muhammad ﷺ called on the Day of Judgment?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Shafa\'ah al-Kubra\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Shafa\'ah al-Sughra\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Shafa\'ah al-Wusta\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Shafa\'ah al-Akhira\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"1\\\"]\"', 'The Prophet Muhammad\'s ﷺ intercession is called the \"Shafa\'ah al-Kubra\" (the Greatest Intercession). He will intercede for people to begin the Judgment and for sinful believers to enter Paradise or be removed from Hell.', 'Kubra means \"great/greatest\" in Arabic.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"akhirah\\\",\\\"shafaah\\\",\\\"intercession\\\",\\\"prophet\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(914, '3a910484-2cec-4dc9-98f4-a0d3a38a75b7', 134, 3, 'According to Islamic eschatology, what will happen to Muslims who committed major sins and entered Hell?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"They remain in Hell forever like disbelievers\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"They will be punished temporarily then taken out to Paradise\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"They go directly to Paradise due to their faith\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"They enter Barzakh permanently\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Muslims who committed major sins but had Tawhid will enter Hell temporarily (unless forgiven by Allah). Through Allah\'s mercy and possibly intercession, they will eventually be taken out of Hell and enter Paradise. Only disbelievers remain forever.', 'Tawhid is the key — it prevents eternal punishment even for sinful Muslims.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"akhirah\\\",\\\"muslims\\\",\\\"hell\\\",\\\"temporary\\\",\\\"paradise\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(915, '19337c19-5091-4219-89be-56651f1cbcea', 134, 3, 'According to a Hadith, about what five things will every human being be asked on the Day of Judgment?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Prayer, Zakat, Fasting, Hajj, and Jihad\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Life (how spent), Youth (how used), Wealth (how earned and spent), and Knowledge (how acted upon)\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Parents, Children, Neighbors, Spouse, and Friends\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Faith, Deeds, Intention, Effort, and Repentance\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'According to the Hadith of Mu\'adh, every person will be asked about five things: (1) Life — how was it spent, (2) Youth — how was it used, (3) Wealth — how was it earned, (4) Wealth — how was it spent, (5) Knowledge — how was it acted upon.', 'The five areas relate to time, age, money, and knowledge — all key responsibilities.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"akhirah\\\",\\\"hisab\\\",\\\"five\\\",\\\"questions\\\",\\\"hadith\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(916, '3bcd498a-9535-4b09-a05d-79911a0c221b', 134, 3, 'In what condition will humans be raised from their graves on the Day of Resurrection?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"In their best clothes and fully healthy\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"In burial shrouds\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"As spirits without bodies\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'According to Hadith, humans will be raised from their graves barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised (in the original state of creation). When Aisha (RA) expressed concern about this, the Prophet ﷺ said the events of that Day would make people too preoccupied to look at each other.', 'The state reflects being returned to one\'s original creation state.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"akhirah\\\",\\\"resurrection\\\",\\\"condition\\\",\\\"hadith\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(917, '7a023836-3d73-4986-b874-8770025c43bb', 134, 3, 'What connects all four Islamic concepts: Tawhid, Shirk, Risalah, and Akhirah?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"They are all pillars of Islam (Arkaan al-Islam)\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"They all relate to belief (Iman) and accountability before Allah\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"They are all mentioned only in Surah Al-Baqarah\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"They all require physical acts of worship\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'All four concepts relate to belief (Iman) and accountability: Tawhid establishes Who to worship, Shirk defines what destroys that worship, Risalah explains how guidance came, and Akhirah shows the ultimate accountability and consequences.', 'Think about why all prophets taught these four — what is the common thread?', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"tawhid\\\",\\\"shirk\\\",\\\"risalah\\\",\\\"akhirah\\\",\\\"comprehensive\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(918, '546ebdc3-885c-4b85-810c-830ae1809768', 134, 3, 'Which Quranic verse from Surah Ad-Duha 93:4 describes the Hereafter?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"The Hereafter is equal to this world\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The Hereafter is worse than this world\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The Hereafter is better than the first (present) life\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"The Hereafter is only for prophets\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Surah Ad-Duha 93:4 states: \"And the Hereafter is better for you than the first life.\" This verse encourages prioritizing the Akhirah over the temporary pleasures of the Dunya.', 'Surah Ad-Duha is a short comforting chapter — what does it say about what comes next?', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"akhirah\\\",\\\"quran\\\",\\\"duha\\\",\\\"hereafter\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(919, '069cfad0-8aec-49fb-9c4d-da0bbbdbb1f1', 134, 3, 'In Paradise, how many levels exist and what is the recommended level to ask for?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"7 levels; ask for the second highest\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"10 levels; ask for Jannah al-Naeem\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"100 levels; ask for Firdaws (the highest)\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"3 levels; ask for the middle one\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Paradise has 100 levels. The Prophet ﷺ instructed believers to ask Allah for Firdaws — the highest level of Paradise — because when you ask Allah, ask for the highest.', 'Hell has 7 levels; Paradise has how many?', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"akhirah\\\",\\\"jannah\\\",\\\"firdaws\\\",\\\"levels\\\",\\\"paradise\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(920, 'd8191cbe-9dde-49a5-8405-ef523166c96b', 134, 3, 'Which of the following correctly describes the order of stages in the Hereafter?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Grave \\\\u2192 Trumpet \\\\u2192 Resurrection \\\\u2192 Gathering \\\\u2192 Reckoning \\\\u2192 Scale \\\\u2192 Sirat \\\\u2192 Paradise\\\\\\/Hell\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Resurrection \\\\u2192 Grave \\\\u2192 Trumpet \\\\u2192 Gathering \\\\u2192 Reckoning \\\\u2192 Paradise\\\\\\/Hell\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Gathering \\\\u2192 Trumpet \\\\u2192 Resurrection \\\\u2192 Scale \\\\u2192 Reckoning \\\\u2192 Paradise\\\\\\/Hell\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Trumpet \\\\u2192 Grave \\\\u2192 Gathering \\\\u2192 Reckoning \\\\u2192 Sirat \\\\u2192 Paradise\\\\\\/Hell\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"1\\\"]\"', 'The correct order is: Grave (Qabr/Barzakh) → Trumpet (Sur) → Resurrection (Ba\'ath) → Gathering (Hashr) → Reckoning (Hisab) → Scale (Mizan) → Bridge (Sirat) → Intercession (Shafa\'ah) → Paradise (Jannah) or Hell (Jahannam).', 'It starts with death/grave and ends with the final destination — trace the journey chronologically.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"akhirah\\\",\\\"stages\\\",\\\"order\\\",\\\"comprehensive\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(921, '4bfb3849-8e0a-42ed-ac45-5f29c0456e13', 134, 3, 'Who has the authority to grant permission for intercession (Shafa\'ah) on the Day of Judgment?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Prophet Muhammad \\\\ufdfa alone\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"All prophets collectively\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Only Allah\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Angels and prophets together\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Only Allah can grant permission for intercession (Shafa\'ah). No one — not even Prophet Muhammad ﷺ — can intercede without Allah\'s explicit permission and approval.', 'All power and authority on that Day belongs to whom?', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"akhirah\\\",\\\"shafaah\\\",\\\"permission\\\",\\\"allah\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies Notes', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:25:12', '2026-04-27 21:25:12'),
(922, '39d6d88b-90f2-4c5f-bd45-ce7f5f8c1e4e', 127, 3, 'What is the linguistic meaning of the word \"Shahadah\"?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"To worship\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"To bear witness \\\\\\/ to testify\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"To submit\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"To fast\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Shahadah comes from the Arabic verb \"shahida,\" meaning \"to bear witness\" or \"to testify.\" It is the declaration of faith in Islam.', 'Think of the word \"shahid\" (witness) — they share the same root.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"shahadah\\\",\\\"definition\\\",\\\"pillar-1\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(923, 'a074a595-19db-4ccf-a525-375817773770', 127, 3, 'How many parts does the Shahadah consist of?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"1\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"4\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"2\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'The Shahadah has two parts: (1) \"La ilaha illa Allah\" — Oneness of Allah (Tawhid), and (2) \"Muhammadun Rasul Allah\" — the Prophethood of Muhammad ﷺ (Risalah).', 'One part about Allah, one part about the Prophet ﷺ.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"shahadah\\\",\\\"parts\\\",\\\"pillar-1\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(924, '998bf0e7-4e67-4a33-8cbb-603403cd5c57', 127, 3, 'What is the Shahadah also known as in Arabic?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Kalimah Shahadah only\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Kalimah Tayyibah\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Kalimah Istighfar\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Kalimah Tamjeed\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The Shahadah is also called \"Kalimah Tayyibah,\" meaning the \"pure/good word.\" It is the key to Paradise and the gateway to all acts of worship.', 'Tayyibah means pure or good in Arabic.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"shahadah\\\",\\\"kalimah-tayyibah\\\",\\\"pillar-1\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(925, '2348d2e6-0d98-440c-9468-95eba2753e07', 127, 3, 'What does the first part of the Shahadah — \"La ilaha illa Allah\" — mean?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"There is no true god worthy of worship except Allah\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Allah is the greatest\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Praise be to Allah\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', '\"La ilaha illa Allah\" means \"There is no true god worthy of worship except Allah.\" It consists of negation (La ilaha — rejection of all false deities) and affirmation (illa Allah — only Allah deserves worship).', '\"La\" = No/Negation, \"illaha\" = deity, \"illa Allah\" = except Allah.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"shahadah\\\",\\\"first-part\\\",\\\"tawhid\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(926, '2371f040-cbb0-49ed-a115-dc30d69ed202', 127, 3, 'Which pillar of Islam is the Shahadah?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Second\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Third\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"First\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Fifth\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Shahadah is the FIRST pillar of Islam. All other pillars (Salah, Zakah, Sawm, Hajj) are built upon this foundation. Without the Shahadah, all other deeds are invalid.', 'It is the key to Islam — it must come first.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"shahadah\\\",\\\"pillar\\\",\\\"first\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(927, '1be3e860-8255-4e61-8c13-a11d6aec1a2f', 127, 3, 'According to a Hadith in Abu Dawood, what will happen to a person whose last words are \"La ilaha illa Allah\"?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"They will be punished in Hell forever\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Their deeds will be doubled\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"They will enter Paradise\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"They will be questioned more strictly\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever\'s last words are \'La ilaha illa Allah\' will enter Paradise.\" (Abu Dawood). This shows the immense virtue of the Shahadah.', 'The Prophet ﷺ linked the last words of a person to their destination.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"shahadah\\\",\\\"last-words\\\",\\\"paradise\\\",\\\"hadith\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(928, 'd1dbe03a-f893-4e96-b84e-6aa355441f26', 127, 3, 'How many conditions must be met for the Shahadah to be accepted?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"5\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"6\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"7\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"8\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'There are 8 conditions for Shahadah to be accepted: Knowledge, Certainty, Sincerity, Truthfulness, Love, Submission, Acceptance, and Rejection of False Deities.', 'Count: Knowledge, Certainty, Sincerity, Truthfulness, Love, Submission, Acceptance, Rejection.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"shahadah\\\",\\\"conditions\\\",\\\"acceptance\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(929, '8992aecc-f336-4e64-85ae-234537870ba6', 127, 3, 'Which condition of Shahadah ensures that the heart and tongue are aligned without any hypocrisy?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Knowledge\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Certainty\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Truthfulness\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Sincerity\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Truthfulness means the heart and tongue are aligned — a person genuinely believes what they say. The opposite (saying it without believing) is hypocrisy (Nifaq), which nullifies the Shahadah.', 'This condition is violated by hypocrites (Munafiqeen) who say it with their tongues but not hearts.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"shahadah\\\",\\\"truthfulness\\\",\\\"conditions\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(930, 'b3552f1c-b742-4492-87b2-ecbb10284279', 127, 3, 'What does the \"negation\" (La ilaha) part of the Shahadah reject?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Only idol worship\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Only grave worship\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"All false deities including idols, graves, wealth, desires, and power\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Only polytheism in ancient times\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\"La ilaha\" rejects ALL false deities — anything worshiped besides Allah, including idols, graves, saints, wealth, desires, and power. It is a comprehensive rejection of every false object of worship.', 'The rejection is not limited to physical idols — it includes anything given the status of deity.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"shahadah\\\",\\\"negation\\\",\\\"la-ilaha\\\",\\\"false-deities\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(931, 'adce5c1b-53c1-44d9-92ab-9443e9a09817', 127, 3, 'What does the second part of the Shahadah regarding Muhammad ﷺ require a Muslim to believe about prophethood?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"More prophets may come after him\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"He is the last prophet and no new prophet will come after him\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"He is one of many equal prophets\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"He is only a messenger, not a prophet\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The second part of the Shahadah requires belief that Muhammad ﷺ is the Seal of the Prophets (Khatam-ul-Nabiyyeen) — the last prophet. No new prophet will come after him.', 'Khatam means \"seal/last\" — this is a core belief in Islam.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"shahadah\\\",\\\"khatam-ul-nabiyyeen\\\",\\\"last-prophet\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(932, '334fca2f-7999-47ae-94dd-dbccb5e9aff2', 127, 3, 'Which Quranic verse (59:7) is referenced to show that following the Prophet ﷺ is obligatory?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"\\\\\\\"So establish prayer and give Zakah\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"\\\\\\\"And whatever the Messenger gives you, take it; and what he forbids you from, refrain\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"\\\\\\\"Indeed Allah loves those who are patient\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"\\\\\\\"O you who believe, fast as it was prescribed\\\\\\\"\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Quran 59:7 states that Muslims must take what the Prophet ﷺ gives and refrain from what he forbids. This establishes obedience to the Prophet ﷺ as part of the Shahadah.', 'Surah Al-Hashr 59:7 — about following the Prophet\'s commands.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"shahadah\\\",\\\"obedience\\\",\\\"prophet\\\",\\\"quran-59-7\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(933, '1274012f-7bee-4b79-9fcf-3434b85d17a1', 127, 3, 'A person recites the Shahadah verbally but worships graves. What is the Islamic ruling on their Shahadah?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Valid, as verbal recitation is sufficient\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Valid, but they need to repent\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Invalid, as worshiping graves violates the 8th condition (rejection of false deities)\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Valid with minor sin\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Worshiping graves violates the 8th condition of Shahadah — \"Rejection of False Deities.\" Grave worship is Major Shirk, which nullifies the Shahadah. Verbal recitation without fulfilling conditions is insufficient.', 'Recall: worshiping other than Allah contradicts the first part \"La ilaha\" (no false deity).', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"shahadah\\\",\\\"conditions\\\",\\\"grave-worship\\\",\\\"invalidation\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(934, 'd33d2efb-54d6-46f3-8e59-3f7dc8eabcff', 127, 3, 'Which condition of Shahadah is violated when someone prays longer only to impress others (Riya)?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Knowledge\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Truthfulness\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Sincerity (Ikhlas)\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Acceptance\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Riya (showing off) violates the condition of Sincerity (Ikhlas). Sincerity means worship is done purely for Allah\'s sake, free from seeking praise from people or hidden shirk. Riya is Minor Shirk that undermines sincerity.', 'Ikhlas = purity of intention — Riya directly opposes this.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"shahadah\\\",\\\"riya\\\",\\\"sincerity\\\",\\\"ikhlas\\\",\\\"conditions\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(935, 'b8f10e7b-0155-4cf5-9f1b-f59d712eb18d', 127, 3, 'Which pillar of Islam is Salah (Prayer)?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"First\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Second\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Third\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Fourth\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Salah is the SECOND pillar of Islam, after the Shahadah. The Prophet ﷺ called it the covenant between Muslims and disbelievers — abandoning it is extremely serious.', 'After declaring faith (Shahadah), the next obligation is...?', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"salah\\\",\\\"pillar\\\",\\\"second\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(936, '583411ed-2e7f-4326-9a88-b0948b9f4fec', 127, 3, 'How many rak\'ahs does the Fajr prayer have?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"4\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"2\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"1\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Fajr (dawn prayer) has 2 rak\'ahs. It is prayed from true dawn until sunrise. Among the five daily prayers, Fajr has the fewest rak\'ahs.', 'Fajr is the shortest obligatory prayer.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"salah\\\",\\\"fajr\\\",\\\"rakah\\\",\\\"prayers\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(937, '5f4ea54a-3a95-474c-b8ca-26e2f37f0b17', 127, 3, 'How many rak\'ahs does the Maghrib prayer have?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"2\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"4\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"5\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Maghrib prayer has 3 rak\'ahs. It is prayed immediately after sunset until twilight disappears. Maghrib is the only obligatory prayer with an odd number of rak\'ahs (3).', 'Maghrib is unique among the five prayers in having an odd number of rak\'ahs.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"salah\\\",\\\"maghrib\\\",\\\"rakah\\\",\\\"prayers\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(938, '5e87bbe5-d70c-4fb4-a12f-175665fc43c3', 127, 3, 'Which direction must Muslims face when performing Salah?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"East\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Towards Jerusalem\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Qiblah (towards the Kaaba)\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"North\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Muslims must face the Qiblah (direction of the Kaaba in Mecca) when performing Salah. Facing the Qiblah is one of the essential conditions of Salah.', 'Qiblah is the direction of the House of Allah (Kaaba) in Mecca.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"salah\\\",\\\"qiblah\\\",\\\"kaaba\\\",\\\"condition\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(939, '582f67be-d06b-4a76-8850-c129bd899607', 127, 3, 'Which Surah must be recited in every rak\'ah of Salah?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Surah Al-Ikhlas\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Surah Al-Baqarah\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Surah Al-Fatihah\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Surah Al-Falaq\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Reciting Surah Al-Fatihah in every rak\'ah is a pillar (Rukn) of Salah. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"There is no prayer for the one who does not recite the Opening of the Book (Al-Fatihah).\" (Bukhari)', 'It is called the \"Opening Chapter\" — essential to every unit of prayer.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"salah\\\",\\\"fatihah\\\",\\\"pillar\\\",\\\"recitation\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(940, 'bd220ac1-f08f-4e70-8f2d-537f6b02a947', 127, 3, 'Which prayers have 4 rak\'ahs each among the five daily prayers?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Fajr, Dhuhr, Asr\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Dhuhr, Asr, Isha\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Asr, Maghrib, Isha\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Dhuhr, Maghrib, Isha\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Dhuhr, Asr, and Isha each have 4 rak\'ahs. Fajr has 2 rak\'ahs and Maghrib has 3 rak\'ahs. So the pattern is: 2, 4, 4, 3, 4.', 'Pattern: Fajr=2, Dhuhr=4, Asr=4, Maghrib=3, Isha=4.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"salah\\\",\\\"rakah\\\",\\\"dhuhr\\\",\\\"asr\\\",\\\"isha\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(941, '439fd787-a6d8-4d3b-91be-3d38287795bb', 127, 3, 'What is the ruling on Witr prayer according to the Hanafi school?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Fardh (Obligatory)\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Nafl (Voluntary)\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Wajib (Necessary)\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Sunnah Ghair Mu\'akkadah\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'According to the Hanafi school, Witr prayer is Wajib (Necessary) — slightly below Fardh but still essential. Leaving it without excuse is sinful. Other schools consider it Sunnah Mu\'akkadah.', 'Hanafi school has a unique ruling on Witr — it is between Fardh and Sunnah.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"salah\\\",\\\"witr\\\",\\\"hanafi\\\",\\\"wajib\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(942, '1c53a853-bf51-47e4-a1a7-1536be70774d', 127, 3, 'How many Sunnah Mu\'akkadah (emphasized Sunnah) rak\'ahs are there daily (Rawatib)?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"8\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"10\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"12\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"14\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'There are 12 daily Sunnah Mu\'akkadah rak\'ahs (Rawatib): 2 before Fajr, 4 before Dhuhr + 2 after Dhuhr, 2 after Maghrib, 2 after Isha. The Prophet ﷺ never abandoned these.', 'Count: 2 + (4+2) + 2 + 2 = 12 rak\'ahs.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"salah\\\",\\\"sunnah\\\",\\\"rawatib\\\",\\\"12-rakah\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(943, 'caf34d34-749d-46a9-987d-b1f7eaa6f789', 127, 3, 'Which Quranic verse (29:45) describes a key spiritual benefit of Salah?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Salah brings wealth\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Salah prevents indecency and evil (Fahisha and Munkar)\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Salah is only for men\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Salah was only obligatory for previous nations\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Quran 29:45 states that Salah prevents al-Fahisha (indecency) and al-Munkar (evil). This is a major spiritual benefit — regular Salah builds a barrier between the believer and sins.', 'This verse says Salah \"prohibits\" something — what does it prohibit?', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"salah\\\",\\\"quran\\\",\\\"fahisha\\\",\\\"munkar\\\",\\\"29-45\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(944, '91ed43a7-26e7-46f3-8200-ddd2305029fc', 127, 3, 'What is the covering requirement (Awrah) for men during Salah?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Whole body\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Navel to knees\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Whole body except face and hands\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Only the private parts\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'For men, the Awrah (area that must be covered) during Salah is from the navel to the knees. For women, the whole body must be covered except the face and hands.', 'Men: navel to knees. Women: whole body except face and hands.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"salah\\\",\\\"awrah\\\",\\\"men\\\",\\\"condition\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(945, '6780b51a-157c-4f7f-b78e-0484f8285af6', 127, 3, 'What is the best voluntary prayer after the obligatory (Fardh) prayers?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Duha prayer\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Ishraaq prayer\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Tahajjud (night prayer)\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Prayer after Wudu\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Tahajjud (the voluntary night prayer) is the best Nafl prayer after the obligatory prayers. It is prayed in the last third of the night and carries immense spiritual reward.', 'This prayer is performed at night — its timing makes it particularly virtuous.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"salah\\\",\\\"tahajjud\\\",\\\"nafl\\\",\\\"best-prayer\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(946, 'a74a19a5-fb89-4d5d-aa48-d010c509a441', 127, 3, 'Which of the following is a PILLAR (Rukn) of Salah — if missed, the prayer is completely invalid?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Reciting Qunut in Witr\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Saying Ameen after Al-Fatihah\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Prostrating (Sajdah) with forehead, nose, palms, knees, and toes\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Wearing clean clothes\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Prostration (Sajdah) with seven body parts (forehead, nose, palms, knees, toes) is a Pillar (Rukn) of Salah. If missed deliberately, the entire prayer is invalid. Options A, B, D are not pillars.', 'Pillars of Salah — if any one is skipped deliberately, the Salah must be repeated.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"salah\\\",\\\"pillar\\\",\\\"sajdah\\\",\\\"rukn\\\",\\\"invalid\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(947, 'dd9d08b5-d2a1-4b37-a573-67bf798bffe5', 127, 3, 'According to a Hadith in Tirmidhi, what is the ruling on a person who abandons Salah completely?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"They become a sinner only\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"They have become a disbeliever (Kafir)\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"They need to pay a fine\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Only their reward is reduced\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The covenant between us and the disbelievers is Salah; whoever abandons it has become a disbeliever.\" (Tirmidhi). Completely abandoning Salah is treated with utmost severity.', 'This Hadith in Tirmidhi uses the word \"kafir\" — disbeliever.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"salah\\\",\\\"abandoning\\\",\\\"kufr\\\",\\\"hadith\\\",\\\"tirmidhi\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(948, '684855a7-be83-4eef-8fb8-6c763b2bc41b', 127, 3, 'What is the linguistic meaning of Zakah?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Fasting and prayer\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Purification and growth\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Pilgrimage and charity\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Patience and gratitude\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Zakah linguistically means \"purification\" and \"growth.\" It purifies the giver\'s wealth from greed and the soul from miserliness, while also blessing and growing the remaining wealth.', 'Think: giving Zakah \"purifies\" wealth and causes it to \"grow\" spiritually.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"zakah\\\",\\\"definition\\\",\\\"purification\\\",\\\"growth\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(949, '1760397b-7e74-4622-84de-b447b9c5481c', 127, 3, 'What is the standard Zakah rate on gold, silver, savings, and trade goods?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"5%\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"10%\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"20%\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"2.5%\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'The standard Zakah rate on gold, silver, cash savings, and trade goods is 2.5% of the total wealth annually, provided Nisab is met and one full lunar year (Hawl) has passed.', 'It is a quarter of a tenth (1/40) of one\'s total wealth.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"zakah\\\",\\\"rate\\\",\\\"2.5\\\",\\\"gold\\\",\\\"silver\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(950, 'ce2287da-31dc-4c06-81cb-caec7be3bc7d', 127, 3, 'In which year of Hijra was Zakah made obligatory?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"1 AH\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"3 AH\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"9 AH\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"2 AH\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'Zakah was made obligatory in 2 AH (After Hijra), along with fasting in Ramadan. Both became obligatory in the same year, establishing two of the five pillars simultaneously.', 'Same year as fasting was made obligatory — 2 AH.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"zakah\\\",\\\"history\\\",\\\"2ah\\\",\\\"obligation\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(951, '35ee5cb3-6dea-459f-81bc-e1580c95b109', 127, 3, 'What is \"Nisab\" in the context of Zakah?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"The rate of Zakah payment\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The minimum threshold of wealth above which Zakah becomes obligatory\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The time period for paying Zakah\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"The name of a Zakah recipient\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Nisab is the minimum threshold of wealth. Zakah becomes obligatory when a person\'s wealth remains above the Nisab for one complete lunar year (Hawl). Below Nisab, no Zakah is due.', 'Nisa = threshold/minimum — below it, no Zakah is required.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"zakah\\\",\\\"nisab\\\",\\\"threshold\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(952, '0c2d2adb-33f4-443f-a47a-6968b9a5298c', 127, 3, 'How many categories of people are eligible to receive Zakah according to the Quran?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"5\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"6\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"8\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"10\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Quran 9:60 specifies exactly 8 categories of Zakah recipients: Fuqara\', Masakin, \'Amilina, Mu\'allafat al-Qulub, Riqab, Gharimin, Fi Sabilillah, and Ibn al-Sabil.', 'Surah At-Tawbah 9:60 lists all 8 categories explicitly.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"zakah\\\",\\\"recipients\\\",\\\"eight\\\",\\\"quran-9-60\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(953, '9c7b4973-7cb5-42da-902d-b514835f3428', 127, 3, 'What is the Zakah rate on agricultural produce that is rain-fed (without irrigation)?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"2.5%\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"5%\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"10%\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"20%\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Rain-fed (natural irrigation) agricultural produce has a Zakah rate of 10% at harvest. Artificially irrigated land has a rate of 5%. No Hawl (full year) is required — Zakah is due at every harvest.', 'Rain (natural) = 10%; Irrigated (artificial effort) = 5%. More effort = lower rate.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"zakah\\\",\\\"agriculture\\\",\\\"rain-fed\\\",\\\"10-percent\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(954, 'e9e4d3ef-2b5e-4236-9da4-870aac0b7dfc', 127, 3, 'What is the Zakah rate on minerals and buried treasure (Rikaz)?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"2.5%\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"5%\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"10%\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"20%\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'Rikaz (buried treasure/minerals) has the highest Zakah rate of 20%. It is due immediately upon finding — no Nisab or Hawl (full lunar year) is required.', 'Rikaz is found without effort — hence the highest rate (20% or 1/5).', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"zakah\\\",\\\"rikaz\\\",\\\"minerals\\\",\\\"20-percent\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(955, '3e422d61-b8a2-4e8a-810b-c6138c9e8d95', 127, 3, 'Which category of Zakah recipients refers to people who are given Zakah to soften their hearts toward Islam?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Fuqara\'\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Gharimin\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Mu\'allafat al-Qulub\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Riqab\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Mu\'allafat al-Qulub means \"those whose hearts are to be reconciled.\" This category includes new Muslims who need support and influential non-Muslims whose goodwill toward Islam is sought.', 'Mu\'allaf shares the root with \"ألف\" meaning to bond/reconcile.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"zakah\\\",\\\"muallafat\\\",\\\"hearts\\\",\\\"recipients\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54');
INSERT INTO `mcqs` (`id`, `uuid`, `topic_id`, `subject_id`, `question`, `question_type`, `options`, `correct_answers`, `explanation`, `hint`, `difficulty_level`, `time_limit_seconds`, `marks`, `negative_marks`, `tags`, `reference_book`, `reference_page`, `is_premium`, `is_verified`, `status`, `created_by`, `approved_by`, `approved_at`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(956, 'e7ee4b20-e8cf-4bc7-a104-05f049131681', 127, 3, 'Why can\'t Zakah be given to the Prophet\'s family (Banu Hashim)?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"They are too wealthy\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Zakah is the \\\\\\\"dirt\\\\\\\" of people; they receive Khums instead\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"They live in Mecca and cannot receive it\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"There is no such ruling\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The Prophet ﷺ said Zakah is the \"dirt/impurity\" of wealth — it purifies the giver. Banu Hashim (the Prophet\'s family) are too honored to receive this, so they receive Khums (1/5 of war booty) instead.', 'The Prophet ﷺ described Zakah as something that \"purifies\" — hence his noble family is exempt.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"zakah\\\",\\\"banu-hashim\\\",\\\"khums\\\",\\\"prohibition\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(957, 'eac07a1a-a275-4398-8937-58c8db16d7f4', 127, 3, 'What is the difference between Fuqara\' and Masakin as Zakah recipients?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"They are the same category\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Fuqara\' have some wealth below Nisab; Masakin are more destitute with almost nothing\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Fuqara\' are non-Muslims; Masakin are Muslims\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Fuqara\' are travelers; Masakin are indebted\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Fuqara\' (the poor) have some wealth but below the Nisab threshold. Masakin (the needy) are even more destitute — having almost nothing. Both are among the 8 eligible Zakah recipients.', 'Masakin (from the root sakan = stillness/inability) are the most destitute.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"zakah\\\",\\\"fuqara\\\",\\\"masakin\\\",\\\"recipients\\\",\\\"distinction\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(958, 'b85d9b91-72b6-436e-8011-0b001581f590', 127, 3, 'Why do many scholars prefer using the Silver Nisab over Gold Nisab when calculating Zakah eligibility today?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Silver is more valuable than gold\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Gold Nisab leads to more people paying Zakah\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Silver Nisab is lower, making more people obligated to pay, increasing distribution to the poor\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Silver is the only Nisab mentioned in the Quran\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Silver Nisab (~$500-600) is much lower than Gold Nisab (~$5,500-6,000). Using Silver Nisab means more people meet the threshold and pay Zakah, which increases distribution to the poor. Many scholars prefer this for greater social benefit.', 'Lower threshold = more payers = more wealth redistributed to the poor.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"zakah\\\",\\\"silver-nisab\\\",\\\"gold-nisab\\\",\\\"scholars\\\",\\\"preference\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(959, '0616c089-423e-426d-a670-c0f30128fbb8', 127, 3, 'What is the difference between Zakah and Sadaqah regarding recipients?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Both can be given to anyone\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Zakah is restricted to 8 specific categories; Sadaqah can be given to anyone including non-Muslims\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Sadaqah is restricted to 8 categories; Zakah can go to anyone\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Neither can be given to non-Muslims\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Zakah has strict rules — it can ONLY go to the 8 categories listed in Quran 9:60. Sadaqah (voluntary charity) is flexible — it can be given to anyone, including non-Muslims, in any amount at any time.', 'Zakah = restricted (Fardh); Sadaqah = flexible (voluntary).', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"zakah\\\",\\\"sadaqah\\\",\\\"distinction\\\",\\\"recipients\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(960, 'fe920acb-92fb-48ad-affb-1e17163fa5e3', 127, 3, 'What does the word \"Sawm\" linguistically mean?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"To give charity\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"To pray\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"To refrain\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"To praise\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Sawm linguistically means \"to refrain.\" Islamically, it means to refrain from eating, drinking, marital relations, and all invalidating actions from true dawn (Fajr) until sunset (Maghrib) with a sincere intention.', 'Fasting is essentially \"refraining\" from specific things for a specific time.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"sawm\\\",\\\"fasting\\\",\\\"definition\\\",\\\"linguistic\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(961, '3d71b255-51d5-4917-a65f-ef12ab6659f7', 127, 3, 'Which pillar of Islam is fasting (Sawm)?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Second\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Third\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Fifth\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Fourth\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'Fasting (Sawm) is the FOURTH pillar of Islam. The five pillars in order are: Shahadah, Salah, Zakah, Sawm (Fasting), and Hajj.', 'After Shahadah, Salah, and Zakah — what comes fourth?', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"sawm\\\",\\\"fasting\\\",\\\"fourth\\\",\\\"pillar\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(962, '61289045-6b8b-4cf8-b4fa-ff8d43fab181', 127, 3, 'Which Quranic verse made fasting in Ramadan obligatory?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Surah Al-Baqarah 2:183\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Surah Al-Imran 3:97\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Surah Al-Ma\'idah 5:6\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Surah At-Tawbah 9:60\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"1\\\"]\"', 'Surah Al-Baqarah 2:183 states: \"O you who believe! Fasting is prescribed for you as it was prescribed for those before you, that you may become righteous.\" This verse made Ramadan fasting obligatory.', 'Al-Baqarah 2:183 — the verse about fasting and Taqwa (righteousness).', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"sawm\\\",\\\"quran\\\",\\\"2-183\\\",\\\"obligation\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(963, 'b855c029-de28-4056-aecc-7df5b2cfcf4b', 127, 3, 'What is the special gate of Paradise reserved only for those who fasted?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Bab al-Jihad\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Bab al-Salah\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Ar-Rayyan\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Bab al-Kawthar\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The special gate of Paradise called \"Ar-Rayyan\" is reserved exclusively for those who fasted. No one else will enter through it. After the fasting people enter, it will be closed.', 'Ar-Rayyan — a name that means \"well-watered/lush\" — fitting for those who endured thirst while fasting.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"sawm\\\",\\\"rayyan\\\",\\\"paradise\\\",\\\"gate\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(964, '472a82c7-c98a-4a44-82c5-cc1c06f5abac', 127, 3, 'What is the recommended Sunnah act to perform before Fajr during Ramadan?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Tahajjud prayer only\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Suhoor (pre-dawn meal)\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Reading Quran until sunrise\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Extra charity\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Suhoor (the pre-dawn meal) is a recommended Sunnah before Fajr. The Prophet ﷺ said there is blessing (Barakah) in Suhoor. It distinguishes Muslim fasting from others who fasted before Islam.', 'This meal is taken BEFORE the fast begins at Fajr.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"sawm\\\",\\\"suhoor\\\",\\\"sunnah\\\",\\\"ramadan\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(965, 'b306fe24-3863-4908-b0fe-2d97a0cbfbbe', 127, 3, 'What is the ruling when a person forgetfully eats or drinks while fasting?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"The fast is broken and Qada is required\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The fast is broken and Kaffarah is required\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The fast remains valid and no Qada is needed\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"The fast is broken and Fidyah is required\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'If a person forgetfully eats or drinks while fasting, their fast remains valid and no Qada or Kaffarah is needed. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Allah fed him and gave him drink.\" They should continue fasting once they remember.', 'Forgetfulness (Nisyan) is excused in Islamic law — the fast continues.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"sawm\\\",\\\"forgetfully\\\",\\\"eating\\\",\\\"ruling\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(966, '59f14184-e00e-4009-9c28-46e45d453f3e', 127, 3, 'What is the Kaffarah for deliberately breaking the fast through marital relations in Ramadan?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Make up 1 day (Qada) only\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Pay Fidyah for 60 days\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Free a slave, OR fast 60 consecutive days, OR feed 60 poor people\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Fast 3 days only\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Kaffarah (expiation) for marital relations during a Ramadan fast is: (1) Free a slave — if unable, (2) Fast 60 consecutive days — if unable, (3) Feed 60 poor people. This is the most severe expiation.', 'This is the only fast violation that requires Kaffarah (heavy expiation), not just Qada.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"sawm\\\",\\\"kaffarah\\\",\\\"marital-relations\\\",\\\"expiation\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(967, '9667bbc2-5530-49de-b554-02638ec5df08', 127, 3, 'What is Fidyah in the context of fasting?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Fasting 60 consecutive days\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Feeding one poor person for each missed fast day (for those permanently unable to fast)\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Making up missed fasts later (Qada)\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Paying money to the government\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Fidyah is feeding one poor person (approximately 2 meals) for each missed fast day. It applies to those who cannot fast and have no hope of recovery — such as the very elderly or chronically ill.', 'Fidyah is for those who CANNOT make up fasts — unlike Qada (making up later).', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"sawm\\\",\\\"fidyah\\\",\\\"elderly\\\",\\\"chronically-ill\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(968, '707ad8b2-292d-4e83-8931-ea86b323108d', 127, 3, 'On which nights of Ramadan is Laylat al-Qadr most likely to occur?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"The first 10 nights\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The middle 10 nights (11th-20th)\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The last 10 nights, especially odd nights (21st, 23rd, 25th, 27th, 29th)\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Every Friday of Ramadan\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Laylat al-Qadr is most likely in the last 10 nights of Ramadan, particularly the odd nights: 21st, 23rd, 25th, 27th, and 29th. Most scholars consider the 27th most likely based on various Hadith.', 'The Prophet ﷺ intensified worship in the LAST 10 nights of Ramadan to find it.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"sawm\\\",\\\"laylat-al-qadr\\\",\\\"last-10-nights\\\",\\\"odd\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(969, 'c0e688f3-2059-4201-8a41-56cdca82bf52', 127, 3, 'Which of the following does NOT break the fast?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Deliberate eating\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Deliberate vomiting\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"A blood test or non-nutritional injection\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Marital relations\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'A blood test or non-nutritional injection does NOT break the fast, as it does not involve consuming food or drink. Eye/ear drops, using a Miswak, and swallowing saliva also do not break the fast.', 'Focus on what constitutes \"eating/drinking\" — medical procedures without nutrition are different.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"sawm\\\",\\\"blood-test\\\",\\\"injection\\\",\\\"nullifiers\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(970, '866613a0-16cc-4f63-a491-da1e432e43ff', 127, 3, 'According to Hadith (Bukhari), what is the reward for fasting Ramadan with faith and seeking reward?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Wealth is increased\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"All previous sins are forgiven\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The person is given 70 times the reward\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Angels make dua for them for 70 years\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever fasts Ramadan with faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven.\" (Bukhari). The two conditions are: (1) with Iman (faith) and (2) seeking Allah\'s reward (Ihtisab).', 'Two conditions: faith + sincerely seeking Allah\'s reward = past sins forgiven.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"sawm\\\",\\\"ramadan\\\",\\\"forgiveness\\\",\\\"bukhari\\\",\\\"reward\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(971, '394c2543-85fd-49e7-aa0c-a7c40fa0d935', 127, 3, 'Laylat al-Qadr is described in the Quran as better than how many months?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"100 months\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"1,000 months\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"10,000 months\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"70 months\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Quran 97:3 (Surah Al-Qadr) states Laylat al-Qadr is \"better than a thousand months.\" 1,000 months = approximately 83 years and 4 months — meaning worship on this night equals a lifetime of worship.', 'Surah Al-Qadr (97) directly answers this — 1,000 months = 83+ years.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"sawm\\\",\\\"laylat-al-qadr\\\",\\\"1000-months\\\",\\\"quran-97-3\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(972, '17a02be4-9edb-4c0b-b735-721105bfac55', 127, 3, 'A pregnant woman fears harm to herself (not the child) if she fasts. What is the ruling on her fasting?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"She must fast regardless\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"She can skip fasting and pays Fidyah only with no Qada\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"She can skip fasting and makes Qada later (some scholars also say Fidyah)\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"She pays Kaffarah\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'A pregnant woman fearing harm to herself may break the fast and must make Qada (make up the missed days later). Some scholars also add Fidyah. This is different from an elderly person who only pays Fidyah without Qada.', 'Pregnant = temporary inability → Qada required. Elderly = permanent inability → Fidyah only.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"sawm\\\",\\\"pregnancy\\\",\\\"exemption\\\",\\\"qada\\\",\\\"fidyah\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(973, 'ef3ac03c-99bd-4298-97fd-856e21b0238b', 127, 3, 'What is the linguistic meaning of Hajj?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"To fast\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"To give charity\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"To pray\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"To intend \\\\\\/ to set out for\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'Hajj linguistically means \"to intend\" or \"to set out for.\" Islamically, it refers to visiting the Kaaba and performing specific rituals during the prescribed days of Dhul-Hijjah (8th to 13th).', 'The word conveys a sense of purposeful travel or intention.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"hajj\\\",\\\"definition\\\",\\\"linguistic\\\",\\\"pillar-5\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(974, 'c4aed16e-4051-4520-965c-dc88698e42a9', 127, 3, 'Which pillar of Islam is Hajj?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Third\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Fourth\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Second\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Fifth\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'Hajj is the FIFTH and final pillar of Islam. It is obligatory once in a lifetime for those who are physically, financially, and logistically able.', 'It is the last pillar — the culmination of the five pillars.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"hajj\\\",\\\"fifth\\\",\\\"pillar\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(975, 'd576a5d4-9af0-4cbf-8598-1196acb3a14e', 127, 3, 'In which year AH was Hajj made obligatory?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"2 AH\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"5 AH\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"9 AH\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"10 AH\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Hajj was made obligatory in 9 AH. The Quranic verse (3:97) states: \"Pilgrimage to this House is an obligation upon Allah for those who are able to find a way.\"', 'Remember: Zakah/Fasting = 2 AH; Hajj = 9 AH.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"hajj\\\",\\\"9AH\\\",\\\"obligation\\\",\\\"history\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(976, '7333170c-768f-4d78-96ed-8b01158f5878', 127, 3, 'What is the most important ritual/station of Hajj, without which the Hajj is invalid?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Tawaf al-Ifadah\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Wuquf (Standing) at Arafah\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Ramy al-Jamarat\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Tawaf al-Wada\'\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Hajj is Arafah.\" Standing (Wuquf) on the plain of Arafat on the 9th of Dhul-Hijjah is the most critical ritual. Missing it means the Hajj is not valid.', 'The Prophet ﷺ summarized Hajj in two words: \"Hajj is ___.\"', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"hajj\\\",\\\"arafah\\\",\\\"wuquf\\\",\\\"pillar\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(977, 'a03235bb-147c-4007-b01b-a3c2fafa8981', 127, 3, 'Which type of Hajj did Prophet Muhammad ﷺ perform?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Ifrad\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Qiran\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Tamattu\'\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"All three types equally\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Prophet Muhammad ﷺ performed Hajj Tamattu\' during his Farewell Pilgrimage. This involves performing Umrah first (during Hajj months), exiting Ihram, then entering a new Ihram for Hajj. It is considered the most virtuous and is the most common type.', 'The Prophet ﷺ recommended what he himself practiced.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"hajj\\\",\\\"tamattu\\\",\\\"prophet\\\",\\\"type\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(978, 'db0f08f0-1c5f-4695-925a-1559de06d3cd', 127, 3, 'What is \"Ramy al-Jamarat\" in Hajj?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Circumambulating the Kaaba\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Throwing pebbles at the pillars\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Standing at Arafah\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Shaving the head\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Ramy al-Jamarat means throwing pebbles at the pillars (Jamarat) in Mina. On the 10th of Dhul-Hijjah, 7 pebbles are thrown at the largest pillar (Jamrat al-Aqabah). On the 11th-12th, all three pillars are targeted.', 'Ramy = throwing; Jamarat = the stone pillars in Mina.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"hajj\\\",\\\"ramy\\\",\\\"jamarat\\\",\\\"pebbles\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(979, '7cb99ff8-ed50-4357-99e1-d18986e55a8e', 127, 3, 'What is the key difference between Hajj Tamattu\' and Hajj Qiran?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Tamattu\' does not include Umrah; Qiran does\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Tamattu\' does Umrah then exits Ihram before re-entering for Hajj; Qiran combines both in one continuous Ihram\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Both are identical except for timing\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Qiran is easier and requires no Hadi sacrifice\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Tamattu\': Umrah first → exit Ihram → new Ihram for Hajj (two separate Ihrams, Hadi required). Qiran: Umrah and Hajj together in ONE continuous Ihram (Hadi required). Ifrad: Hajj only (no Umrah, no Hadi required).', 'Tamattu = \"enjoyment/intermission\" between Umrah and Hajj; Qiran = combined with no break.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"hajj\\\",\\\"tamattu\\\",\\\"qiran\\\",\\\"ihram\\\",\\\"distinction\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(980, '97b89172-508c-4b77-98ec-3a2345c10f79', 127, 3, 'What happens at Muzdalifah during Hajj on the night of the 9th Dhul-Hijjah?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Tawaf al-Ifadah is performed\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Pilgrims stand in Arafah until sunrise\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Pilgrims combine Maghrib and Isha, rest, and collect pebbles for Ramy\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"The Hadi (sacrifice) is slaughtered\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'After leaving Arafah at sunset, pilgrims proceed to Muzdalifah, where they combine Maghrib and Isha prayers, spend the night, and collect pebbles to be thrown at the Jamarat the next day.', 'Muzdalifah is between Arafah and Mina — a rest stop where pebbles are collected.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"hajj\\\",\\\"muzdalifah\\\",\\\"pebbles\\\",\\\"maghrib-isha\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(981, 'c54f5cc7-2a98-40d8-9d89-1c0ec3aa73e8', 127, 3, 'What is \"Tawaf al-Wada\'\" and who is exempt from it?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"The first circumambulation upon arrival; exempt: elderly\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The farewell circumambulation before leaving Mecca; exempt: menstruating women\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"A voluntary Tawaf; exempt: non-pilgrims\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"The Tawaf on the 9th of Dhul-Hijjah; exempt: travelers\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Tawaf al-Wada\' is the farewell circumambulation of the Kaaba performed before leaving Mecca — it is obligatory for all pilgrims. The only exception is menstruating women, who are exempt due to the condition of purity required in the Masjid.', 'Wada\' = farewell in Arabic. Who is normally restricted from mosques?', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"hajj\\\",\\\"tawaf-wada\\\",\\\"farewell\\\",\\\"menstruating\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(982, '6fc3cc4d-fc89-4413-9547-68ec0520caca', 127, 3, 'On which day of Dhul-Hijjah do pilgrims stand at Arafah (Wuquf)?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"8th Dhul-Hijjah\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"10th Dhul-Hijjah\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"12th Dhul-Hijjah\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"9th Dhul-Hijjah\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'Wuquf (standing at Arafah) takes place on the 9th of Dhul-Hijjah from noon until sunset. This is the core ritual of Hajj — the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Hajj is Arafah.\"', 'The 9th of Dhul-Hijjah is also called \"Yawm Arafah\" (the Day of Arafah).', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"hajj\\\",\\\"arafah\\\",\\\"9th\\\",\\\"dhul-hijjah\\\",\\\"wuquf\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(983, '0e9597b2-6276-438f-b633-5c13bd1c6ea3', 127, 3, 'What does \"Halq or Taqsir\" refer to in Hajj rituals?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Throwing pebbles at the pillars\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The animal sacrifice\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Shaving the head (men) or trimming hair (women) to exit Ihram\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Circumambulating the Kaaba\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Halq means shaving the head (for men — which is preferable) and Taqsir means trimming the hair (an alternative for men, and the only option for women). Both mark partial or full exit from the state of Ihram.', 'Halq = complete shave (men); Taqsir = trim (men alternative/women only option).', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"hajj\\\",\\\"halq\\\",\\\"taqsir\\\",\\\"hair\\\",\\\"ihram\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(984, 'eb29c55f-b91c-4163-82f4-d55114428ec2', 127, 3, 'Which type of Hajj requires the Hadi (animal sacrifice), and which does NOT?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Ifrad and Qiran require Hadi; Tamattu\' does not\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"All three types require Hadi equally\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Tamattu\' and Qiran require Hadi; Ifrad does not\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Only Tamattu\' requires Hadi\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Tamattu\' and Qiran both require the Hadi (animal sacrifice) because the pilgrim benefits by combining Umrah and Hajj. Ifrad (Hajj only, no Umrah) does NOT require the Hadi sacrifice.', 'Hadi compensates for the \"benefit\" of combining Umrah with Hajj — Ifrad gets no such benefit.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"hajj\\\",\\\"hadi\\\",\\\"sacrifice\\\",\\\"tamattu\\\",\\\"qiran\\\",\\\"ifrad\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(985, '0f3e6f6f-b23c-4c1b-a76b-97275810bf8d', 127, 3, 'What are the prohibited acts during the state of Ihram?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Only cutting hair and nails\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Wearing perfume, hunting, marital relations, cutting hair\\\\\\/nails\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Only marital relations and hunting\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Salah and fasting\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'While in Ihram, a pilgrim must avoid: wearing perfume/scents, hunting, marital relations, cutting hair or nails, uprooting plants, and (for men) wearing sewn clothing and covering the head. Violations require a Fidyah or Dam (penalty).', 'Ihram creates a sacred boundary — a state of purity and restrictions.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"hajj\\\",\\\"ihram\\\",\\\"prohibitions\\\",\\\"mahzurat\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(986, 'ea72f803-f3ad-4156-aad4-78ffbba66d9b', 127, 3, 'What are the conditions for Hajj being OBLIGATORY on a Muslim?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Being Muslim, sane, adult, free, physically able, financially able, and route safe\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Being Muslim and having enough money only\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Being Muslim, adult, and physically able only\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Being Muslim, completing Ramadan, and paying Zakah first\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"1\\\"]\"', 'Hajj is obligatory when all conditions are met: (1) Muslim, (2) Sane, (3) Reached puberty, (4) Free (not enslaved), (5) Physical ability, (6) Financial ability (including family maintenance), and (7) Route safety.', 'There are 7 conditions — covering personal status, physical, financial, and security factors.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"hajj\\\",\\\"conditions\\\",\\\"obligatory\\\",\\\"ability\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(987, 'a0cb43c5-e7a7-48e4-a902-eda02296a038', 127, 3, 'What is the correct order of the Five Pillars of Islam?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Salah, Shahadah, Zakah, Sawm, Hajj\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Shahadah, Salah, Zakah, Sawm, Hajj\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Shahadah, Zakah, Salah, Hajj, Sawm\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Shahadah, Salah, Sawm, Zakah, Hajj\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The Five Pillars in correct order: (1) Shahadah (Declaration of Faith), (2) Salah (Prayer), (3) Zakah (Alms-giving), (4) Sawm (Fasting), (5) Hajj (Pilgrimage). This order is based on the famous Hadith of Jibreel.', 'S-S-Z-S-H: Shahadah, Salah, Zakah, Sawm, Hajj.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"pillars\\\",\\\"order\\\",\\\"comprehensive\\\",\\\"all-five\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(988, 'e1796915-ce90-420e-b32a-8115a1c9c3e5', 127, 3, 'Which two pillars of Islam were made obligatory in 2 AH?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Salah and Hajj\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Zakah and Sawm (Fasting)\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Shahadah and Salah\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Hajj and Zakah\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Both Zakah and Sawm (fasting in Ramadan) were made obligatory in 2 AH (After Hijra). Salah was made obligatory during the Mi\'raj (before Hijra), and Hajj was made obligatory in 9 AH.', 'Three different time periods: Mi\'raj (Salah), 2 AH (Zakah + Fasting), 9 AH (Hajj).', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"zakah\\\",\\\"sawm\\\",\\\"2AH\\\",\\\"history\\\",\\\"pillars\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(989, '680ac8a0-80a2-4c67-8cf9-6ae382f20d7e', 127, 3, 'Which pillar of Islam is obligatory only ONCE in a lifetime (if conditions are met)?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Salah\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Zakah\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Sawm\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Hajj\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'Hajj is obligatory only once in a lifetime for those who meet all conditions (ability). Additional Hajj beyond the first is voluntary (Nafl). The Quran 3:97 says: \"...an obligation upon Allah for those who are able.\"', 'Daily prayers = 5 times/day; Zakah = annually; Sawm = 29-30 days/year; _____ = once in life.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"hajj\\\",\\\"once-in-lifetime\\\",\\\"pillar\\\",\\\"obligation\\\"]\"', 'Five Pillars of Islam Notes', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:43:54', '2026-04-27 21:43:54'),
(990, 'cc12e626-6775-4daf-b440-62695ae74649', 128, 3, 'What is Tawhid?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Oneness of Allah\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Many gods\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Angel belief\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Book belief\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"1\\\"]\"', 'Tawhid means belief in one Allah.', 'Basic', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"tawhid\\\"]\"', 'Iman Book', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:52:16', '2026-04-27 21:52:16'),
(991, '9f24319e-7b33-46af-aa07-355af7719c1b', 128, 3, 'Creator belongs to?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Uluhiyyah\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Rububiyyah\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Names\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"None\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Creator is Rububiyyah.', 'Think creator', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"tawhid\\\"]\"', 'Iman Book', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:52:16', '2026-04-27 21:52:16'),
(992, 'a3f260fe-f24a-4cb5-8831-020000fd96f1', 128, 3, 'Angels made of?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Fire\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Light\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Clay\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Water\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Light.', 'Recall', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"angels\\\"]\"', 'Iman Book', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:52:16', '2026-04-27 21:52:16'),
(993, '9535d6e8-3e6e-4341-a0fa-0f536da004a2', 128, 3, 'Jibreel duty?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Death\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Rain\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Revelation\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Recording\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Brings revelation.', 'Wahi', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"angels\\\"]\"', 'Iman Book', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-27 21:52:16', '2026-04-27 21:52:16'),
