(1114, '8306ea4a-f768-4995-8f45-651ab9affaa2', 132, 3, 'Which Rightly Guided Caliph had the LONGEST reign?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Abu Bakr (RA)\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Umar (RA)\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Uthman (RA)\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Ali (RA)\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Uthman (RA) ruled for 12 years (23–35 AH), the longest among all four Rightly Guided Caliphs.', 'Compare: Abu Bakr 2y 3m, Umar 10y 6m, Uthman 12y, Ali 5y.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Uthman\\\",\\\"Duration\\\",\\\"Caliphate\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1115, '84c8952f-173f-4eb3-8d76-757233c63c94', 132, 3, 'Which Rightly Guided Caliph had the SHORTEST reign?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Abu Bakr (RA)\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Umar (RA)\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Uthman (RA)\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Ali (RA)\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"1\\\"]\"', 'Abu Bakr (RA) ruled for 2 years and 3 months (11–13 AH), the shortest reign.', 'His caliphate was from 11 AH to 13 AH.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Abu Bakr\\\",\\\"Duration\\\",\\\"Caliphate\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1116, '61a88caa-4e0d-4f30-af2b-8812065e8204', 132, 3, 'What is the title of Hasan bin Ali (RA)?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Asadullah\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Dhun-Noorayn\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Sabt ar-Rasul\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Al-Farooq\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Hasan bin Ali (RA) held the title \'Sabt ar-Rasul\' meaning grandson of the Messenger.', 'Sabt means grandson in Arabic.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Hasan bin Ali\\\",\\\"Title\\\",\\\"Sabt ar-Rasul\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1117, '0aa22193-5103-4d98-a0f4-bfbc6d16dce9', 132, 3, 'For how long did Hasan bin Ali (RA) serve as Caliph?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"1 year\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"6 months\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"3 months\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"2 years\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Hasan (RA) served as Caliph for 6 months (40–41 AH) before handing the caliphate to Mu\'awiyah.', 'This brief caliphate completed the 30-year period prophesied in the hadith.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Hasan bin Ali\\\",\\\"6 months\\\",\\\"Caliphate\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1118, 'b251a356-3c43-4454-9a55-9e64229af0cd', 132, 3, 'What was the actual name of Abu Bakr as-Siddiq (RA)?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Umar bin Khattab\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Abdullah bin Uthman\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Ali bin Abi Talib\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Uthman bin Affan\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Abu Bakr\'s actual name was Abdullah bin Uthman bin Amir (Abu Quhafah). Abu Bakr was his kunya (nickname).', 'His father was known as Abu Quhafah.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Abu Bakr\\\",\\\"Name\\\",\\\"Companions\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1119, 'c6b5b4ff-ef41-4a0e-a8dd-87c5d105d85a', 132, 3, 'What does the title \'As-Siddiq\' mean?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"The Brave\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The Ever-Truthful\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The Freed One\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"The Distinguisher\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'As-Siddiq means \'the ever-truthful\'. Abu Bakr received this title for immediately believing the account of Isra wal-Mi\'raj.', 'Siddiq is derived from \'Sidq\' meaning truth.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Abu Bakr\\\",\\\"As-Siddiq\\\",\\\"Title\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1120, '0e8d8fe0-3399-4629-b6c2-5e795ded1fa8', 132, 3, 'Abu Bakr (RA) was the father-in-law of the Prophet ﷺ through which daughter?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Fatimah (RA)\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Zainab (RA)\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Aisha (RA)\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Umm Kulthum (RA)\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Abu Bakr (RA) was the father of Aisha (RA), wife of the Prophet ﷺ, making him the Prophet\'s father-in-law.', 'Aisha (RA) is the most famous wife of the Prophet and daughter of Abu Bakr.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Abu Bakr\\\",\\\"Aisha\\\",\\\"Family\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1121, '0aa20f94-9119-4709-810e-32341d71b469', 132, 3, 'Where was Abu Bakr (RA) selected as the first Caliph?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Masjid an-Nabawi\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Saqifah Bani Sa\'idah\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Masjid al-Haram\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Cave of Hira\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'After the death of the Prophet ﷺ, the Companions gathered at Saqifah Bani Sa\'idah and selected Abu Bakr (RA) as the first Caliph.', 'Saqifah means a covered hall where the Ansar used to gather.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Abu Bakr\\\",\\\"Saqifah\\\",\\\"Caliphate Selection\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1122, 'f76da57a-ef9f-4ee9-a434-0a1e9aaac573', 132, 3, 'How many Huffaz were martyred in the Battle of Yamamah during Abu Bakr\'s caliphate?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"300\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"500\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"700\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"1000\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '700 Huffaz (Quran memorizers) were martyred in the Battle of Yamamah, which prompted Umar to advise the compilation of the Quran.', 'This great loss led to the concern about the Quran being lost with its memorizers.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Battle of Yamamah\\\",\\\"Huffaz\\\",\\\"700\\\",\\\"Quran\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1123, 'b2022d86-bc53-439e-a921-cd77658c4157', 132, 3, 'On whose advice did Abu Bakr (RA) order the compilation of the Quran?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Ali (RA)\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Uthman (RA)\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Umar (RA)\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Zaid bin Thabit\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Umar (RA) advised Abu Bakr (RA) to compile the Quran after 700 Huffaz were martyred in the Battle of Yamamah.', 'The fear of losing Quran memorizers prompted this suggestion.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Quran Compilation\\\",\\\"Abu Bakr\\\",\\\"Umar\\\",\\\"Advice\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1124, '324f6c71-d2d5-4776-92e7-32e57acecbd3', 132, 3, 'Who was ordered to compile the Quran into a single volume during Abu Bakr\'s caliphate?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Umar bin Khattab\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Ali bin Abi Talib\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Zaid bin Thabit\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Abdullah bin Masud\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Abu Bakr ordered Zaid bin Thabit to compile the Quran into a single Mushaf. Zaid was one of the Prophet\'s chief scribes.', 'Zaid bin Thabit was a trusted scribe who had written revelation for the Prophet.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Zaid bin Thabit\\\",\\\"Quran Compilation\\\",\\\"Abu Bakr\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1125, '19d95776-af08-45ed-847a-615d4fc8d6cb', 132, 3, 'Which false prophet was fought in the Battle of Yamamah?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Tulayhah al-Asadi\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Aswad al-Ansi\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Musaylimah al-Kadhdhab\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Sajah\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Battle of Yamamah was specifically fought against Musaylimah al-Kadhdhab, the most powerful false prophet.', 'Al-Kadhdhab means \'the liar\' — a title given by Muslims to this false prophet.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Musaylimah\\\",\\\"Battle of Yamamah\\\",\\\"Wars of Riddah\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1126, '6abdef17-30f9-4038-9f81-ac997ac66a49', 132, 3, 'At what age did Abu Bakr (RA) pass away?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"55\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"60\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"63\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"70\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Abu Bakr (RA) passed away at 63 years of age in 13 AH (634 CE), the same age as the Prophet ﷺ.', 'He died in 13 AH, just over 2 years after becoming Caliph.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Abu Bakr\\\",\\\"Death\\\",\\\"Age\\\",\\\"13 AH\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1127, '5831ee6a-a7a9-43ea-a676-62f4440b3224', 132, 3, 'Where is Abu Bakr (RA) buried?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Jannat al-Baqi, Medina\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Masjid al-Haram, Makkah\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Chamber of Aisha beside the Prophet \\\\ufdfa\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Najaf, Iraq\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Abu Bakr (RA) is buried in the chamber of Aisha in Masjid an-Nabawi, right beside the Prophet ﷺ.', 'Both the Prophet and Abu Bakr share the same burial chamber in Masjid an-Nabawi.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Abu Bakr\\\",\\\"Burial\\\",\\\"Masjid an-Nabawi\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1128, '2efd6122-1b44-4889-b878-e1c1a35e146c', 132, 3, 'What does the title \'Al-Farooq\' mean?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"The Brave Lion\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The Distinguisher between Truth and Falsehood\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The Possessor of Two Lights\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"The Wealthy\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Al-Farooq means \'the distinguisher between truth and falsehood\'. The Prophet ﷺ gave Umar this title.', 'Farooq comes from \'Farq\' meaning to distinguish or separate.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Umar\\\",\\\"Al-Farooq\\\",\\\"Title\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1129, '8aa532ad-909f-45e7-b611-b6b2be01d3ba', 132, 3, 'In which year AH was the Hijri Calendar introduced?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"13 AH\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"15 AH\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"17 AH\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"20 AH\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Hijri Calendar was introduced in 17 AH during Umar\'s caliphate, on the advice of Ali (RA), with Muharram as the first month.', 'It was introduced about 6 years into Umar\'s caliphate.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Hijri Calendar\\\",\\\"17 AH\\\",\\\"Umar\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1130, '98edef68-adb7-4ae1-b15b-59d0cf9b9313', 132, 3, 'Who suggested starting the Hijri Calendar?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Abu Bakr (RA)\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Uthman (RA)\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Ali (RA)\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Zaid bin Thabit\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Ali (RA) suggested using the Hijra of the Prophet as the starting point, and Umar (RA) implemented it in 17 AH.', 'The calendar begins from the year the Prophet migrated to Medina.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Hijri Calendar\\\",\\\"Ali\\\",\\\"Umar\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1131, '9b3ffd83-706b-4ce4-973a-d7c2d50d7672', 132, 3, 'The Battle of Yarmouk (15 AH) was a victory against which power?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Persians\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Mongols\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Byzantines (Romans)\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Crusaders\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Battle of Yarmouk in 15 AH (636 CE) was a decisive Muslim victory over the Byzantine (Roman) forces in Syria.', 'Yarmouk is a river in Syria — the battle was fought near it.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Battle of Yarmouk\\\",\\\"Umar\\\",\\\"Byzantines\\\",\\\"15 AH\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1132, '419f0f67-4e53-4b25-ba7d-cfc36c47aa62', 132, 3, 'The Battle of Qadisiyyah (16 AH) resulted in the defeat of which empire?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Byzantine Empire\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Mongol Empire\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Sassanid Persian Empire\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Roman Empire\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Battle of Qadisiyyah in 16 AH (637 CE) defeated the Sassanid Persian forces, opening the way for Muslim conquest of Persia.', 'Qadisiyyah was the decisive battle that broke the Persian military power permanently.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Battle of Qadisiyyah\\\",\\\"Umar\\\",\\\"Persia\\\",\\\"16 AH\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1133, '09eeed01-04ad-4292-b81e-337b8d0b644f', 132, 3, 'Umar (RA) personally traveled to accept the surrender of which city?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Damascus\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Baghdad\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Jerusalem\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Cairo\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'When Jerusalem was conquered in 16 AH (638 CE), Umar (RA) personally traveled there to accept its surrender and pray.', 'The patriarch of Jerusalem requested only the Caliph himself come to receive the city.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Jerusalem\\\",\\\"Umar\\\",\\\"Conquest\\\",\\\"16 AH\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1134, '6f4118aa-d05f-4d6f-ae48-88510b3671de', 132, 3, 'Who conquered Egypt during the caliphate of Umar (RA)?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Khalid bin Walid\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Amr ibn al-As\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Sa\'d bin Abi Waqqas\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Usamah bin Zaid\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Amr ibn al-As conquered Egypt in 19 AH (640 CE) under the orders of Umar (RA).', 'He later became the governor of Egypt after its conquest.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Egypt\\\",\\\"Amr ibn al-As\\\",\\\"Umar\\\",\\\"19 AH\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1135, '4bfe3784-efb9-4e2c-aefb-adcd00f31ed1', 132, 3, 'Who assassinated Umar al-Farooq (RA)?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Abdullah ibn Saba\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Abdur-Rahman ibn Muljam\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Abu Lu\'lu Firoz\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Hajjaj bin Yusuf\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Umar (RA) was assassinated by Abu Lu\'lu Firoz, a Persian slave, who stabbed him 3 times with a dagger while he was leading the Fajr prayer.', 'He was a non-Muslim Persian slave who attacked while Umar led morning prayer.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Umar\\\",\\\"Assassination\\\",\\\"Abu Lu\'lu Firoz\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1136, '80e1cc0d-bbba-46c6-9ca6-499395fd81a5', 132, 3, 'Umar (RA) was the father-in-law of the Prophet ﷺ through which daughter?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Aisha (RA)\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Fatimah (RA)\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Hafsa (RA)\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Umm Kulthum (RA)\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Umar (RA) was the father of Hafsa (RA), who was a wife of the Prophet ﷺ, making him the Prophet\'s father-in-law.', 'Hafsa (RA) is the daughter of Umar and a wife of the Prophet.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Umar\\\",\\\"Hafsa\\\",\\\"Family\\\",\\\"Prophet\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1137, '8c9cbe5d-729c-49e9-aa61-9033ceb13baa', 132, 3, 'What does the title \'Dhun-Noorayn\' mean?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"The Wealthy\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The Possessor of Two Lights\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The Rightly Guided\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"The Brave\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Dhun-Noorayn means \'possessor of two lights\' because Uthman married two daughters of the Prophet ﷺ — Ruqayyah then Umm Kulthum.', 'Noorayn means two lights — referring to two daughters of the Prophet.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Uthman\\\",\\\"Dhun-Noorayn\\\",\\\"Title\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1138, '952beb29-d998-456e-b8d9-ece4aa5e5039', 132, 3, 'Which two daughters of the Prophet ﷺ did Uthman (RA) marry?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Fatimah and Zainab\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Ruqayyah and Umm Kulthum\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Zainab and Umm Kulthum\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Ruqayyah and Fatimah\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Uthman (RA) first married Ruqayyah (RA), and after her death married Umm Kulthum (RA), earning the title Dhun-Noorayn.', 'He was the only man to marry two daughters of a prophet.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Uthman\\\",\\\"Ruqayyah\\\",\\\"Umm Kulthum\\\",\\\"Prophet\'s daughters\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1139, 'b54b9971-486b-4a8f-8705-e17931e81d21', 132, 3, 'Why did Uthman (RA) standardize the Quran?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"To increase the number of copies\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Because different regions had different recitations causing confusion\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"To replace Abu Bakr\'s compilation\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"On instruction of the Prophet \\\\ufdfa\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Uthman (RA) noticed different recitations of the Quran in different regions causing confusion, so he prepared a standard Mushaf.', 'The issue arose when Muslim armies from different regions met and recited Quran differently.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Uthman\\\",\\\"Quran Standardization\\\",\\\"Mushaf\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1140, '7404060c-46bb-45a8-811b-b4f9c63e364a', 132, 3, 'How many copies of the standardized Mushaf did Uthman (RA) prepare?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"2-3 copies\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"4-6 copies\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"7-8 copies\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"10 copies\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Uthman (RA) prepared 4-6 copies of the standardized Mushaf, sending them to Makkah, Kufa, Basra, Damascus, and keeping one in Medina.', 'Copies were distributed to major cities of the Islamic state.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Uthman\\\",\\\"Mushaf Copies\\\",\\\"Quran\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04');
INSERT INTO `mcqs` (`id`, `uuid`, `topic_id`, `subject_id`, `question`, `question_type`, `options`, `correct_answers`, `explanation`, `hint`, `difficulty_level`, `time_limit_seconds`, `marks`, `negative_marks`, `tags`, `reference_book`, `reference_page`, `is_premium`, `is_verified`, `status`, `created_by`, `approved_by`, `approved_at`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(1141, '9c5a9965-997d-43c5-9fed-77afcb4c5608', 132, 3, 'What did Uthman (RA) do with the old and differing copies of the Quran?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Buried them\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Kept them in a library\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Burned and destroyed them\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Sent them to scholars\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Uthman (RA) ordered the burning and destruction of all old and differing copies to ensure only the standardized Mushaf was used.', 'This ensured uniformity in Quranic recitation throughout the Muslim world.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Uthman\\\",\\\"Quran\\\",\\\"Old Copies\\\",\\\"Burned\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1142, '3d8d881a-ba72-4b5a-af9f-a756c63f5fc6', 132, 3, 'Who was allowed to build a navy during Uthman\'s (RA) caliphate?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Amr ibn al-As\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Khalid bin Walid\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Mu\'awiyah (governor of Syria)\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Sa\'d bin Abi Waqqas\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Uthman (RA) allowed Mu\'awiyah, governor of Syria, to establish naval forces, making it the first Muslim navy.', 'Syria\'s coastal location made Mu\'awiyah the ideal person to build a navy.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Uthman\\\",\\\"Navy\\\",\\\"Mu\'awiyah\\\",\\\"Naval Forces\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1143, '38c4d99e-e0a7-43d1-9fda-88e9269f28bd', 132, 3, 'How was Uthman (RA) martyred?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Stabbed while leading prayer\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Poisoned\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Rebels broke into his house and martyred him while he recited Quran\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Killed in battle\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'In 35 AH, rebels besieged Medina, broke into Uthman\'s house, and martyred him while he was reciting the Quran.', 'The date was 18th Dhul Hijjah 35 AH.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Uthman\\\",\\\"Martyrdom\\\",\\\"35 AH\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1144, '8bb0681c-603f-4c3a-bcf8-be62d4a05015', 132, 3, 'At what age was Uthman (RA) martyred?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"63 years\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"70 years\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"75 years\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"82 years\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'Uthman (RA) was approximately 82 years old (some say 86) when he was martyred on 18th Dhul Hijjah 35 AH.', 'He lived much longer than the other Rightly Guided Caliphs.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Uthman\\\",\\\"Age\\\",\\\"Martyrdom\\\",\\\"82\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1145, '5bcb4b20-73f2-4e86-86f1-f7f3935f3ccf', 132, 3, 'Where is Uthman (RA) buried?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Masjid an-Nabawi\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Chamber of Aisha\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Jannat al-Baqi, Medina\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Najaf, Iraq\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Uthman (RA) is buried in Jannat al-Baqi, the famous cemetery in Medina.', 'Jannat al-Baqi is the graveyard adjacent to Masjid an-Nabawi.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Uthman\\\",\\\"Burial\\\",\\\"Jannat al-Baqi\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1146, '5a3d437f-d168-407a-aa9d-4772b70c3082', 132, 3, 'What does the title \'Asadullah\' mean?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Lion of the Tribe\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Lion of Allah\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Sword of Allah\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Shield of Allah\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Asadullah means \'Lion of Allah\'. Ali (RA) was also called Al-Murtada meaning \'the pleased one\'.', 'Asad means lion in Arabic.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Ali\\\",\\\"Asadullah\\\",\\\"Title\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1147, '4edc37b1-f1b5-46ac-9571-e2bc802c2f57', 132, 3, 'Ali (RA) was the first child to accept Islam at what age?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Age 7\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Age 8\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Age 10\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Age 12\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Ali (RA) accepted Islam at the age of 10, making him the first child to embrace Islam.', 'He was living in the Prophet\'s household when Islam was revealed.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Ali\\\",\\\"First Child\\\",\\\"Islam\\\",\\\"Age 10\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1148, '9d5cf06c-0485-4434-826e-314a998a6171', 132, 3, 'Why did Ali (RA) move the capital from Medina to Kufa?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Kufa was richer\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Medina was too hot\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The rebels\' center was in Iraq\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"The Prophet recommended it\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Ali (RA) moved the capital to Kufa (Iraq) because the center of opposition and rebels was in Iraq, making it strategically important.', 'Kufa was centrally located in the Muslim world and closer to the areas of conflict.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Ali\\\",\\\"Capital\\\",\\\"Kufa\\\",\\\"Medina\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1149, 'fd1b247c-caff-47aa-8e5d-070473306736', 132, 3, 'The Battle of the Camel (Jamal) in 36 AH was fought between Ali (RA) and which group?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Mu\'awiyah and the Syrians\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Kharijites\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Aisha (RA), Talhah (RA) and Zubair (RA)\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Persian rebels\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Battle of the Camel (36 AH) was the first internal Muslim battle, fought between Ali (RA) and the forces of Aisha, Talhah, and Zubair.', 'It is called \'Jamal\' (camel) because Aisha watched from a litter on a camel.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Battle of Camel\\\",\\\"Jamal\\\",\\\"Ali\\\",\\\"Aisha\\\",\\\"36 AH\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1150, '7bd41973-22df-4370-8a19-34d7e8c57de5', 132, 3, 'What was agreed upon at the end of the Battle of Siffin (37 AH)?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Ali became sole ruler\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Mu\'awiyah surrendered\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Arbitration (Tahkim) between both sides\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"A truce of 10 years\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'After the Battle of Siffin (37 AH) between Ali and Mu\'awiyah, arbitration (Tahkim) was agreed upon to resolve the dispute.', 'This arbitration led to the emergence of the Kharijites who opposed it.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Battle of Siffin\\\",\\\"Tahkim\\\",\\\"Arbitration\\\",\\\"Ali\\\",\\\"Mu\'awiyah\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1151, 'd5cc0bfa-df37-4bd9-bc02-c1cb4aceb612', 132, 3, 'Who emerged as a new group after the Battle of Siffin?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Mu\'tazilah\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Shia\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Kharijites\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Murji\'ah\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Kharijites emerged after the Battle of Siffin, opposing both Ali and Mu\'awiyah. They believed anyone who accepted arbitration was an unbeliever.', 'Kharijites literally means \'those who went out\' (withdrew from the army).', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Kharijites\\\",\\\"Battle of Siffin\\\",\\\"Ali\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1152, '578bc17d-eb49-4a15-819a-45b3021a7a6d', 132, 3, 'Who assassinated Ali al-Murtada (RA)?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Abu Lu\'lu Firoz\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Hajjaj bin Yusuf\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Abdur-Rahman ibn Muljam\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Yazid bin Mu\'awiyah\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Ali (RA) was assassinated by Abdur-Rahman ibn Muljam, a Kharijite, who struck him with a poisoned sword while he was leading the Fajr prayer on 17th (or 19th) Ramadan 40 AH.', 'Ibn Muljam was a Kharijite who opposed Ali\'s acceptance of arbitration at Siffin.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Ali\\\",\\\"Assassination\\\",\\\"Ibn Muljam\\\",\\\"Kharijite\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1153, '912afeab-ae50-4f1b-b4ee-7473ea9aafa3', 132, 3, 'Where is Ali (RA) buried?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Medina\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Makkah\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Najaf, Iraq\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Damascus\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Ali (RA) is buried in Najaf, Iraq, which is near Kufa — the capital he had established.', 'Najaf became a major pilgrimage site for Muslims after Ali\'s burial there.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Ali\\\",\\\"Burial\\\",\\\"Najaf\\\",\\\"Iraq\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1154, '98b14e7d-f6a9-4eab-8cd3-0e309d7d3afb', 132, 3, 'What is the peace made by Hasan (RA) with Mu\'awiyah called?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Hudaybiyyah Peace\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Aam al-Jama\'ah\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Sulh-e-Kul\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Al-Aman\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The peace between Hasan (RA) and Mu\'awiyah is called \'Aam al-Jama\'ah\' meaning \'The Year of Unity\', as it united the Muslim community under one ruler.', 'Jama\'ah means gathering or unity — this year reunified the Muslim ummah.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Hasan\\\",\\\"Mu\'awiyah\\\",\\\"Aam al-Jama\'ah\\\",\\\"Peace\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1155, '0b0919f0-5206-4a3b-9d5f-298fcd7ea06d', 132, 3, 'Who founded the Umayyad Caliphate?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Yazid bin Mu\'awiyah\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Abdul Malik bin Marwan\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Mu\'awiyah bin Abi Sufyan\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Marwan bin al-Hakam\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Mu\'awiyah bin Abi Sufyan (RA) founded the Umayyad Caliphate in 41 AH with Damascus as the capital.', 'He became Caliph after Hasan (RA) handed over the caliphate.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Mu\'awiyah\\\",\\\"Umayyad\\\",\\\"Founder\\\",\\\"Damascus\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '7', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1156, '2f718fc3-f9af-459f-9066-315e23561eb9', 132, 3, 'What was the capital of the Umayyad Caliphate?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Baghdad\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Kufa\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Damascus\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Jerusalem\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Damascus (Syria) was the capital of the Umayyad Caliphate throughout its existence (41–132 AH).', 'Mu\'awiyah had been the governor of Syria before becoming Caliph.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Umayyad\\\",\\\"Damascus\\\",\\\"Capital\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '7', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1157, 'fe4c0569-5a6b-490b-b5ef-ff11a04be828', 132, 3, 'During whose reign did the Battle of Karbala and martyrdom of Husayn (RA) take place?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Mu\'awiyah bin Abi Sufyan\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Abdul Malik bin Marwan\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Yazid bin Mu\'awiyah\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Al-Waleed bin Abdul Malik\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Battle of Karbala occurred in 61 AH during the reign of Yazid bin Mu\'awiyah, resulting in the martyrdom of Husayn (RA).', 'Karbala is in present-day Iraq — 61 AH corresponds to 680 CE.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Battle of Karbala\\\",\\\"Yazid\\\",\\\"Husayn\\\",\\\"61 AH\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '7', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1158, 'fa47a43d-dac8-437a-a9e6-297a09d3ad41', 132, 3, 'Who built the Dome of the Rock (Qubbat as-Sakhrah) in Jerusalem?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Mu\'awiyah bin Abi Sufyan\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Al-Waleed bin Abdul Malik\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Abdul Malik bin Marwan\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Umar bin Abdul Aziz\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Abdul Malik bin Marwan (65–86 AH) built the famous Dome of the Rock (Qubbat as-Sakhrah) in Jerusalem and was the first to mint Islamic coins.', 'The Dome of the Rock is one of the oldest surviving Islamic structures.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Abdul Malik\\\",\\\"Dome of Rock\\\",\\\"Jerusalem\\\",\\\"Umayyad\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '7', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1159, '29e626b3-e0e8-4316-ae7e-c6886dd81c59', 132, 3, 'Which Umayyad Caliph conquered Spain (Andalus)?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Sulayman bin Abdul Malik\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Abdul Malik bin Marwan\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Umar bin Abdul Aziz\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Al-Waleed bin Abdul Malik\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'Al-Waleed bin Abdul Malik (86–96 AH) oversaw the conquest of Spain (Andalus) under the command of Tariq bin Ziyad.', 'Tariq bin Ziyad crossed the strait (later named Gibraltar after him) to conquer Spain.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Al-Waleed\\\",\\\"Spain\\\",\\\"Andalus\\\",\\\"Umayyad\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '7', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1160, '86aad346-d259-4537-9372-2149369f2ce1', 132, 3, 'Which Umayyad Caliph is called the \'Fifth Rightly Guided Caliph\'?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Mu\'awiyah bin Abi Sufyan\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Yazid bin Mu\'awiyah\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Abdul Malik bin Marwan\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Umar bin Abdul Aziz\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'Umar bin Abdul Aziz (99–101 AH) is called the \'Fifth Rightly Guided Caliph\' due to his extraordinary justice, fairness and simple lifestyle.', 'He reigned for only 2 years 5 months but is renowned for his just rule.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Umar bin Abdul Aziz\\\",\\\"Fifth Rightly Guided Caliph\\\",\\\"Umayyad\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '7', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1161, '4cdf79be-ddf0-4c16-a0f5-ac8edc4c180b', 132, 3, 'What distinguishing act did Umar bin Abdul Aziz do regarding Husayn (RA)?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Built a shrine for Husayn\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Abolished the practice of cursing Husayn\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Wrote a biography of Husayn\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Declared Husayn a martyr\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Umar bin Abdul Aziz abolished the Umayyad practice of cursing Husayn (RA) from pulpits, which had been a shameful tradition since Yazid\'s time.', 'This practice had been introduced after Karbala and was ended by Umar bin Abdul Aziz.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Umar bin Abdul Aziz\\\",\\\"Husayn\\\",\\\"Cursing Abolished\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '7', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1162, 'e047e842-b0aa-4533-83fe-73105fae8586', 132, 3, 'Who was the last Caliph of the Umayyad dynasty?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Umar bin Abdul Aziz\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Sulayman bin Abdul Malik\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Hisham bin Abdul Malik\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Marwan bin Muhammad\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'Marwan bin Muhammad (127–132 AH) was the last Umayyad Caliph. The Umayyad Caliphate ended at the hands of the Abbasids in 132 AH.', 'He ruled during the final years of the Umayyad dynasty before its collapse.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Umayyad\\\",\\\"Last Caliph\\\",\\\"Marwan bin Muhammad\\\",\\\"132 AH\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '7', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1163, '505679f2-d46e-42b6-9c16-7a00072f9a4e', 132, 3, 'How long did the Umayyad Caliphate last?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Approximately 50 years\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Approximately 70 years\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Approximately 90 years\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Approximately 120 years\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Umayyad Caliphate lasted approximately 90 years, from 41 AH to 132 AH, with a total of 14 Caliphs.', 'It began with Mu\'awiyah and ended with Marwan bin Muhammad.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Umayyad\\\",\\\"Duration\\\",\\\"90 years\\\",\\\"41-132 AH\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '7', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1164, 'ca8c820b-6fb0-477b-8870-7769887a7d32', 132, 3, 'Who founded the Abbasid Caliphate?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Abu Ja\'far al-Mansur\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Harun ar-Rashid\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Al-Ma\'mun ar-Rashid\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Abul Abbas as-Saffah\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'Abul Abbas as-Saffah founded the Abbasid Caliphate in 132 AH after overthrowing the Umayyads.', 'As-Saffah means \'the blood-shedder\' due to his harsh treatment of the Umayyads.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Abbasid\\\",\\\"Founder\\\",\\\"Abul Abbas as-Saffah\\\",\\\"132 AH\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '8', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1165, '9cfbfe5b-cd2a-435b-87d5-5fc1c54e9597', 132, 3, 'What was the capital of the Abbasid Caliphate?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Damascus\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Kufa\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Baghdad\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Samarra\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Baghdad (Iraq) was the main capital of the Abbasid Caliphate. It was later briefly shifted to Samarra. Baghdad was founded by al-Mansur in 145 AH.', 'Baghdad became the largest and most prosperous city in the world during the Abbasid Golden Age.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Abbasid\\\",\\\"Baghdad\\\",\\\"Capital\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '8', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1166, 'bfa8b551-1a51-4397-8191-d5bc860dff81', 132, 3, 'Who founded the city of Baghdad?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Abul Abbas as-Saffah\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Harun ar-Rashid\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Abu Ja\'far al-Mansur\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Al-Ma\'mun ar-Rashid\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Abu Ja\'far al-Mansur (136–158 AH) founded the city of Baghdad in 145 AH, which became the Abbasid capital.', 'Al-Mansur chose the location carefully for its strategic and agricultural advantages.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Baghdad\\\",\\\"Al-Mansur\\\",\\\"145 AH\\\",\\\"Abbasid\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '8', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1167, '42bb9c3d-3f23-49f9-9649-1a7f925abab0', 132, 3, 'Whose era is called the \'Golden Age\' of the Abbasid Caliphate?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Abu Ja\'far al-Mansur\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Al-Ma\'mun ar-Rashid\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Harun ar-Rashid\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Al-Mu\'tasim Billah\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Harun ar-Rashid\'s era (170–193 AH) is called the \'Golden Age\' of the Abbasids, known for the House of Wisdom and great cultural achievements.', 'He had diplomatic relations with Charlemagne of France and the emperor of China.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Harun ar-Rashid\\\",\\\"Golden Age\\\",\\\"Abbasid\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '8', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1168, 'aaae1415-7bda-4ded-9166-a3f435d2f7f7', 132, 3, 'What was the \'Bait-ul-Hikmah\' (House of Wisdom)?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"A royal palace in Baghdad\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The world\'s largest library and research center in Baghdad\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"A religious school in Kufa\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"A treasury in Samarra\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Bait-ul-Hikmah (House of Wisdom) was the world\'s largest library and research center established in Baghdad during Harun ar-Rashid\'s era, promoting science, math, and philosophy.', 'It attracted scholars from across the world and facilitated the translation of Greek texts.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Bait-ul-Hikmah\\\",\\\"House of Wisdom\\\",\\\"Harun ar-Rashid\\\",\\\"Baghdad\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '8', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1169, '419d70aa-080a-4976-a539-fe9cb6e19a82', 132, 3, 'Which Abbasid Caliph promoted the Mu\'tazilah school of thought as state religion?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Harun ar-Rashid\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Al-Mu\'tasim Billah\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Al-Ma\'mun ar-Rashid\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Al-Mutawakkil\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Al-Ma\'mun ar-Rashid (198–218 AH) made Mu\'tazilah the state religion and had Greek, Persian and Indian books translated into Arabic. This was later reversed by Al-Mutawakkil.', 'Mu\'tazilah was a rationalist theological school that dominated during Al-Ma\'mun\'s reign.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Al-Ma\'mun\\\",\\\"Mu\'tazilah\\\",\\\"Abbasid\\\",\\\"State Religion\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '8', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1170, '159d0529-fdcb-485d-93dc-a6f2386c30c6', 132, 3, 'Which Abbasid Caliph introduced Turkish slave-guards and made Samarra the new capital?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Harun ar-Rashid\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Al-Ma\'mun ar-Rashid\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Al-Mu\'tasim Billah\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Al-Mutawakkil\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Al-Mu\'tasim Billah (218–227 AH) introduced Turkish slave-guards into the army and moved the capital from Baghdad to Samarra.', 'These Turkish guards later became so powerful they controlled the caliphate.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Al-Mu\'tasim\\\",\\\"Turkish Guards\\\",\\\"Samarra\\\",\\\"Abbasid\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '8', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1171, 'cfaff899-99db-4a79-b985-575424038703', 132, 3, 'Who destroyed Baghdad and ended the Abbasid Caliphate in 656 AH?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Crusaders\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Seljuk Turks\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Mongols under Hulagu Khan\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Ottoman forces\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Hulagu Khan led the Mongol forces that destroyed Baghdad in 656 AH (1258 CE), killing hundreds of thousands and throwing the books of the House of Wisdom into the Tigris River.', 'The Tigris River reportedly turned black from the ink of thousands of books thrown into it.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Hulagu Khan\\\",\\\"Mongols\\\",\\\"Baghdad\\\",\\\"656 AH\\\",\\\"1258 CE\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '8', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1172, '6bdc01a6-802d-4ab8-a930-f66ea757dea5', 132, 3, 'What happened to the books of the House of Wisdom when Baghdad fell?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"They were taken to Persia\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"They were burned\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"They were thrown into the Tigris River\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"They were preserved by Mongols\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'When Hulagu Khan destroyed Baghdad, the books of the House of Wisdom were thrown into the Tigris River — it is said the water turned black from the ink.', 'This was one of history\'s greatest intellectual destructions.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"House of Wisdom\\\",\\\"Books\\\",\\\"Tigris\\\",\\\"Mongols\\\",\\\"1258\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '8', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1173, '4f88e25d-80bf-41ce-aac4-499c3730919d', 132, 3, 'The Abbasid Caliphate was descended from which companion of the Prophet ﷺ?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Ali bin Abi Talib\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Umar bin Khattab\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Abu Bakr as-Siddiq\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Abbasids were descendants of Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib, the uncle of the Prophet ﷺ.', 'Abbas was the Prophet\'s paternal uncle — the Abbasids used this lineage to legitimize their rule.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Abbasid\\\",\\\"Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib\\\",\\\"Lineage\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '8', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1174, '4fcf0875-0619-4f2c-be2d-965805fe311a', 132, 3, 'Who founded the Ottoman Empire?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Mehmed the Conqueror\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Suleiman the Magnificent\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Selim I\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Osman I (Osman Ghazi)\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'Osman I (Osman Ghazi) founded the Ottoman Empire in 699 AH (1299 CE). The empire is named after him.', 'Ottoman/Osmani comes from the name Osman (Uthman in Arabic).', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Osman I\\\",\\\"Ottoman\\\",\\\"Founder\\\",\\\"699 AH\\\",\\\"1299 CE\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '10', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1175, '76f193c0-396f-4940-b9fc-ed4be1b4f43a', 132, 3, 'Which Ottoman Sultan conquered Constantinople in 1453 CE?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Suleiman the Magnificent\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Selim I\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Abdul Hamid II\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Mehmed the Conqueror (Mehmed II)\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'Mehmed II (Mehmed the Conqueror) conquered Constantinople in 857 AH (1453 CE), fulfilling a prophecy of the Prophet ﷺ. He renamed it Istanbul.', 'The conquest ended the Byzantine Empire which had lasted over 1000 years.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Mehmed the Conqueror\\\",\\\"Constantinople\\\",\\\"1453 CE\\\",\\\"857 AH\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '10', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1176, 'b9badbf6-8dff-45b6-8438-65035609987f', 132, 3, 'Which Ottoman Sultan is known as \'The Magnificent\' and presided over the Ottoman Golden Age?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Mehmed II\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Selim I\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Suleiman I\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Abdul Hamid II\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Suleiman I (Suleiman the Magnificent) ruled for 48 years (926–974 AH) and presided over the Ottoman Golden Age — expanding into Europe, Asia, and Africa while establishing laws.', 'He is known in Europe as the Magnificent and in the Ottoman world as Kanuni (the Lawgiver).', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Suleiman the Magnificent\\\",\\\"Ottoman Golden Age\\\",\\\"Lawmaker\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '10', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1177, '1d3c5a4c-87c2-412a-88d7-b1631d818411', 132, 3, 'Which Ottoman Sultan transferred the Caliphate to Istanbul?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Osman I\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Mehmed the Conqueror\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Suleiman the Magnificent\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Selim I\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'Selim I (918–926 AH) conquered Egypt and transferred the title of Caliph from the Abbasid shadow caliphate in Cairo to Istanbul.', 'After conquering Egypt, Selim I became the custodian of the two Holy Mosques as well.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Selim I\\\",\\\"Caliphate\\\",\\\"Istanbul\\\",\\\"Egypt\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '10', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1178, '2a381456-5d01-4cbb-8444-a15bf3234a7e', 132, 3, 'How long did the Ottoman Caliphate last?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Around 300 years\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Around 450 years\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Around 643 years\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Around 900 years\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Ottoman Caliphate lasted approximately 643 years, from 699 AH (1299 CE) to 1342 AH (1924 CE).', 'It is the longest-lasting Islamic caliphate in history.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Ottoman\\\",\\\"Duration\\\",\\\"643 years\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '10', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1179, 'abd15c6a-7b4e-45be-8944-b9528baa8b6f', 132, 3, 'Over how many continents did the Ottoman Caliphate spread?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"One continent\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Two continents\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Three continents\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Four continents\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Ottoman Caliphate spread across three continents — Europe, Asia, and Africa — making it one of the largest empires in history.', 'At its peak, it controlled southeastern Europe, western Asia, and North Africa.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Ottoman\\\",\\\"Three Continents\\\",\\\"Europe\\\",\\\"Asia\\\",\\\"Africa\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '10', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1180, 'a2a79541-30c6-423b-9286-bad8cda326f2', 132, 3, 'Who was the last powerful Ottoman Caliph who struggled against colonial powers?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Suleiman the Magnificent\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Selim I\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Abdul Hamid II\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Mehmed VI\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Abdul Hamid II (1293–1327 AH) was the last powerful Ottoman Caliph who resisted European colonial powers and worked to unite Muslims globally.', 'He ruled for 34 years and was eventually deposed by the Young Turks movement.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Abdul Hamid II\\\",\\\"Last Powerful Caliph\\\",\\\"Colonial Powers\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '10', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1181, 'ffaaa1c5-bad0-4eab-9bb7-cdb91f906de7', 132, 3, 'Who was the last Ottoman Sultan?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Abdul Hamid II\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Selim III\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Mehmed V\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Mehmed VI (Wahid ad-Din)\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'Mehmed VI (Wahid ad-Din) was the last Ottoman Sultan, ruling from 1327–1341 AH before the caliphate was abolished.', 'After Mehmed VI, the title of Caliph briefly went to Abdul Majid II before full abolition.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Mehmed VI\\\",\\\"Last Ottoman Sultan\\\",\\\"Wahid ad-Din\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '10', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1182, '7bbad9c1-b4be-427d-b850-783fe0c551cd', 132, 3, 'When was the Ottoman Caliphate officially abolished?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"1918 CE\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"1920 CE\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"1922 CE\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"1924 CE\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'The Ottoman Caliphate was officially abolished on March 3, 1924 CE (1342 AH) by Mustafa Kemal Ataturk.', 'This date marks the end of the institution of Caliphate that had lasted over 1300 years.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Ottoman\\\",\\\"1924\\\",\\\"Abolished\\\",\\\"Ataturk\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '10', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1183, 'd31e8f1b-f877-4bb6-b4dd-71e1eff7040b', 132, 3, 'Who led the Khilafat Movement in the Indian Subcontinent?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Maulana Abul Kalam Azad\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Maulana Shaukat Ali\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Maulana Muhammad Ali Johar\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Maulana Mahmud al-Hasan\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Maulana Muhammad Ali Johar was the main leader of the Khilafat Movement (1919–1924) in the Indian Subcontinent.', 'He and his brother Shaukat Ali were the most prominent faces of the movement.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Khilafat Movement\\\",\\\"Muhammad Ali Johar\\\",\\\"Leader\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '11', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1184, '608d48c6-dd32-4225-8a10-dbb70bd0d707', 132, 3, 'When was the Khilafat Committee established and in which city?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"1918, Delhi\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"1919, Bombay\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"1920, Calcutta\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"1921, Lahore\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The Khilafat Committee was established in 1919 in Bombay to organize Muslims in support of the Ottoman Caliphate.', 'Bombay (now Mumbai) was a major center of Muslim political activity at the time.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Khilafat Committee\\\",\\\"1919\\\",\\\"Bombay\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '11', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1185, 'e6f801d4-8385-4398-8eb8-004a0190003c', 132, 3, 'What was the Hijrat Movement (1920) in the context of the Khilafat Movement?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Migration of Muslims to Turkey\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Migration to Afghanistan to escape British rule (failed)\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Migration to Arabia\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Migration to Makkah for Hajj\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The Hijrat Movement of 1920 was an attempt by Indian Muslims to migrate to Afghanistan to escape British rule, but it failed as Afghanistan could not absorb the large numbers.', 'Hijrat means migration — inspired by the Prophet\'s migration from Makkah to Medina.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Hijrat Movement\\\",\\\"1920\\\",\\\"Afghanistan\\\",\\\"Khilafat\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '11', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1186, '3e9cbc1b-1de1-4de5-89d4-d80a4bf6dd82', 132, 3, 'Which incident in 1922 caused Gandhi to withdraw from the Non-Cooperation Movement?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Jallianwala Bagh\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Lahore Resolution\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Chauri Chaura incident\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Simon Commission\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Chauri Chaura incident in 1922, where protestors burned a police station killing policemen, caused Gandhi to withdraw the Non-Cooperation Movement.', 'Gandhi opposed violence and withdrew the movement after this incident despite its momentum.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Chauri Chaura\\\",\\\"1922\\\",\\\"Gandhi\\\",\\\"Non-Cooperation\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '11', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1187, '9120ee52-ee6a-4f04-86da-7f91d9e22da1', 132, 3, 'Who abolished the Ottoman Caliphate in 1924?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Abdul Hamid II\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Enver Pasha\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Mustafa Kemal Ataturk\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Muhammad Ali Johar\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Mustafa Kemal Ataturk, the founder of modern Turkey, abolished the Ottoman Caliphate on March 3, 1924, ending over 1300 years of the institution.', 'Ataturk wanted to secularize Turkey and saw the Caliphate as an obstacle.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Ataturk\\\",\\\"Caliphate Abolished\\\",\\\"1924\\\",\\\"Ottoman\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '11', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1188, '960b3827-908c-4c30-aeb6-83cf0736ddfd', 132, 3, 'What role did Gandhi play in the Khilafat Movement?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"He led the movement\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"He opposed the movement\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"He participated to promote Hindu-Muslim unity\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"He had no role\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Gandhi participated in the Khilafat Movement to promote Hindu-Muslim unity, seeing it as an opportunity to build a joint front against British colonial rule.', 'This was one of the key moments of Hindu-Muslim cooperation in Indian independence history.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Gandhi\\\",\\\"Khilafat Movement\\\",\\\"Hindu-Muslim Unity\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '11', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1189, '2511305d-52cd-431c-a296-7406fd9536e2', 132, 3, 'The Battle of Nahrawan (38 AH) was fought between Ali (RA) and which group?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Mu\'awiyah\'s forces\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Byzantine forces\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Kharijites\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Persian rebels\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Battle of Nahrawan (38 AH) was fought between Ali (RA) and the Kharijites, who had emerged after the Battle of Siffin. The Kharijites were defeated.', 'Nahrawan is a location near Baghdad in Iraq.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Battle of Nahrawan\\\",\\\"Ali\\\",\\\"Kharijites\\\",\\\"38 AH\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '13', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1190, '91db739c-a5c8-4c1b-aafd-b519d653f3e5', 132, 3, 'In which year CE did Hulagu Khan destroy Baghdad?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"1099 CE\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"1187 CE\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"1258 CE\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"1453 CE\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Hulagu Khan (Mongol) destroyed Baghdad in 656 AH corresponding to 1258 CE, ending the Abbasid Caliphate.', 'This date is one of the most catastrophic events in Islamic history.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Baghdad\\\",\\\"Hulagu Khan\\\",\\\"1258 CE\\\",\\\"656 AH\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '13', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1191, 'b69196e8-7254-44de-b182-e4c9082bed17', 132, 3, 'Which Abbasid Caliph was killed when Baghdad fell to the Mongols?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Harun ar-Rashid\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Al-Ma\'mun ar-Rashid\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Al-Mu\'tasim Billah\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Al-Muqtadir\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Al-Musta\'sim Billah (640–656 AH) was the last Abbasid Caliph who was killed when Hulagu Khan destroyed Baghdad in 656 AH.', 'He was the 37th and last Abbasid Caliph in Baghdad.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Al-Musta\'sim\\\",\\\"Last Abbasid Caliph\\\",\\\"Baghdad\\\",\\\"Mongols\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '13', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1192, 'd96f8d3d-7bd5-4032-95ea-212efecbae23', 132, 3, 'The conquest of Constantinople in 1453 CE fulfilled what?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"A Quranic verse\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"A prophecy of the Prophet \\\\ufdfa\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"A dream of Osman I\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"A strategic Ottoman plan\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The conquest of Constantinople in 1453 CE by Mehmed the Conqueror fulfilled a famous prophecy of the Prophet ﷺ who praised the army and commander who would conquer it.', 'The Prophet praised this future conquest as a great achievement for Islam.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Constantinople\\\",\\\"1453\\\",\\\"Prophecy\\\",\\\"Mehmed\\\",\\\"Ottoman\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '13', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
(1193, '7c8ee01f-0540-48fe-b256-d24f63cf2969', 132, 3, 'The total number of Abbasid Caliphs was:', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"14\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"20\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"37\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"50\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Abbasid Caliphate had a total of 37 Caliphs ruling from 132 AH to 656 AH — a period of approximately 524 years.', 'Compare: Umayyads had 14 Caliphs; Ottomans had 36 Sultans/Caliphs.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Abbasid\\\",\\\"37 Caliphs\\\",\\\"Number\\\"]\"', 'Islamic Studies - Caliphate & Rulers', '8', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 11:33:04', '2026-04-30 11:33:04'),
