(1537, '0d7637cf-172d-48c7-b4eb-241b8425504f', 31, 1, 'On which national days is the national flag of Pakistan hoisted on government buildings?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Only on Independence Day\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Only on Defence Day\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"On Independence Day, Pakistan Day, and other national days\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Only on Quaid-e-Azam Day\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The national flag is hoisted on government buildings, educational institutions, and public places on national days such as Independence Day and Pakistan Day.', 'Flags are raised on all major national occasions, not just one.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"National Flag\\\",\\\"Independence Day\\\",\\\"Pakistan Day\\\",\\\"Hoisting\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1538, '791de053-ec63-4194-8ee1-201fb92196ba', 31, 1, 'What is the background (field) color of Pakistan\'s national flag?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"White\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Light green\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Dark green\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Blue\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The national flag of Pakistan has a dark green field (background) with a white vertical stripe on the left and a white crescent moon and star in the center of the green area.', 'Dark green, not light green — an important distinction.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"National Flag\\\",\\\"Dark Green\\\",\\\"Color\\\",\\\"Pakistan\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1539, 'f6470905-b20e-436b-8522-c92fba304114', 31, 1, 'Where is the crescent and star positioned on Pakistan\'s national flag?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"On the white stripe\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"In the top left corner\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"In the center of the green area\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"At the bottom of the flag\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The white crescent moon and five-pointed star are positioned in the center of the green area of Pakistan\'s national flag, not on the white stripe.', 'The symbols appear on the green part, not the white stripe.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"National Flag\\\",\\\"Crescent\\\",\\\"Star\\\",\\\"Position\\\",\\\"Pakistan\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1540, 'a992cd80-492d-4d0e-80c8-1a0b5ae66220', 31, 1, 'What is the official name of Pakistan\'s national anthem?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Pakistan Zindabad\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Sohni Dharti\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Qaumi Taranah\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Aye Watan\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Pakistan\'s national anthem is officially known as \'Qaumi Taranah\', which means \'National Song\' or \'National Anthem\' in Urdu.', 'Qaumi means national, Taranah means anthem or tune.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"National Anthem\\\",\\\"Qaumi Taranah\\\",\\\"Pakistan\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1541, 'c71573b0-4950-45bc-b842-f56b9ba70265', 31, 1, 'Who composed the music of Pakistan\'s national anthem?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Hafeez Jalandhari\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Syed Amir-uddin Kedwaii\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Faiz Ahmad Faiz\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Ahmad Ghulam Ali Chagla\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'The music of Pakistan\'s national anthem was composed by Ahmad Ghulam Ali Chagla in 1949. The lyrics were written separately by Hafeez Jalandhari.', 'The music composer and the lyricist are two different people.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"National Anthem\\\",\\\"Music\\\",\\\"Ahmad Ghulam Ali Chagla\\\",\\\"Composer\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1542, '7fd25a3a-93b8-4823-a7c2-2c6a2ac2712c', 31, 1, 'Who wrote the lyrics of Pakistan\'s national anthem?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Ahmad Ghulam Ali Chagla\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Muhammad Iqbal\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Hafeez Jalandhari\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Liaquat Ali Khan\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The lyrics (words) of Pakistan\'s national anthem were written by Hafeez Jalandhari. The music was composed by Ahmad Ghulam Ali Chagla in 1949.', 'The lyricist\'s last name starts with \'J\' — Jalandhari.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"National Anthem\\\",\\\"Lyrics\\\",\\\"Hafeez Jalandhari\\\",\\\"Pakistan\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1543, '00bc8521-aa79-4409-8924-532865dc0b46', 31, 1, 'In which year was Pakistan\'s national anthem officially adopted?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"1947\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"1949\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"1954\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"1956\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Pakistan\'s national anthem was officially adopted in 1954. The music was composed in 1949 but the anthem was formally adopted five years later.', 'Music composed in 1949, but officially adopted in 1954 — five years later.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"National Anthem\\\",\\\"Adopted\\\",\\\"1954\\\",\\\"Pakistan\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1544, '7c8cd564-aa7f-4a80-8c4e-bef09a45f19a', 31, 1, 'What is the primary language of Pakistan\'s national anthem?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Pure Urdu\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Arabic\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Persianized Urdu with many Persian and Arabic words\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Persian only\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The language of the national anthem is mainly Persianized Urdu — it contains many Persian and Arabic words, reflecting Pakistan\'s cultural and Islamic heritage.', 'It is not pure Urdu — it has a heavy Persian and Arabic influence.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"National Anthem\\\",\\\"Language\\\",\\\"Persianized Urdu\\\",\\\"Persian\\\",\\\"Arabic\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1545, '767c33fe-cdde-4e82-b7e2-b7692b109c5b', 31, 1, 'What ideals does Pakistan\'s national anthem highlight?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Democracy, equality, and freedom\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Unity, faith, and discipline\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Progress, prosperity, and peace\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Justice, courage, and loyalty\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Pakistan\'s national anthem highlights the ideals of unity, faith, and discipline — the same principles as the national motto given by Quaid-e-Azam Jinnah.', 'These three ideals are also found in the national motto.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"National Anthem\\\",\\\"Unity\\\",\\\"Faith\\\",\\\"Discipline\\\",\\\"Ideals\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1546, '7d360545-59ae-4fe9-a924-8464edeae746', 31, 1, 'What do citizens do when the national anthem is played to show respect?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Salute with their right hand\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Bow their heads\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Stand respectfully\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Sing along loudly\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Citizens stand respectfully when the national anthem is played to show their respect and loyalty to the country at official ceremonies and events.', 'The standard respectful gesture is to stand at attention.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"National Anthem\\\",\\\"Respect\\\",\\\"Stand\\\",\\\"Citizens\\\",\\\"Pakistan\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1547, '06b00b94-9308-4cea-953a-f0fe902dc480', 31, 1, 'On which occasions is Pakistan\'s national anthem played?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Only at cricket matches\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Important national occasions, official ceremonies, and international events\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Only in schools daily\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Only on Independence Day\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The national anthem is played on important national occasions, official ceremonies, and international events where Pakistan is represented.', 'It is played wherever Pakistan is officially represented or honored.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"National Anthem\\\",\\\"Occasions\\\",\\\"Ceremonies\\\",\\\"International Events\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1548, '5460954c-e42d-4abf-861f-344faff2ffc4', 31, 1, 'In which year was the music of Pakistan\'s national anthem composed?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"1947\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"1949\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"1952\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"1954\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The music of Pakistan\'s national anthem was composed by Ahmad Ghulam Ali Chagla in 1949, though the anthem was officially adopted later in 1954.', 'Music composed: 1949. Officially adopted: 1954. Two different years.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"National Anthem\\\",\\\"Music\\\",\\\"1949\\\",\\\"Ahmad Ghulam Ali Chagla\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1549, 'facc9e5a-7f71-49e6-8232-e5a5b3285a7c', 31, 1, 'In which year was Pakistan\'s national emblem officially adopted?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"1947\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"1949\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"1954\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"1956\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Pakistan\'s national emblem was officially adopted in 1954, the same year as the national anthem.', 'Both the national anthem and national emblem were adopted in the same year.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"National Emblem\\\",\\\"Adopted\\\",\\\"1954\\\",\\\"Pakistan\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1550, 'bfffc4fc-7449-4120-a877-d1752232b7c4', 31, 1, 'What is at the center of Pakistan\'s national emblem?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"A crescent and star\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"A floral wreath\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"A shield\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"A banner with the motto\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The center of Pakistan\'s national emblem consists of a shield surrounded by a floral wreath. The shield contains four sections representing major crops.', 'The shield is the central element, surrounded by the wreath.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"National Emblem\\\",\\\"Shield\\\",\\\"Center\\\",\\\"Pakistan\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1551, 'acb9ce64-2dcf-4dd4-b904-c05cc11ecc5a', 31, 1, 'Which four crops are represented in the shield of Pakistan\'s national emblem?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Wheat, rice, sugarcane, maize\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Cotton, wheat, tea, jute\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Rice, cotton, mango, dates\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Wheat, cotton, sugarcane, rice\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The shield in Pakistan\'s national emblem contains four sections representing the major agricultural crops: cotton, wheat, tea, and jute — reflecting agriculture\'s vital role in the economy.', 'The four crops are: cotton, wheat, tea, and jute — not rice or sugarcane.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"National Emblem\\\",\\\"Shield\\\",\\\"Crops\\\",\\\"Cotton\\\",\\\"Wheat\\\",\\\"Tea\\\",\\\"Jute\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1552, '05172d51-eec6-443a-aa3c-958a64fc2abe', 31, 1, 'What does the floral wreath around the shield in Pakistan\'s national emblem represent?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"The agricultural economy\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The Islamic heritage\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The cultural heritage of Pakistan\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"The four provinces\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The floral wreath surrounding the shield in Pakistan\'s national emblem represents the cultural heritage of Pakistan.', 'The wreath symbolizes culture, not agriculture (that is represented by the shield crops).', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"National Emblem\\\",\\\"Floral Wreath\\\",\\\"Cultural Heritage\\\",\\\"Pakistan\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1553, '5e7b0ba2-00ff-4e83-9bab-90b44ebad7fc', 31, 1, 'What is written on the banner at the bottom of Pakistan\'s national emblem?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Pakistan Zindabad\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"14 August 1947\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The national motto in Urdu script\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"The name of Pakistan\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'At the bottom of Pakistan\'s national emblem is a banner containing the national motto (Faith, Unity, Discipline / Iman, Ittehad, Nazm) written in Urdu script.', 'The banner carries the three-word motto of Pakistan.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"National Emblem\\\",\\\"Banner\\\",\\\"National Motto\\\",\\\"Urdu\\\",\\\"Pakistan\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1554, '8f40d5d3-3d1b-449e-8d95-64d80be32b77', 31, 1, 'What appears above the shield in Pakistan\'s national emblem?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"The name of Pakistan\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"A floral wreath\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"A crescent and star\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"An eagle\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Above the shield in Pakistan\'s national emblem is a crescent and star — traditional Islamic symbols representing light, progress, and guidance.', 'Islamic symbols crown the shield from above.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"National Emblem\\\",\\\"Crescent\\\",\\\"Star\\\",\\\"Islamic Symbols\\\",\\\"Pakistan\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1555, '8e05d118-4b34-4c5b-bf73-cb2bdc5f48b6', 31, 1, 'Why were cotton, wheat, tea, and jute chosen for Pakistan\'s national emblem shield?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"They are the most expensive crops\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Agriculture has historically played a vital role in Pakistan\'s economy\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"They are grown in all four provinces\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"They were Jinnah\'s favorite crops\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'These four crops were chosen because agriculture has historically played a vital role in Pakistan\'s economy, and these crops represent the agricultural foundation of the country.', 'The choice reflects the economic importance of farming in Pakistan.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"National Emblem\\\",\\\"Crops\\\",\\\"Agriculture\\\",\\\"Economy\\\",\\\"Pakistan\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1556, '62474c41-39d6-4f81-bbc1-4fd25a795ea3', 31, 1, 'What do the crescent and star above the shield in Pakistan\'s national emblem represent?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"The Muslim majority of Pakistan\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Light, progress, and guidance\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Independence and freedom\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Unity and discipline\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The crescent and star above the shield are traditional Islamic symbols representing light, progress, and guidance — the same symbolism as on the national flag.', 'These symbols carry consistent meaning across both the flag and the emblem.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"National Emblem\\\",\\\"Crescent\\\",\\\"Star\\\",\\\"Light\\\",\\\"Progress\\\",\\\"Guidance\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1557, 'c5c94c32-6652-440b-87d0-9e5a9ffbf05d', 31, 1, 'What is the national motto of Pakistan?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Unity, Faith, Democracy\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Iman, Ittehad, Nazm (Faith, Unity, Discipline)\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Peace, Justice, Progress\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Islam, Pakistan, Jinnah\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The national motto of Pakistan is \'Faith, Unity, Discipline\' — written in Urdu as \'Iman, Ittehad, Nazm\'. It was given by Muhammad Ali Jinnah, the founder of Pakistan.', 'Three words: Faith (Iman), Unity (Ittehad), Discipline (Nazm).', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"National Motto\\\",\\\"Faith\\\",\\\"Unity\\\",\\\"Discipline\\\",\\\"Iman\\\",\\\"Ittehad\\\",\\\"Nazm\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1558, '8b0ade93-3327-40e7-ad33-adbb79004be7', 31, 1, 'Who gave Pakistan its national motto \'Faith, Unity, Discipline\'?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Liaquat Ali Khan\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Allama Iqbal\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Hafeez Jalandhari\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Muhammad Ali Jinnah\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'The national motto \'Faith, Unity, Discipline\' (Iman, Ittehad, Nazm) was given by Muhammad Ali Jinnah, the founder of Pakistan, reflecting the core principles of the nation.', 'The founder of Pakistan gave the nation its guiding motto.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"National Motto\\\",\\\"Jinnah\\\",\\\"Founder\\\",\\\"Pakistan\\\",\\\"Faith Unity Discipline\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1559, '50f8150a-3562-41e3-95e0-74d7bc55f9c0', 31, 1, 'What does \'Ittehad\' mean in Pakistan\'s national motto?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Faith\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Discipline\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Unity\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Progress\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'In Pakistan\'s national motto \'Iman, Ittehad, Nazm\', Ittehad means Unity — emphasizing national solidarity among people of different regions, languages, and cultures.', 'Iman=Faith, Ittehad=Unity, Nazm=Discipline — remember the order.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"National Motto\\\",\\\"Ittehad\\\",\\\"Unity\\\",\\\"Pakistan\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1560, '05e90d39-b4b7-46b4-a182-93c71c7959dd', 31, 1, 'What does \'Faith\' (Iman) refer to in Pakistan\'s national motto?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Only religious worship\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Strong belief in Allah and confidence in the country\'s ideals and future\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Only political loyalty\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Obedience to the government\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'In the national motto, Faith (Iman) refers to strong belief in Allah and confidence in the country\'s ideals and future — both spiritual and national confidence.', 'Faith here has both a religious and a national dimension.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"National Motto\\\",\\\"Iman\\\",\\\"Faith\\\",\\\"Allah\\\",\\\"Pakistan\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1561, '2cab5ef5-1545-4c23-8cbe-9e56222a0740', 31, 1, 'What does \'Discipline\' (Nazm) emphasize in Pakistan\'s national motto?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Military training and strength\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Order, responsibility, and commitment in building a strong nation\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Following religious rituals strictly\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Academic excellence only\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Discipline (Nazm) in Pakistan\'s national motto highlights the need for order, responsibility, and commitment in building a strong and successful nation.', 'Discipline is about national responsibility and organized conduct.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"National Motto\\\",\\\"Nazm\\\",\\\"Discipline\\\",\\\"Order\\\",\\\"Responsibility\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1562, 'aa6e97a4-c13c-40a0-b28b-bfb9f06a00cf', 31, 1, 'What is the Urdu equivalent of \'Discipline\' in Pakistan\'s national motto?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Iman\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Ittehad\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Nazm\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Watan\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Urdu word for Discipline in Pakistan\'s national motto is \'Nazm\'. The full motto in Urdu is: Iman (Faith), Ittehad (Unity), Nazm (Discipline).', 'Remember the three Urdu words: Iman, Ittehad, Nazm — in order.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"National Motto\\\",\\\"Nazm\\\",\\\"Discipline\\\",\\\"Urdu\\\",\\\"Pakistan\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1563, '59704917-83e5-4527-bb5e-8d9c7a083cc0', 31, 1, 'On which date is Pakistan\'s Independence Day celebrated?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"23 March\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"6 September\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"25 December\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"14 August\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'Pakistan\'s Independence Day is celebrated on 14 August each year, commemorating Pakistan\'s emergence as an independent state in 1947 after the end of British colonial rule.', 'This is Pakistan\'s birthday — 14th August 1947.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Independence Day\\\",\\\"14 August\\\",\\\"Pakistan\\\",\\\"1947\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1564, 'b5419dfb-1783-4fe3-bc07-eb6b34e9fa7f', 31, 1, 'What historical event does Pakistan Day (23 March) commemorate?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Pakistan\'s independence from Britain\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The birth of Quaid-e-Azam\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The Lahore Resolution of 1940\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Defence of Pakistan in 1965\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Pakistan Day on 23 March commemorates the historic Lahore Resolution passed in 1940, which demanded a separate homeland for the Muslims of the Indian subcontinent.', 'This resolution set the direction for the creation of Pakistan.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Pakistan Day\\\",\\\"23 March\\\",\\\"Lahore Resolution\\\",\\\"1940\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1565, '5cddf416-2473-4870-b720-31b21c0f974e', 31, 1, 'In which year was the Lahore Resolution passed?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"1930\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"1935\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"1940\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"1945\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Lahore Resolution was passed in 1940 at the annual session of the All India Muslim League in Lahore. It demanded a separate Muslim state, later becoming Pakistan.', 'The resolution was passed seven years before Pakistan\'s actual independence.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Lahore Resolution\\\",\\\"1940\\\",\\\"Pakistan Day\\\",\\\"23 March\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1566, 'c2dd8e7f-189c-4a8d-9f60-6239452757ed', 31, 1, 'What does Defence Day (6 September) commemorate?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"The Lahore Resolution of 1940\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The creation of Pakistan in 1947\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The bravery of Pakistani armed forces in the 1965 war with India\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"The birth of Quaid-e-Azam\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Defence Day on 6 September commemorates the bravery and sacrifices of Pakistan\'s armed forces during the Indo-Pakistan War of 1965.', '6 September = Defence Day = 1965 war with India.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Defence Day\\\",\\\"6 September\\\",\\\"1965 War\\\",\\\"Armed Forces\\\",\\\"Pakistan\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1567, 'c1be3b76-5d1b-49c6-8a90-b76ed53a2d69', 31, 1, 'On which date is Quaid-e-Azam Day celebrated?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"9 November\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"23 March\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"6 September\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"25 December\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'Quaid-e-Azam Day is celebrated on 25 December each year, marking the birth anniversary of Muhammad Ali Jinnah, the founder of Pakistan.', '25 December is the birthday of the founder of Pakistan.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Quaid-e-Azam Day\\\",\\\"25 December\\\",\\\"Jinnah\\\",\\\"Birth Anniversary\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1568, 'badee149-c7f4-43f6-9363-401bc2ae0b6c', 31, 1, 'On which date is Iqbal Day observed in Pakistan?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"25 December\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"23 March\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"9 November\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"14 August\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Iqbal Day is observed on 9 November to honor Muhammad Iqbal, the national poet and philosopher who inspired the idea of a separate Muslim state in South Asia.', 'Remember: Iqbal Day = 9 November; Quaid Day = 25 December.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Iqbal Day\\\",\\\"9 November\\\",\\\"Muhammad Iqbal\\\",\\\"Pakistan\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1569, '7098d61d-0a33-4743-9588-ead3163ed6b7', 31, 1, 'Who is Muhammad Iqbal and why is Iqbal Day observed?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"A military general who won the 1965 war\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The founder of Pakistan who created the state\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The national poet and philosopher who inspired the idea of a separate Muslim state\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"The composer of the national anthem\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Muhammad Iqbal was Pakistan\'s national poet and philosopher whose ideas inspired the concept of a separate Muslim state (Pakistan) in South Asia. Iqbal Day honors his contributions.', 'Iqbal provided the philosophical foundation for Pakistan\'s creation.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Muhammad Iqbal\\\",\\\"National Poet\\\",\\\"Philosopher\\\",\\\"Iqbal Day\\\",\\\"Pakistan Movement\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1570, '98c4032a-c1f9-4578-be2a-b6046e5f78ce', 31, 1, 'How is Independence Day celebrated in Pakistan?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Only with military parades\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"With flag hoisting, parades, national songs, cultural programs, and decorations\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Only with government speeches\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Only with lighting of buildings\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Independence Day is celebrated with flag hoisting ceremonies, parades, national songs, and cultural programs. Government buildings and streets are decorated with national flags and lights.', 'It is a full national celebration combining military, cultural, and civic events.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Independence Day\\\",\\\"Celebration\\\",\\\"Flag Hoisting\\\",\\\"Parade\\\",\\\"Pakistan\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1571, '3520a19c-f96e-4cb0-b065-ad8f4ec9d66f', 31, 1, 'Which war does Defence Day (6 September) honor Pakistan\'s armed forces for?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"The 1971 war\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The 1948 Kashmir war\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The Indo-Pakistan War of 1965\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"World War II\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Defence Day on 6 September specifically honors the bravery of Pakistan\'s armed forces during the Indo-Pakistan War of 1965, when they defended the country.', '6 September 1965 is when India launched attacks — Pakistan celebrated its defence.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Defence Day\\\",\\\"1965 War\\\",\\\"Indo-Pakistan War\\\",\\\"Armed Forces\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1572, 'cb441510-188d-41e3-b72d-9aed4f1bcf14', 31, 1, 'How is Pakistan Day (23 March) observed?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"With fireworks and concerts only\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"With military parades, national ceremonies, and speeches on unity and national strength\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Only with flag hoisting at schools\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Only with government holidays\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Pakistan Day is celebrated with military parades, national ceremonies, and speeches that highlight the importance of unity and national strength.', 'Military parades are the most visible feature of Pakistan Day celebrations.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Pakistan Day\\\",\\\"23 March\\\",\\\"Military Parade\\\",\\\"Ceremony\\\",\\\"Pakistan\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1573, 'f77c5970-488b-443a-a852-4e92a64ac3a4', 31, 1, 'What is the purpose of national holidays in Pakistan?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Only to give citizens a day off work\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"To commemorate historical events, honor national leaders, and encourage patriotism and national unity\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Only for military demonstrations\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Only for international guests\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'National holidays and days of significance remind citizens of sacrifices made for the country and encourage patriotism and national unity by commemorating important historical events.', 'Beyond rest, these days carry deeper historical and patriotic meaning.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"National Holidays\\\",\\\"Patriotism\\\",\\\"Historical Events\\\",\\\"Pakistan\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1574, '4e483231-a74a-4f9f-8ea0-1386ed99370c', 31, 1, 'How is Quaid-e-Azam Day observed across Pakistan?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"With military parades only\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Paying tribute to Jinnah\'s leadership, vision, and struggle through events at institutions and public organizations\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Only with a national holiday\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"With sports competitions\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Quaid-e-Azam Day is observed by paying tribute to Muhammad Ali Jinnah\'s leadership, vision, and struggle for Pakistan\'s creation through events at educational institutions and government offices.', 'It is primarily a day of remembrance and tribute, not major public events.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Quaid-e-Azam Day\\\",\\\"Jinnah\\\",\\\"Tribute\\\",\\\"Leadership\\\",\\\"Pakistan\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1575, '11460946-064f-435b-af55-4d268c2e0477', 31, 1, 'How is Iqbal Day celebrated in Pakistan?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Military parades and flag hoisting\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Seminars, poetry recitations, and educational programs about Iqbal\'s philosophy\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Fireworks and street festivals\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Only with a public holiday\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Iqbal Day is celebrated through seminars, poetry recitations, and educational programs that highlight Allama Iqbal\'s philosophical ideas and his contributions to the Pakistan Movement.', 'Iqbal was a poet-philosopher, so his day is marked with intellectual and cultural events.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Iqbal Day\\\",\\\"Seminars\\\",\\\"Poetry\\\",\\\"Philosophy\\\",\\\"Muhammad Iqbal\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1576, 'e5ab09d4-b88e-4650-a9cb-ed1dd8d6e408', 31, 1, 'Which national day specifically honors the role of Pakistan\'s armed forces?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Independence Day\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Pakistan Day\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Iqbal Day\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Defence Day\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'Defence Day (6 September) specifically honors the bravery and sacrifices of Pakistan\'s armed forces during the 1965 war and recognizes the courage of the Pakistani people.', 'The very name \'Defence Day\' indicates it is about military service.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Defence Day\\\",\\\"Armed Forces\\\",\\\"Military\\\",\\\"6 September\\\",\\\"Pakistan\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1577, '4f6183c1-5c54-4a8f-bc8e-f9f49b04acf4', 31, 1, 'What did the Lahore Resolution of 1940 demand?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Independence from British rule immediately\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"A federal democratic Pakistan\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"A separate homeland for Muslims of the subcontinent\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Military alliance with Muslim countries\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The historic Lahore Resolution of 1940 demanded a separate homeland for the Muslims of the Indian subcontinent — the resolution that ultimately led to the creation of Pakistan.', 'This resolution formally articulated the demand for Pakistan as a separate state.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Lahore Resolution\\\",\\\"1940\\\",\\\"Separate Homeland\\\",\\\"Muslims\\\",\\\"Pakistan\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1578, '3be8609f-84c0-493e-9c11-86cab8699cc9', 31, 1, 'Which personality is commemorated on 9 November in Pakistan?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Muhammad Ali Jinnah\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Liaquat Ali Khan\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Muhammad Iqbal\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Sir Syed Ahmad Khan\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '9 November is Iqbal Day, observed to honor Muhammad Iqbal — Pakistan\'s national poet and philosopher who inspired the idea of a separate Muslim state.', '9 November is the birth anniversary of Allama Muhammad Iqbal.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Iqbal Day\\\",\\\"9 November\\\",\\\"Muhammad Iqbal\\\",\\\"National Poet\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1579, 'b3de75ed-2ad5-4b0c-83e8-304bba84ca44', 31, 1, 'What makes national symbols important for a country like Pakistan?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"They make the country look good to foreigners only\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"They represent identity, history, culture, and values, creating unity, patriotism, and pride among citizens\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"They are only important for government use\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"They are required for international trade agreements\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'National symbols represent the identity, history, culture, and values of a nation. They create a sense of unity, patriotism, and pride among citizens — binding them to a shared identity.', 'Symbols serve a deeper social and psychological purpose for national unity.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"National Symbols\\\",\\\"Identity\\\",\\\"Unity\\\",\\\"Patriotism\\\",\\\"Pakistan\\\"]\"', 'National Symbols of Pakistan - General Knowledge', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:04:33', '2026-04-30 20:04:33'),
(1580, '2a3e69f6-db44-4733-abda-c2948349630e', 32, 1, 'In which city was Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) born?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Medina\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Jerusalem\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Mecca\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Taif\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) was born in the city of Mecca in the Arabian Peninsula in the year 570 CE.', 'The city that is home to the Kaaba — the holiest site in Islam.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\",\\\"Birth\\\",\\\"Mecca\\\",\\\"Arabian Peninsula\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1581, 'fc77287e-79b0-40e6-8e3e-03ba22f958fa', 32, 1, 'In which year was Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) born?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"610 CE\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"622 CE\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"570 CE\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"580 CE\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) was born in 570 CE in Mecca. This year is also known as the Year of the Elephant.', 'Born in 570 CE — 40 years before receiving prophethood in 610 CE.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\",\\\"Birth\\\",\\\"570 CE\\\",\\\"Year of Elephant\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1582, '65ba57d6-3c87-459b-b91d-322bf97da7f6', 32, 1, 'Why is the year of the Prophet\'s birth called the \'Year of the Elephant\'?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Because elephants were common in Mecca that year\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Because a powerful army led by Abraha attempted to attack the Kaaba using elephants\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Because the Prophet was born near an elephant caravan\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Because Abraha gifted elephants to the Quraysh\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The year 570 CE is called the Year of the Elephant because Abraha\'s army, which included war elephants, marched toward Mecca to destroy the Kaaba but was miraculously stopped by Allah.', 'Surah Al-Fil in the Quran refers to this event.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Year of Elephant\\\",\\\"Abraha\\\",\\\"Kaaba\\\",\\\"570 CE\\\",\\\"Mecca\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1583, 'f2343190-0206-4120-a11f-92bb8daf6db5', 32, 1, 'What was the name of the Prophet\'s father?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Abu Talib\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Abd al-Muttalib\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Abdullah ibn Abd al-Muttalib\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Uthman ibn Affan\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Prophet\'s father was Abdullah ibn Abd al-Muttalib, who passed away before the Prophet was born, making the Prophet an orphan from birth.', 'His father died before his birth — that is why the Prophet was born an orphan.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\",\\\"Father\\\",\\\"Abdullah\\\",\\\"Orphan\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1584, 'ae27a5b4-0cff-4592-a754-fd365fad4a8b', 32, 1, 'What was the name of the Prophet\'s mother?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Khadija bint Khuwaylid\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Halima Saadia\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Fatimah bint Asad\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Aminah bint Wahb\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'The Prophet\'s mother was Aminah bint Wahb. She passed away when the Prophet was only six years old during a journey.', 'She died when the Prophet was six, leaving him an orphan for the second time.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\",\\\"Mother\\\",\\\"Aminah bint Wahb\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1585, '2f142d43-256c-4259-8bb5-dadd750554b5', 32, 1, 'Who was the wet nurse (foster mother) of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH)?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Umm Ayman\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Aminah bint Wahb\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Halima bint Abi Dhuayb (Halima Saadia)\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Fatimah bint Asad\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) was cared for by Halima bint Abi Dhuayb, also known as Halima Saadia, who belonged to the tribe of Banu Saad and raised him in the desert.', 'She is also called Halima Saadia — her tribe was Banu Saad.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Halima Saadia\\\",\\\"Wet Nurse\\\",\\\"Foster Mother\\\",\\\"Banu Saad\\\",\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1586, '3c39f65e-5d25-4dd7-810b-5124cd712ef0', 32, 1, 'Why were Arab infants sent to the desert to be raised?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Because the desert air was considered spiritually pure\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"To be raised in a healthier environment away from city diseases\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"To learn survival skills\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Because it was a religious obligation\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'According to Arab custom of the time, infants were sent to the desert to be raised in a healthier environment, away from the diseases and pollution of crowded cities.', 'This was a social custom for upper-class Arab families in Mecca.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Arab Custom\\\",\\\"Desert\\\",\\\"Infants\\\",\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\",\\\"Early Life\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1587, '883068b4-8294-4658-9ea5-9d901f302c03', 32, 1, 'At what age did the Prophet\'s mother Aminah pass away?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"When the Prophet was 2 years old\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"When the Prophet was 4 years old\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"When the Prophet was 6 years old\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"When the Prophet was 8 years old\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Prophet\'s mother Aminah bint Wahb passed away when Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) was six years old, during a journey, leaving him without both parents.', 'Six years old — he had already lost his father before birth.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Aminah\\\",\\\"Death\\\",\\\"Six Years Old\\\",\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1588, 'f9c7ebdb-d860-4da3-8282-a35af46be310', 32, 1, 'Who took care of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) after his mother\'s death?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"His uncle Abu Talib\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"His foster mother Halima\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"His grandfather Abd al-Muttalib\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Khadija bint Khuwaylid\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'After Aminah\'s death, the Prophet\'s grandfather Abd al-Muttalib took responsibility for raising him. Two years later, after his grandfather\'s death, his uncle Abu Talib took over.', 'First the grandfather, then after 2 years, uncle Abu Talib.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Abd al-Muttalib\\\",\\\"Grandfather\\\",\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\",\\\"Guardian\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1589, '6774d7ff-82e6-41ec-87fa-01ac5f6e222e', 32, 1, 'Who was the Prophet\'s uncle who supported and protected him for many years?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Abu Sufyan\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Hamzah\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Abbas\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Abu Talib\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'After his grandfather Abd al-Muttalib died, the Prophet was cared for by his uncle Abu Talib, who supported and protected him for many years throughout his prophethood.', 'Abu Talib remained the Prophet\'s protector in Mecca despite not accepting Islam.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Abu Talib\\\",\\\"Uncle\\\",\\\"Guardian\\\",\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\",\\\"Protection\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1590, '6d146bb0-c56d-478d-9b37-0c0e6b3ca601', 32, 1, 'What title was given to Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) by the people of Mecca for his honesty?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Al-Mustafa\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Al-Habib\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Al-Amin\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"As-Sadiq\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Because of his exceptional honesty and trustworthy character, the people of Mecca gave the Prophet the title \'Al-Amin\', which means \'the trustworthy\'.', 'Al-Amin means \'the trustworthy\' — earned before prophethood.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Al-Amin\\\",\\\"Trustworthy\\\",\\\"Mecca\\\",\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\",\\\"Title\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1591, '58e50f01-a5fd-41d2-ac1c-fe745ebce6a6', 32, 1, 'At what age did Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) marry Khadija bint Khuwaylid?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"20 years\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"25 years\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"30 years\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"35 years\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) married Khadija bint Khuwaylid at the age of twenty-five. She was a respected and wealthy businesswoman of Mecca who supported him throughout his mission.', '25 years old — 15 years before prophethood at age 40.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Khadija\\\",\\\"Marriage\\\",\\\"25 Years\\\",\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1592, 'fb849dda-ea99-4e9b-bbae-fb27b38a517f', 32, 1, 'What was Khadija bint Khuwaylid known for before her marriage to the Prophet?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Being the daughter of a tribal chief\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Being a teacher of the Quran\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Being a respected and wealthy businesswoman of Mecca\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Being a famous poet\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Khadija bint Khuwaylid was a respected and wealthy businesswoman of Mecca before her marriage to the Prophet. The Prophet had worked as a trader for her caravan.', 'She was an independent, successful merchant — one of the most respected women in Mecca.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Khadija\\\",\\\"Businesswoman\\\",\\\"Mecca\\\",\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\",\\\"Marriage\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1593, '4bd06e61-d553-4f48-bd44-8ed08a0ef7e0', 32, 1, 'In which cave did Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) used to meditate before receiving prophethood?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Cave of Thawr\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Cave of Hira\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Cave of Uhud\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Cave of Badr\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Before receiving prophethood, Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) often spent time in deep reflection and worship in the Cave of Hira, located in the mountains near Mecca.', 'Hira is the mountain cave where the first revelation came.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Cave of Hira\\\",\\\"Meditation\\\",\\\"Prophethood\\\",\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1594, '79e0263a-a3aa-42e6-8ec6-62b83b19092f', 32, 1, 'At what age did Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) receive his first revelation?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"30 years\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"35 years\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"40 years\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"45 years\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) received his first revelation from Allah at the age of forty, in the year 610 CE, while meditating in the Cave of Hira.', '40 years old in 610 CE — born in 570 CE.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"First Revelation\\\",\\\"40 Years\\\",\\\"610 CE\\\",\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\",\\\"Prophethood\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1595, '08574be1-e0e9-469e-bfc5-959dfb22272d', 32, 1, 'Through which angel did Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) receive the first revelation?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Israfil\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Mikail\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Azrail\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Jibril (Gabriel)\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'The first revelation was brought to Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) by the angel Jibril (Gabriel), who commanded him to read in the name of Allah.', 'Jibril is the angel of revelation in Islam — also known as Gabriel in other religions.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Jibril\\\",\\\"Gabriel\\\",\\\"Angel\\\",\\\"First Revelation\\\",\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1596, '14b154ee-4013-48b7-974d-53a22453be3b', 32, 1, 'What were the first revealed words commanded in the first revelation to the Prophet?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Pray in the name of Allah\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Read in the name of Allah\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Worship Allah alone\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Warn your people\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The first revealed words commanded the Prophet to \'Read in the name of Allah\' (Iqra bismi Rabbik). These opening verses are from Surah Al-Alaq.', 'Iqra means \'Read\' or \'Recite\' — the first word of the Quran\'s revelation.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"First Revelation\\\",\\\"Iqra\\\",\\\"Read\\\",\\\"Surah Al-Alaq\\\",\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1597, '72270a8d-74fa-4a55-bac9-ce2ac3367b15', 32, 1, 'In which year did the Prophet receive his first revelation?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"570 CE\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"600 CE\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"610 CE\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"622 CE\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) received his first revelation in 610 CE at the age of forty while meditating in the Cave of Hira near Mecca.', 'Born 570 CE + 40 years = 610 CE first revelation.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"First Revelation\\\",\\\"610 CE\\\",\\\"Prophethood\\\",\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00');
INSERT INTO `mcqs` (`id`, `uuid`, `topic_id`, `subject_id`, `question`, `question_type`, `options`, `correct_answers`, `explanation`, `hint`, `difficulty_level`, `time_limit_seconds`, `marks`, `negative_marks`, `tags`, `reference_book`, `reference_page`, `is_premium`, `is_verified`, `status`, `created_by`, `approved_by`, `approved_at`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(1598, 'b8e7789e-65cf-43f3-bcfd-63916d7c3b8c', 32, 1, 'What was the main message that Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) preached?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"To follow the Quraysh tribe\'s traditions\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"To worship one God (Allah) and abandon idol worship\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"To establish a new political empire\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"To promote Arab nationalism\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The Prophet preached the worship of one God (Allah), abandonment of idol worship, and emphasized justice, honesty, kindness to the poor, and equality among people.', 'Tawheed (monotheism) was the core message — worship only Allah.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\",\\\"Preaching\\\",\\\"Monotheism\\\",\\\"Allah\\\",\\\"Islam\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1599, 'fdc00c96-53d7-41bf-8397-58cf7c955f19', 32, 1, 'Which tribe was the main opponent of the Prophet\'s message in Mecca?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Banu Saad\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Banu Hashim\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Quraysh\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Banu Nadir\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The leaders of the Quraysh tribe were the main opponents who persecuted the early Muslims and tried to stop the spread of Islam, as the Prophet\'s message challenged their beliefs.', 'The Quraysh were the ruling tribe of Mecca and guardians of the Kaaba.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Quraysh\\\",\\\"Opposition\\\",\\\"Mecca\\\",\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\",\\\"Persecution\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1600, 'f26b2c41-8354-4e4a-9c97-c31178237cbc', 32, 1, 'Why did many people in Mecca oppose the Prophet\'s message?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Because they preferred other prophets\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Because his message challenged their traditional beliefs and idol worship practices\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Because he was an orphan with no status\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Because he was too young\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Many Meccans opposed the Prophet because his message challenged their traditional beliefs and the practice of idol worship, which was central to their way of life and economy.', 'Idol worship was deeply embedded in Meccan culture and their economic interests (pilgrims).', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Opposition\\\",\\\"Mecca\\\",\\\"Idol Worship\\\",\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\",\\\"Quraysh\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1601, 'f1803be0-c039-4720-a3e1-16ed04718c30', 32, 1, 'What qualities did Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) demonstrate while facing persecution in Mecca?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Anger and military force\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Withdrawal and silence\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Patience and determination\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Negotiation and compromise\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Despite severe persecution from the Quraysh, Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) continued preaching with patience and determination, never abandoning his mission.', 'Patience (Sabr) is one of the most emphasized qualities of the Prophet.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\",\\\"Patience\\\",\\\"Determination\\\",\\\"Persecution\\\",\\\"Mecca\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1602, '550560e7-b94d-40ca-8319-aabf417a8a72', 32, 1, 'What is the Hijra?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"The first revelation of the Quran\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The Prophet\'s migration from Mecca to Medina\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The conquest of Mecca\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"The Battle of Badr\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The Hijra refers to the Prophet\'s migration from Mecca to Medina in 622 CE. It marks a major turning point in Islamic history and is the starting point of the Islamic calendar.', 'Hijra means migration — from Hijra comes the Hijri calendar.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Hijra\\\",\\\"Migration\\\",\\\"Mecca\\\",\\\"Medina\\\",\\\"622 CE\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1603, '80906c00-b43c-4794-af22-d6a7e010a6c8', 32, 1, 'In which year did the Hijra (migration to Medina) take place?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"610 CE\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"618 CE\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"622 CE\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"630 CE\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Hijra took place in 622 CE, when Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) migrated from Mecca to Medina. This year became the starting point of the Islamic (Hijri) calendar.', '622 CE is year 1 of the Hijri (Islamic) calendar.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Hijra\\\",\\\"622 CE\\\",\\\"Islamic Calendar\\\",\\\"Migration\\\",\\\"Medina\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1604, 'ed166fa0-c4b0-4045-afcd-5f99967057b7', 32, 1, 'Who accompanied Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) during the Hijra to Medina?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Ali ibn Abi Talib\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Umar ibn al-Khattab\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Abu Bakr\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Uthman ibn Affan\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) was accompanied by his close companion Abu Bakr during the migration to Medina. Together they hid in the Cave of Thawr to avoid the Quraysh.', 'Abu Bakr was the Prophet\'s closest companion and companion of the Hijra.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Abu Bakr\\\",\\\"Hijra\\\",\\\"Migration\\\",\\\"Companion\\\",\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1605, 'c74757f7-a507-44bb-8c4a-a8c27af9fb9a', 32, 1, 'What does the Hijra mark in Islamic history?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"The end of revelation\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The first battle of Islam\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"A turning point and the starting point of the Islamic calendar\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"The death of the Prophet\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Hijra marks a major turning point in Islamic history and is also used as the starting point of the Islamic (Hijri) calendar — year 1 AH begins from this migration.', 'All Islamic dates are calculated from this event.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Hijra\\\",\\\"Islamic Calendar\\\",\\\"Turning Point\\\",\\\"622 CE\\\",\\\"History\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1606, '420271d1-aae1-4964-923e-0fc8ad4cbc0e', 32, 1, 'What important structure did the Prophet build first upon arriving in Medina?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"The Kaaba\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Al-Masjid al-Haram\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Al-Masjid an-Nabawi\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"The Prophet\'s palace\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Upon arriving in Medina, the Prophet built Al-Masjid an-Nabawi (the Prophet\'s Mosque), which became the center of religious, political, and social life for the Muslim community.', 'The Prophet\'s Mosque in Medina is the second holiest mosque in Islam.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Al-Masjid an-Nabawi\\\",\\\"Mosque\\\",\\\"Medina\\\",\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\",\\\"Construction\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1607, '673ce9ea-2b5b-4515-a5bc-9e7b533fd8ee', 32, 1, 'What was the Constitution of Medina?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"A military alliance against the Quraysh\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"A religious charter for Muslims only\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"An agreement establishing peaceful relations among Muslims, Jews, and other communities in Medina\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"A treaty with the Byzantine Empire\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Constitution of Medina was a landmark agreement created by the Prophet that established peaceful relations and rights among Muslims, Jews, and other communities living in Medina.', 'It is considered one of the earliest constitutional documents in history.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Constitution of Medina\\\",\\\"Agreement\\\",\\\"Muslims\\\",\\\"Jews\\\",\\\"Communities\\\",\\\"Medina\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1608, '0ad08fb2-ecc2-4e92-967a-1ef35a50616c', 32, 1, 'What type of community did the Prophet establish in Medina?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"A purely military state\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"A tribal confederation\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"A Muslim community based on justice, brotherhood, and cooperation\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"A monarchy under the Prophet\'s family\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'In Medina, the Prophet established the first Muslim community based on the principles of justice, brotherhood, and cooperation among all its members.', 'This community model later became the foundation of Islamic governance.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Muslim Community\\\",\\\"Medina\\\",\\\"Justice\\\",\\\"Brotherhood\\\",\\\"Cooperation\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1609, 'd13ec6df-fe6a-4655-88dd-9a613753309f', 32, 1, 'Why did the Quraysh try to capture the Prophet during the Hijra?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Because he owed them money\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Because he had taken their property\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Because they wanted to stop the migration and eliminate the Muslim leader\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Because he had insulted their gods publicly\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Quraysh plotted to capture and kill the Prophet during the Hijra to prevent the establishment of a Muslim community in Medina that could challenge their power.', 'They planned to kill him before he could safely reach Medina.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Quraysh\\\",\\\"Capture\\\",\\\"Hijra\\\",\\\"Plot\\\",\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1610, '1a1e81d3-b019-44f2-94a6-4f50ee0451f1', 32, 1, 'Which principle did the Constitution of Medina establish among different communities?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Muslim supremacy over all other groups\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Peaceful relations and rights for Muslims, Jews, and other communities\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Mandatory conversion to Islam\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Military conscription for all residents\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The Constitution of Medina established peaceful relations and defined the rights and responsibilities of Muslims, Jews, and other communities living in Medina under one agreement.', 'It was an inclusive document — not just for Muslims.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Constitution of Medina\\\",\\\"Peaceful Relations\\\",\\\"Rights\\\",\\\"Jews\\\",\\\"Muslims\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1611, 'eb4e8196-1ee6-4ee7-be96-28f03990a648', 32, 1, 'In which year was the Battle of Badr fought?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"622 CE\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"623 CE\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"624 CE\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"625 CE\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Battle of Badr was fought in 624 CE. It was one of the first major battles between the small Muslim army and the larger Quraysh forces, resulting in a significant Muslim victory.', 'Badr = 624 CE; Uhud = 625 CE; Trench = 627 CE — remember the sequence.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Battle of Badr\\\",\\\"624 CE\\\",\\\"Quraysh\\\",\\\"Muslim Victory\\\",\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1612, '51689cfd-ff6e-4a6d-a176-19b9b574b130', 32, 1, 'What was the outcome of the Battle of Badr?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"The Muslims were defeated\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The battle ended in a truce\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The Muslims achieved a significant victory despite having a small army\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Both sides suffered equal losses\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Despite having a significantly smaller army, the Muslims achieved a major victory at the Battle of Badr in 624 CE. This victory strengthened the early Muslim community.', 'A small force defeating a larger one — a defining victory for early Islam.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Battle of Badr\\\",\\\"Victory\\\",\\\"Muslims\\\",\\\"Quraysh\\\",\\\"624 CE\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1613, 'e80c5fe3-1b35-41dd-97fa-f7e488878762', 32, 1, 'Why did Muslims suffer heavy losses at the Battle of Uhud?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Because they had fewer weapons\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Because enemy forces were too large\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Because some soldiers disobeyed the Prophet\'s instructions\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Because the Prophet was absent\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'At the Battle of Uhud (625 CE), the Muslims faced heavy losses primarily because some soldiers abandoned their assigned positions, disobeying the Prophet\'s instructions to stay put.', 'The archers left their positions on the hill, allowing the enemy cavalry to attack from behind.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Battle of Uhud\\\",\\\"625 CE\\\",\\\"Disobedience\\\",\\\"Heavy Losses\\\",\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1614, '76623712-7ea7-4b27-89cb-b822c559253d', 32, 1, 'In which year was the Battle of Uhud fought?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"623 CE\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"624 CE\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"625 CE\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"627 CE\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Battle of Uhud was fought in 625 CE, one year after the Battle of Badr. It was fought near Mount Uhud close to Medina.', 'Uhud = 625 CE; Badr = 624 CE — one year apart.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Battle of Uhud\\\",\\\"625 CE\\\",\\\"Medina\\\",\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1615, 'e495400f-5523-4ec0-83d8-2a7d30cb4723', 32, 1, 'What military strategy was used in the Battle of the Trench (Khandaq)?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"A cavalry charge at sunrise\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Naval blockade of Medina\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Digging a trench around Medina to prevent enemy entry\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Guerrilla warfare in the mountains\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'In the Battle of the Trench (627 CE), the Muslims dug a large trench (khandaq) around the city of Medina to prevent the Quraysh and their allies from entering and attacking.', 'The trench idea was suggested by Salman al-Farisi, a Persian companion.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Battle of Trench\\\",\\\"Khandaq\\\",\\\"627 CE\\\",\\\"Trench\\\",\\\"Medina\\\",\\\"Strategy\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1616, '27e9e877-62d2-491c-b97a-cf2575705cda', 32, 1, 'In which year was the Battle of the Trench (Khandaq) fought?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"624 CE\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"625 CE\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"627 CE\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"628 CE\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Battle of the Trench (Khandaq) was fought in 627 CE. The Muslims defended Medina by digging a trench, preventing the large Quraysh-allied force from entering.', 'Trench = 627 CE — two years after Uhud.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Battle of Trench\\\",\\\"Khandaq\\\",\\\"627 CE\\\",\\\"Medina\\\",\\\"Defence\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1617, '5310521a-3315-4665-be60-37a0617963fc', 32, 1, 'What was the Treaty of Hudaybiyyah and when was it signed?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"A military alliance signed in 624 CE\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"A peace agreement signed with the Quraysh in 628 CE\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"A trade agreement with Medina\'s Jews in 622 CE\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"A defence pact with Byzantine Empire in 630 CE\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The Treaty of Hudaybiyyah was a peace agreement signed between Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) and the Quraysh in 628 CE. Though it seemed unfavorable initially, it led to rapid spread of Islam.', '628 CE — two years before the Conquest of Mecca.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Treaty of Hudaybiyyah\\\",\\\"628 CE\\\",\\\"Peace Agreement\\\",\\\"Quraysh\\\",\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1618, '00c2d33a-008d-450f-8f5c-e4d3f7dd89df', 32, 1, 'What was the long-term effect of the Treaty of Hudaybiyyah?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"It weakened the Muslim community\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"It led to peace and allowed Islam to spread rapidly\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"It divided the Muslims into two factions\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"It gave the Quraysh full control of Mecca\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Although some Muslims initially thought the Treaty of Hudaybiyyah was unfavorable, it eventually led to peace and created conditions that allowed Islam to spread rapidly across Arabia.', 'Short-term compromise for long-term gain — a strategic masterpiece.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Treaty of Hudaybiyyah\\\",\\\"Peace\\\",\\\"Islam Spread\\\",\\\"Long-term Effect\\\",\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1619, 'dec55f25-6b36-47cd-9294-2c8126e83f6d', 32, 1, 'When did the Conquest of Mecca take place?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"626 CE\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"628 CE\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"630 CE\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"632 CE\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Conquest of Mecca took place in 630 CE, when Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) peacefully entered Mecca with a large number of followers.', 'Conquest of Mecca = 630 CE — two years before the Prophet\'s death.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Conquest of Mecca\\\",\\\"630 CE\\\",\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\",\\\"Quraysh\\\",\\\"Mecca\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1620, '9df5e8eb-4c86-49bd-98eb-1979988a0b7f', 32, 1, 'What did the Prophet do with idols in the Kaaba after the Conquest of Mecca?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"He destroyed them with fire\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"He sent them to Medina\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"He removed them, restoring the Kaaba as a center for worship of one God\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"He preserved them as historical artifacts\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'After the Conquest of Mecca, the Prophet removed all idols from the Kaaba, restoring it to its original purpose as a center for the worship of Allah alone.', 'The Kaaba was returned to its purpose from the time of Ibrahim (AS).', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Conquest of Mecca\\\",\\\"Idols\\\",\\\"Kaaba\\\",\\\"Monotheism\\\",\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1621, 'd2205da1-6694-49f3-9081-5a489efb71a5', 32, 1, 'How did the Prophet treat his former enemies after the Conquest of Mecca?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"He imprisoned them all\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"He exiled them from Arabia\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"He forgave many of them\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"He made them pay heavy taxes\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'After the Conquest of Mecca, Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) famously forgave many of his former enemies — a remarkable act of mercy that led many Meccans to accept Islam.', 'This forgiveness is considered one of the most powerful moments of the Prophet\'s life.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Conquest of Mecca\\\",\\\"Forgiveness\\\",\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\",\\\"Mercy\\\",\\\"Enemies\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1622, '91b2039a-4ed7-48a6-ac0c-0714345b3110', 32, 1, 'What was the Battle of Khandaq also known as?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Battle of Uhud\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Battle of the Allies\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Battle of the Trench\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Battle of Badr\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Battle of Khandaq (meaning \'trench\' in Arabic) is also known as the Battle of the Trench. It took place in 627 CE when Muslims dug a trench to defend Medina.', 'Khandaq means trench in Arabic — the battle is named after this defence strategy.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Battle of Khandaq\\\",\\\"Battle of Trench\\\",\\\"627 CE\\\",\\\"Medina\\\",\\\"Defence\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1623, 'a686074d-79fd-4ccc-b47a-5cf21100bb21', 32, 1, 'What is the Farewell Pilgrimage?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"The Prophet\'s first Hajj in Medina\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The Prophet\'s last pilgrimage to Mecca in 632 CE\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The pilgrimage performed after the Conquest of Mecca\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Any pilgrimage performed by a dying person\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The Farewell Pilgrimage (Hajjat al-Wada) refers to the last pilgrimage to Mecca performed by Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) in 632 CE, just months before his death.', 'It is called \'farewell\' because it was the last time the Prophet performed Hajj.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Farewell Pilgrimage\\\",\\\"Hajjat al-Wada\\\",\\\"632 CE\\\",\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\",\\\"Mecca\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1624, '1bec1bbb-5109-4e11-8188-58ca7f2b7a43', 32, 1, 'What were the key themes of the Prophet\'s Farewell Sermon?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Military conquest and expansion\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Equality, justice, respect for women, and unity among Muslims\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Economic development and trade\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Strict religious laws and punishments\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'In the famous Farewell Sermon, Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) emphasized equality of all people, justice, respect and rights of women, and unity among Muslims.', 'The Farewell Sermon is considered a charter of human rights in Islamic tradition.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Farewell Sermon\\\",\\\"Equality\\\",\\\"Justice\\\",\\\"Women\\\",\\\"Unity\\\",\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1625, 'c303d6b7-3926-4ec5-9960-d1f6979b4d2f', 32, 1, 'On which date did Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) pass away?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"12 Rabi al-Awwal 10 AH\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"8 June 632 CE\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"14 August 632 CE\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"23 March 630 CE\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) passed away on 8 June 632 CE in the city of Medina, shortly after returning from the Farewell Pilgrimage.', 'He passed away in Medina — not in Mecca.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\",\\\"Death\\\",\\\"8 June 632 CE\\\",\\\"Medina\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1626, 'bec017ba-e219-4f4b-9f43-0267d928ffd3', 32, 1, 'At what age did Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) pass away?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"55 years\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"60 years\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"63 years\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"70 years\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) passed away at the age of sixty-three in 632 CE in Medina. This is the same age at which many great companions also passed away.', '63 years — born 570 CE, died 632 CE.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\",\\\"Death\\\",\\\"63 Years\\\",\\\"632 CE\\\",\\\"Medina\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1627, 'da32eb7b-8bec-43d1-aec3-45efc00ececf', 32, 1, 'In which city did Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) pass away?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Mecca\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Taif\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Jerusalem\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Medina\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) passed away in the city of Medina on 8 June 632 CE, shortly after returning from the Farewell Pilgrimage to Mecca.', 'He migrated to Medina and it became his home — he died there too.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\",\\\"Death\\\",\\\"Medina\\\",\\\"632 CE\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1628, '8bd71922-f6db-4879-87c0-d89f3a944e53', 32, 1, 'What is the lasting legacy of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH)?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"A military empire that lasted centuries\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Political control over the Arabian Peninsula\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Transforming the religious, social, and moral life of humanity through Islam and the Quran\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Economic prosperity for Arab nations\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Prophet left behind a powerful legacy that transformed the religious, social, and moral life of humanity. His teachings through the Quran guide Muslims in faith, law, and ethics.', 'His legacy is spiritual and moral — not merely political or military.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\",\\\"Legacy\\\",\\\"Islam\\\",\\\"Quran\\\",\\\"Humanity\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1629, 'fdc241e6-0248-4f1f-97c8-39e805c766d9', 32, 1, 'What does the life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) provide for Muslims?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"A political model for Arab governments\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"A military strategy manual\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"A complete example of honesty, patience, justice, mercy, and devotion to Allah\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Only historical information\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Prophet\'s life provides Muslims with a complete example (Sunnah) of honesty, patience, justice, mercy, and devotion to Allah to follow in their daily lives.', 'His life is the practical model for living as a Muslim.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Prophet Muhammad\\\",\\\"Sunnah\\\",\\\"Example\\\",\\\"Honesty\\\",\\\"Patience\\\",\\\"Mercy\\\"]\"', 'Life of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:33:00', '2026-04-30 20:33:00'),
(1630, '53cdcc2a-f574-41d2-a16b-9122f9a9fe15', 33, 1, 'What does the word \'Rashidun\' mean?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Brave Warriors\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Rightly Guided\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Chosen by Allah\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"First Muslims\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The word \'Rashidun\' means \'Rightly Guided\'. The Rashidun Caliphate (632–661 CE) is considered a model of Islamic governance based on the Quran and Sunnah.', 'Rashid in Arabic means guided to the right path.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Rashidun\\\",\\\"Rightly Guided\\\",\\\"Caliphate\\\",\\\"Islamic History\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1631, '44f941e5-673f-489c-8989-a604d6d41ff7', 33, 1, 'Which was the first caliphate established after the death of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH)?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Umayyad Caliphate\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Abbasid Caliphate\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Rashidun Caliphate\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Ottoman Caliphate\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Rashidun Caliphate (632–661 CE) was the first caliphate after the Prophet\'s death, led by the four Rightly Guided Caliphs — Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, and Ali.', 'It began immediately after the Prophet\'s death in 632 CE.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Rashidun Caliphate\\\",\\\"First Caliphate\\\",\\\"632 CE\\\",\\\"Islamic History\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1632, 'f4689612-d4be-4b9b-a408-bba77ddb7647', 33, 1, 'Who was the first caliph of the Rashidun Caliphate?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Umar ibn al-Khattab\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Ali ibn Abi Talib\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Uthman ibn Affan\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Abu Bakr Siddiq\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'Abu Bakr Siddiq (632–634 CE) was the first caliph. He united Arabia after the Prophet\'s death and suppressed rebellions (Wars of Riddah) against the Muslim state.', 'Abu Bakr served as caliph for only about 2 years (632–634 CE).', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Abu Bakr\\\",\\\"First Caliph\\\",\\\"Rashidun\\\",\\\"632 CE\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1633, 'bfd4e8fa-b1e6-4c88-ae31-7da63382e89d', 33, 1, 'Which Rashidun Caliph expanded the Islamic empire to Egypt, Syria, and Iraq?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Abu Bakr Siddiq\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Ali ibn Abi Talib\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Uthman ibn Affan\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Umar ibn al-Khattab\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (634–644 CE) was responsible for the great territorial expansion of the Islamic empire into Egypt, Syria, Iraq, and Persia, and also established administrative systems.', 'Umar\'s caliphate saw the most rapid territorial expansion in Islamic history.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Umar\\\",\\\"Second Caliph\\\",\\\"Expansion\\\",\\\"Egypt\\\",\\\"Syria\\\",\\\"Iraq\\\",\\\"Rashidun\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1634, '0d7db680-af7f-4cb4-839b-8aaa1c756a6b', 33, 1, 'Which Rashidun Caliph compiled the Quran into a single written text?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Abu Bakr Siddiq\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Umar ibn al-Khattab\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Ali ibn Abi Talib\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Uthman ibn Affan\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'Uthman ibn Affan (644–656 CE) compiled and standardized the Quran into a single written text (Mushaf), sending copies to major cities to ensure uniformity of the scripture.', 'Uthman is also known as Dhun-Noorayn — he standardized the Quran.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Uthman\\\",\\\"Quran\\\",\\\"Compilation\\\",\\\"Third Caliph\\\",\\\"Rashidun\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1635, '8652f71f-493f-4445-8871-65b10dcf2578', 33, 1, 'Which internal conflicts did Ali ibn Abi Talib face during his caliphate?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Wars against Rome and Persia\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Rebellions in Egypt and Syria only\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Battle of Camel and Battle of Siffin\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Mongol invasions\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Ali ibn Abi Talib (656–661 CE) faced major internal conflicts including the Battle of the Camel (against Aisha, Talhah, and Zubair) and the Battle of Siffin (against Mu\'awiyah).', 'These were civil wars within the Muslim community — the first major internal conflicts.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Ali\\\",\\\"Fourth Caliph\\\",\\\"Battle of Camel\\\",\\\"Battle of Siffin\\\",\\\"Rashidun\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1636, 'c39c9f57-b35d-4eba-96ad-d75e1a41a687', 33, 1, 'What were the key characteristics of the Rashidun period?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Military conquest only\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Luxury and expansion of palaces\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Justice, simplicity, adherence to Quran and Sunnah, and rapid expansion\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Cultural development and arts\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Rashidun period was marked by justice, simplicity, strict adherence to the Quran and Sunnah, and rapid expansion of the Islamic state — making it a model of Islamic governance.', 'The Rashidun are admired for their simple, pious, and just leadership style.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Rashidun\\\",\\\"Justice\\\",\\\"Simplicity\\\",\\\"Quran\\\",\\\"Sunnah\\\",\\\"Expansion\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1637, '41f57605-23b5-4137-bec8-977b3ab83127', 33, 1, 'When did the Rashidun Caliphate end?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"632 CE\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"644 CE\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"656 CE\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"661 CE\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'The Rashidun Caliphate ended in 661 CE with the assassination of Ali ibn Abi Talib, after which Mu\'awiyah established the Umayyad Caliphate with Damascus as its capital.', '661 CE marks both the end of Rashidun and the start of the Umayyad era.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Rashidun Caliphate\\\",\\\"End\\\",\\\"661 CE\\\",\\\"Ali\\\",\\\"Umayyad\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1638, '9b05629a-7b08-42c3-b942-296c200e9359', 33, 1, 'What was Abu Bakr\'s main challenge as the first caliph?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Expanding the empire to Spain\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Compiling the Quran\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Uniting Arabia and suppressing rebellions after the Prophet\'s death\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Building mosques across Arabia\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Abu Bakr Siddiq\'s main challenge was uniting Arabia and suppressing the rebellions (Wars of Riddah) that broke out after the Prophet\'s death, including false prophets and those refusing to pay Zakat.', 'Wars of Riddah = apostasy wars — a major early challenge for the Muslim state.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Abu Bakr\\\",\\\"Rashidun\\\",\\\"Wars of Riddah\\\",\\\"Rebellions\\\",\\\"Arabia\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1639, '0ad5025a-3cb3-4f90-ab0b-65075d6f4d09', 33, 1, 'Ali ibn Abi Talib was particularly known for which two qualities?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Bravery in battle and wealth\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Justice and knowledge\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Military strategy and diplomacy\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Trade skills and scholarship\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, the fourth Rashidun Caliph, was well known for his justice and deep knowledge of Islamic law and theology. He is revered for his wisdom and piety.', 'Ali\'s knowledge of Islamic jurisprudence is legendary — he is called \'Bab al-Ilm\' (Gate of Knowledge).', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Ali\\\",\\\"Justice\\\",\\\"Knowledge\\\",\\\"Fourth Caliph\\\",\\\"Rashidun\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1641, '19726327-9630-4ce6-a587-d457c99bbcff', 33, 1, 'During which years did the Umayyad Caliphate rule?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"632\\\\u2013661 CE\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"661\\\\u2013750 CE\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"750\\\\u20131258 CE\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"1258\\\\u20131517 CE\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The Umayyad Caliphate ruled from 661 CE to 750 CE, when it was overthrown by the Abbasid revolution. It lasted approximately 90 years.', 'Umayyad: 661–750 CE; Abbasid: 750–1258 CE — remember these dates.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Umayyad Caliphate\\\",\\\"661 CE\\\",\\\"750 CE\\\",\\\"Duration\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1642, '3550ccbf-6457-45b8-a77d-2a246b405828', 33, 1, 'The Umayyad Caliphate expanded Islam into which regions?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"East Asia and Australia\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"North Africa, Spain (Al-Andalus), and Central Asia\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Scandinavia and Eastern Europe\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Sub-Saharan Africa only\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The Umayyad Caliphate expanded the Islamic empire into North Africa, Spain (known as Al-Andalus), and Central Asia, creating one of the largest empires in history.', 'Spain under Muslims was called Al-Andalus — a famous center of Islamic civilization.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Umayyad\\\",\\\"Expansion\\\",\\\"North Africa\\\",\\\"Spain\\\",\\\"Al-Andalus\\\",\\\"Central Asia\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1643, 'b567bc22-2b58-4d10-b792-082d80f0b349', 33, 1, 'What language did the Umayyad Caliphate introduce as the official administrative language?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Persian\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Turkish\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Greek\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Arabic\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'The Umayyad Caliphate introduced Arabic as the official administrative language of the empire, replacing Greek, Persian, and other local languages used in government records.', 'This Arabization policy unified the vast empire through a common language.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Umayyad\\\",\\\"Arabic\\\",\\\"Official Language\\\",\\\"Administration\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1644, '0bbd8c76-5b49-4836-8542-652075a7fb43', 33, 1, 'What social tension arose during the Umayyad Caliphate?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Conflict between Muslims and Christians only\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Tension between Arab and non-Arab Muslims due to focus on political authority\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Conflict over trade routes\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Disagreements about prayer methods\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The Umayyad focus on political authority and Arab identity created social tensions between Arab Muslims and non-Arab Muslims (Mawali), who felt marginalized despite being equal in Islam.', 'Non-Arab Muslims (called Mawali) were often treated as second-class citizens.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Umayyad\\\",\\\"Social Tension\\\",\\\"Arab\\\",\\\"Non-Arab\\\",\\\"Mawali\\\",\\\"Political Authority\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1645, '188c5d56-a304-48c7-b077-eac8a853a811', 33, 1, 'The Umayyad Caliphate stretched from which regions?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Arabia to Egypt only\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Central Asia to North Africa only\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Spain to India\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Persia to China\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Umayyad Caliphate stretched from Spain (Al-Andalus) in the west to India in the east, creating one of the largest land empires in world history.', 'From the Iberian Peninsula (Spain) in Europe to the Indian subcontinent in Asia.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Umayyad\\\",\\\"Extent\\\",\\\"Spain\\\",\\\"India\\\",\\\"Empire\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1646, 'edb3fbe5-5463-47dc-8f4e-290bc32b91f6', 33, 1, 'What infrastructure developments occurred during the Umayyad Caliphate?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Only military forts were built\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Development of roads, mosques, and cities\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Only trading posts\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Only schools and libraries\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The Umayyad Caliphate developed significant infrastructure including roads for trade and military movement, mosques for worship, and planned cities across the empire.', 'Infrastructure development helped consolidate control over the vast empire.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Umayyad\\\",\\\"Infrastructure\\\",\\\"Roads\\\",\\\"Mosques\\\",\\\"Cities\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1647, '9efbe3d1-e3f5-4514-82df-0c352b572ce8', 33, 1, 'Which caliphate overthrew the Umayyads in 750 CE?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Ottoman Caliphate\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Rashidun Caliphate\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Fatimid Caliphate\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Abbasid Caliphate\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'The Abbasid Caliphate overthrew the Umayyad Caliphate in 750 CE through a revolution, then established Baghdad as the new capital of the Islamic world.', '750 CE marks the end of Umayyad and the beginning of Abbasid rule.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Abbasid\\\",\\\"Umayyad\\\",\\\"Overthrow\\\",\\\"750 CE\\\",\\\"Revolution\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1648, '847df262-9269-4e54-aee3-a9817816f526', 33, 1, 'What is Al-Andalus?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"The Umayyad name for Baghdad\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The Umayyad name for Egypt\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The Muslim name for Spain during the Islamic period\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"The Umayyad name for Persia\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Al-Andalus is the Arabic name for the Iberian Peninsula (modern Spain and Portugal) during the period of Muslim rule under the Umayyads and their successors.', 'Al-Andalus was a center of Islamic learning and culture in Europe for centuries.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Al-Andalus\\\",\\\"Spain\\\",\\\"Umayyad\\\",\\\"Islamic History\\\",\\\"Europe\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1650, 'bfe04d28-fcf9-463f-9d0b-efed25c2ae67', 33, 1, 'During which years did the Abbasid Caliphate rule?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"632\\\\u2013661 CE\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"661\\\\u2013750 CE\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"750\\\\u20131258 CE\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"1258\\\\u20131500 CE\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Abbasid Caliphate ruled from 750 CE to 1258 CE — a period of approximately 500 years, making it one of the longest-lasting caliphates in Islamic history.', 'Abbasid: 750 CE to 1258 CE — ended with the Mongol invasion of Baghdad.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Abbasid Caliphate\\\",\\\"750 CE\\\",\\\"1258 CE\\\",\\\"Duration\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1651, 'c9b4cfe1-3813-4f8d-9cd4-a7e825cf80a5', 33, 1, 'What is Bayt al-Hikmah (House of Wisdom)?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"A military training center in Baghdad\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The Abbasid royal palace\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"A center in Baghdad for translation, research, and learning\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"A famous mosque in Damascus\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Bayt al-Hikmah (House of Wisdom) was established in Baghdad during the Abbasid period as a great center for translation, research, and learning — the intellectual heart of the Islamic Golden Age.', 'It preserved and translated knowledge from Greek, Persian, and Indian sources.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Bayt al-Hikmah\\\",\\\"House of Wisdom\\\",\\\"Baghdad\\\",\\\"Abbasid\\\",\\\"Knowledge\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1652, '2dc3ecb7-171f-4dcf-8412-90c5eb516145', 33, 1, 'What period is known as the \'Golden Age of Islam\'?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Rashidun Caliphate period\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Umayyad Caliphate period\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Abbasid Caliphate period\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Ottoman Caliphate period\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Abbasid Caliphate period (750–1258 CE) is known as the Golden Age of Islam, characterized by extraordinary advances in science, mathematics, medicine, philosophy, and culture.', 'The establishment of Bayt al-Hikmah in Baghdad symbolizes this golden age.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Golden Age of Islam\\\",\\\"Abbasid Caliphate\\\",\\\"Science\\\",\\\"Culture\\\",\\\"Baghdad\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1653, '995e4150-c506-444b-8dd2-6c1b92b09959', 33, 1, 'Which knowledge sources did the Abbasids blend with Islamic principles?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Chinese and Japanese knowledge\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"African and South American knowledge\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Greek, Indian, and Persian knowledge\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Viking and Roman knowledge\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Abbasids emphasized intellectual development by blending Islamic principles with knowledge from Greece (philosophy, science), India (mathematics, astronomy), and Persia (administration, literature).', 'Translation movement brought Greek, Indian, and Persian texts into Arabic.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Abbasid\\\",\\\"Greek\\\",\\\"Indian\\\",\\\"Persian\\\",\\\"Knowledge\\\",\\\"Translation\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1654, '9c0268fc-73cf-4a98-99e8-11599aa84161', 33, 1, 'What ended the Abbasid Caliphate in 1258 CE?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"An internal revolution by Arab tribes\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The Crusader invasion from Europe\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The Mongol invasion of Baghdad\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"The Ottoman conquest\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Abbasid Caliphate ended in 1258 CE when Mongol forces under Hulagu Khan invaded and destroyed Baghdad, killing the last Abbasid caliph and ending Muslim political power in Baghdad.', 'Hulagu Khan was the grandson of Genghis Khan — his forces sacked Baghdad in 1258 CE.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Mongol Invasion\\\",\\\"Baghdad\\\",\\\"1258 CE\\\",\\\"Abbasid\\\",\\\"Hulagu Khan\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1655, '079f8a6f-c6e2-4904-a08a-1e0bbd503f44', 33, 1, 'What did the Abbasids promote that made their era remarkable?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Military conquest above everything else\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Education, literature, Islamic scholarship, and scientific advancement\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Trade and merchant guilds only\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Strict political control and taxation\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The Abbasids promoted education, literature, Islamic scholarship, and remarkable scientific advancement, earning their era the title of the \'Golden Age of Islam\'.', 'Their emphasis was on knowledge — the pen alongside the sword.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Abbasid\\\",\\\"Education\\\",\\\"Literature\\\",\\\"Scholarship\\\",\\\"Science\\\",\\\"Golden Age\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1656, 'a28b98e2-9b0b-44a1-896f-f583c8c34549', 33, 1, 'What happened to Islamic civilization after the Mongol invasion of 1258 CE?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"It collapsed entirely and permanently\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"It immediately recovered within a year\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Islamic civilization continued to flourish despite the end of Abbasid political power\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"It moved to Spain permanently\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Although the Mongol invasion ended Abbasid political power in Baghdad, Islamic civilization continued to flourish in other regions — Egypt, Persia, and later the Ottoman, Safavid, and Mughal empires.', 'Political power ended in Baghdad, but Islamic civilization survived and continued elsewhere.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Mongol Invasion\\\",\\\"1258 CE\\\",\\\"Islamic Civilization\\\",\\\"Abbasid\\\",\\\"Continuation\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1657, '7fa2b709-aa8e-4fc9-a11a-1e5111294fa0', 33, 1, 'The Abbasid Caliphate promoted trade networks across which regions?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Only within the Arabian Peninsula\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Only Europe and Africa\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Asia, Europe, and Africa\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Only Central Asia\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Abbasid Caliphate expanded trade networks across Asia, Europe, and Africa, making Baghdad a global center of commerce connecting East and West.', 'Baghdad\'s location made it ideal for intercontinental trade routes.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Abbasid\\\",\\\"Trade\\\",\\\"Asia\\\",\\\"Europe\\\",\\\"Africa\\\",\\\"Baghdad\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1658, '84569ca9-7552-4231-8084-fb8c76a55358', 33, 1, 'How long did the Abbasid Caliphate last?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"About 90 years\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"About 200 years\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"About 300 years\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"About 500 years\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'The Abbasid Caliphate lasted from 750 CE to 1258 CE — approximately 508 years, making it one of the longest-running caliphates in Islamic history.', '750 CE to 1258 CE = approximately 500 years.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Abbasid Caliphate\\\",\\\"Duration\\\",\\\"500 Years\\\",\\\"Islamic History\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49');
INSERT INTO `mcqs` (`id`, `uuid`, `topic_id`, `subject_id`, `question`, `question_type`, `options`, `correct_answers`, `explanation`, `hint`, `difficulty_level`, `time_limit_seconds`, `marks`, `negative_marks`, `tags`, `reference_book`, `reference_page`, `is_premium`, `is_verified`, `status`, `created_by`, `approved_by`, `approved_at`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(1659, '5e1ea56b-be3e-4535-8486-2f4d91fe8afe', 33, 1, 'What was the Battle of Badr and when was it fought?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"First Muslim defeat against Rome in 622 CE\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"First major Muslim victory against Quraysh in 624 CE\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"A defensive battle against Persians in 627 CE\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"A battle during Uthman\'s caliphate in 650 CE\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The Battle of Badr (624 CE) was the first major military victory of Muslims against the Quraysh of Mecca. Despite being outnumbered, the Muslims won decisively.', 'Badr = 624 CE, first major Muslim victory — a turning point for early Islam.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Battle of Badr\\\",\\\"624 CE\\\",\\\"Muslim Victory\\\",\\\"Quraysh\\\",\\\"Islamic History\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1660, '48bbd1f3-c39f-4714-8e84-ea7ea52f6f1d', 33, 1, 'What lesson did the Battle of Uhud (625 CE) teach?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"That Muslims should never fight Quraysh\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"That large armies always win\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"That discipline and following the Prophet\'s orders are essential\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"That peace is always better than war\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Battle of Uhud (625 CE) resulted in Muslim losses because some soldiers abandoned their positions against the Prophet\'s orders. The lesson was that discipline and obedience are essential.', 'Archers left their hilltop positions, allowing enemy cavalry to flank the Muslim army.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Battle of Uhud\\\",\\\"625 CE\\\",\\\"Discipline\\\",\\\"Disobedience\\\",\\\"Lesson\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1661, '0ab18988-bce4-41e2-98c7-5f31273c3961', 33, 1, 'What defensive strategy was used in the Battle of the Trench (627 CE)?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Night raid on the enemy camp\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Cavalry charge at dawn\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Digging a trench around Medina\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Retreating to the mountains\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'In the Battle of the Trench (627 CE), Muslims dug a large trench (khandaq) around Medina to prevent a massive coalition army from entering the city, effectively neutralizing the attack.', 'The idea of digging a trench came from Salman al-Farisi, a Persian companion.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Battle of Trench\\\",\\\"627 CE\\\",\\\"Khandaq\\\",\\\"Trench\\\",\\\"Medina\\\",\\\"Defence\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1662, '76a41734-6909-42e8-af7d-0408af1a76b1', 33, 1, 'What was the strategic importance of the Treaty of Hudaybiyyah (628 CE)?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"It ended the Battle of Badr\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"It gave Muslims control of Mecca immediately\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"It was a peace agreement that allowed Islam to spread peacefully\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"It ended the Umayyad Caliphate\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Treaty of Hudaybiyyah (628 CE) was a peace agreement with the Quraysh that, despite seeming unfavorable, allowed Muslims to spread Islam peacefully and led to the Conquest of Mecca.', 'Short-term compromise led to long-term victory — the Conquest of Mecca 2 years later.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Treaty of Hudaybiyyah\\\",\\\"628 CE\\\",\\\"Peace\\\",\\\"Islam Spread\\\",\\\"Quraysh\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1663, '743590ad-2395-4a3b-8111-d29e5c6824b3', 33, 1, 'What was the significance of the Conquest of Mecca (630 CE)?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"It marked the end of the Prophet\'s life\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Islam became firmly established in the Arabian Peninsula\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"It started the Islamic calendar\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"It began the Abbasid Caliphate\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The Conquest of Mecca in 630 CE firmly established Islam in the Arabian Peninsula. The Prophet entered Mecca peacefully, removed idols from the Kaaba, and granted amnesty to former enemies.', 'The Prophet\'s peaceful entry and mass forgiveness became a defining moment.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Conquest of Mecca\\\",\\\"630 CE\\\",\\\"Islam\\\",\\\"Arabian Peninsula\\\",\\\"Kaaba\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1664, '54919f02-717f-4486-9781-1ccf714983b3', 33, 1, 'What event caused the end of Abbasid political power in 1258 CE?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"The Crusades from Europe\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The rise of the Ottoman Turks\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The Mongol invasion of Baghdad\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"An internal revolution\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Mongol invasion of Baghdad in 1258 CE, led by Hulagu Khan, destroyed the city, killed the caliph, and ended Abbasid political power, though Islamic civilization continued elsewhere.', '1258 CE = Mongols destroy Baghdad = End of Abbasid Caliphate.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Mongol Invasion\\\",\\\"1258 CE\\\",\\\"Baghdad\\\",\\\"Abbasid\\\",\\\"Hulagu Khan\\\",\\\"End\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1665, '929dc7df-186b-4101-b614-94377245abad', 33, 1, 'In what sequence did the following battles occur? Badr, Uhud, Trench', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Trench, Badr, Uhud\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Uhud, Badr, Trench\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Badr, Trench, Uhud\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Badr, Uhud, Trench\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'The correct sequence is: Battle of Badr (624 CE), Battle of Uhud (625 CE), Battle of the Trench (627 CE). Each was one to two years apart.', '624, 625, 627 CE — Badr first, then Uhud, then Trench.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Battle of Badr\\\",\\\"Battle of Uhud\\\",\\\"Battle of Trench\\\",\\\"Sequence\\\",\\\"Islamic History\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1666, '3ff6b117-768f-4c85-a827-df5d1999951c', 33, 1, 'What does the rapid spread of Islam beyond Arabia demonstrate?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"That it was spread only by military force\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"That early Muslims were economically powerful\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The appeal of Islamic principles and effective leadership of early caliphs\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"That the Arabian Peninsula was overpopulated\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The rapid spread of Islam beyond Arabia reflects both the universal appeal of Islamic principles (justice, equality, monotheism) and the effective governance and leadership of the early caliphs.', 'Islam spread through a combination of military expansion, trade, and genuine conversion.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Spread of Islam\\\",\\\"Arabia\\\",\\\"Islamic Principles\\\",\\\"Early Caliphs\\\",\\\"Expansion\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1667, '00fb7ed4-5342-425a-b1aa-78e69b00e1fe', 33, 1, 'Which treaty directly led to the eventual Conquest of Mecca?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Treaty of Medina\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Constitution of Medina\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Treaty of Hudaybiyyah\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Treaty of Taif\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Treaty of Hudaybiyyah (628 CE) created a period of peace during which Islam spread rapidly. When the Quraysh violated it, the Prophet marched on and conquered Mecca in 630 CE.', 'Hudaybiyyah was signed in 628 CE and Mecca was conquered just 2 years later in 630 CE.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Treaty of Hudaybiyyah\\\",\\\"Conquest of Mecca\\\",\\\"628 CE\\\",\\\"630 CE\\\",\\\"Connection\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1668, '899854e6-63df-4038-99c5-67b1cbecaf1f', 33, 1, 'What made the Battle of Badr historically significant?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"It was the largest battle in Islamic history\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"It was fought outside Arabia\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"It was the first major Muslim victory despite Muslims being outnumbered\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"It established the Islamic calendar\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Battle of Badr was historically significant as the first major Muslim military victory. The Muslims were greatly outnumbered but defeated the Quraysh, boosting Muslim morale and credibility.', 'Being outnumbered yet victorious — this battle proved the early Muslim community\'s strength.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Battle of Badr\\\",\\\"First Victory\\\",\\\"Outnumbered\\\",\\\"Significance\\\",\\\"Islamic History\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1669, 'd39aa205-f112-46ac-861c-6588d48771a4', 33, 1, 'What year did the spread of Islam beyond Arabia begin most rapidly?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"During Abu Bakr\'s caliphate from 632 CE\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"During Umar\'s caliphate from 634 CE\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"During the Umayyad period from 661 CE\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"All of the above are correct\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'The spread of Islam beyond Arabia began under Abu Bakr, accelerated dramatically under Umar (who conquered Egypt, Syria, Iraq), and continued at pace under the Umayyads — all phases contributed.', 'Each caliphate contributed to Islamic expansion — no single one can be credited alone.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Islam Expansion\\\",\\\"Arabia\\\",\\\"Abu Bakr\\\",\\\"Umar\\\",\\\"Umayyad\\\",\\\"Historical\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1670, '7251ebc3-15fe-450d-bf64-8a5613b34df4', 33, 1, 'Who is Al-Khwarizmi and what is he known for?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"A Muslim philosopher who refuted Greek logic\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"A Muslim physician known for medical encyclopedias\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"A Muslim mathematician known for developing algebra and geometry\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"A Muslim astronomer who discovered new planets\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Al-Khwarizmi was a Muslim mathematician who developed algebra, geometry, and trigonometry during the Abbasid period. The word \'algorithm\' is derived from his name.', 'The word \'algebra\' comes from his book \'Al-Kitab al-Mukhtasar fi Hisab al-Jabr.\'', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Al-Khwarizmi\\\",\\\"Algebra\\\",\\\"Mathematics\\\",\\\"Abbasid\\\",\\\"Islamic Science\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1671, '2f072a49-b173-4c35-957b-fccafbb3a73b', 33, 1, 'Who was Ibn Sina (Avicenna) and what was his major contribution?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"A poet famous for Arabic literature\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"A caliph who expanded the empire\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"A physician known for advances in medicine\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"An architect who designed the Dome of the Rock\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Ibn Sina (known in the West as Avicenna) was a renowned Muslim physician whose medical encyclopedia \'Al-Qanun fi al-Tibb\' (Canon of Medicine) was used in European universities for centuries.', 'Avicenna = Ibn Sina — his Canon of Medicine influenced medical education worldwide.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Ibn Sina\\\",\\\"Avicenna\\\",\\\"Medicine\\\",\\\"Physician\\\",\\\"Islamic Science\\\",\\\"Abbasid\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1672, '81dadd4f-3bbe-4d52-bb46-53c20390840b', 33, 1, 'What significant role did Muslims play in preserving ancient knowledge?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"They destroyed ancient texts\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"They preserved and translated Greek, Roman, and Indian knowledge into Arabic\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"They ignored non-Islamic knowledge\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"They only preserved Islamic texts\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Muslim scholars preserved and translated vast amounts of Greek, Roman, and Indian knowledge into Arabic at Bayt al-Hikmah, saving works that would otherwise have been lost and later transmitting them to Europe.', 'Without Muslim preservation, much of ancient Greek philosophy and science would have been lost.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Muslims\\\",\\\"Preservation\\\",\\\"Translation\\\",\\\"Greek\\\",\\\"Roman\\\",\\\"Indian\\\",\\\"Knowledge\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1673, '261d2b22-fb6b-43ba-83c8-5ecdc08846eb', 33, 1, 'Which architectural structures are examples of Islamic contribution to arts and culture?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"The Eiffel Tower and Big Ben\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The Colosseum and Pantheon\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The Dome of the Rock and Alhambra\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"The Taj Mahal and Angkor Wat\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The Dome of the Rock in Jerusalem and the Alhambra palace in Spain are iconic examples of Islamic architectural achievement, demonstrating Muslim contributions to arts and urban planning.', 'Dome of the Rock = Islamic architecture in Jerusalem; Alhambra = Islamic architecture in Spain.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Islamic Architecture\\\",\\\"Dome of Rock\\\",\\\"Alhambra\\\",\\\"Culture\\\",\\\"Arts\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1674, '8f731c6c-155b-4b0f-abea-dd37aaa96f29', 33, 1, 'In which fields did Muslims make significant scientific advances during the Abbasid period?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Only in military weapons and ships\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Science, mathematics, astronomy, medicine, and philosophy\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Only in agriculture and trade\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Only in literature and poetry\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'During the Abbasid period, Muslims made major advances in science, mathematics, astronomy, medicine, and philosophy — earning this era the title of the Golden Age of Islam.', 'All branches of knowledge flourished in this golden period.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Abbasid\\\",\\\"Science\\\",\\\"Mathematics\\\",\\\"Astronomy\\\",\\\"Medicine\\\",\\\"Philosophy\\\",\\\"Golden Age\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1675, 'd00fde9d-71f2-4c5d-a9cd-613de92e4419', 33, 1, 'What were madrasas and what role did they play?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Military training centers for soldiers\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Islamic schools that promoted education and scholarly learning\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Markets for book trading\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Government administrative offices\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Madrasas were Islamic educational institutions that promoted literacy and scholarly learning. They were established across the Islamic world during the Abbasid and later periods.', 'Madrasa means \'place of study\' — the Islamic equivalent of a university.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Madrasas\\\",\\\"Education\\\",\\\"Islamic Schools\\\",\\\"Scholarship\\\",\\\"Islamic History\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1676, '90c942ef-aa71-4c29-a489-211faa5fdf8e', 33, 1, 'What is the significance of Islamic contributions to algebra?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Muslims invented counting systems\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Muslims developed algebra which later became foundational to modern mathematics and science\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Muslims only used algebra for religious purposes\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Muslims borrowed algebra entirely from Greeks\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Al-Khwarizmi\'s development of algebra during the Islamic Golden Age became foundational to modern mathematics, engineering, and computer science. The word \'algebra\' comes from his Arabic text.', 'Without algebra, modern science, engineering, and computing would not exist as we know them.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Algebra\\\",\\\"Al-Khwarizmi\\\",\\\"Mathematics\\\",\\\"Islamic Contribution\\\",\\\"Modern Science\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1677, '76905e52-8dc4-452d-bbc3-ee30e0e2a56c', 33, 1, 'How did Islamic civilization influence Europe?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Islam had no influence on Europe\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Islamic civilization shaped European education, science, governance, and culture for centuries\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Muslims conquered all of Europe\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Only Islamic architecture influenced Europe\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Islamic civilization significantly influenced Europe through translated scientific and philosophical texts, medical knowledge, mathematical concepts, and cultural exchanges during the medieval period.', 'The European Renaissance was partly fueled by Islamic knowledge transmitted through Spain and Sicily.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Islamic Civilization\\\",\\\"Europe\\\",\\\"Influence\\\",\\\"Science\\\",\\\"Education\\\",\\\"Culture\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1678, '4af171ad-da22-41d3-b3b9-0869d245439b', 33, 1, 'What artistic contributions did Islamic civilization make?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Only religious manuscripts\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Development of Arabic literature, poetry, calligraphy, and innovations in textiles and ceramics\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Only mosque architecture\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Only military arts\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Islamic civilization contributed Arabic literature, poetry, calligraphy, mosque and palace architecture, and innovations in textiles, ceramics, and handicrafts — enriching global culture.', 'Islamic art is particularly known for geometric patterns and calligraphy.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Islamic Art\\\",\\\"Literature\\\",\\\"Poetry\\\",\\\"Calligraphy\\\",\\\"Textiles\\\",\\\"Ceramics\\\",\\\"Culture\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1679, '461d5d20-a654-4466-b488-6b0e9ccfb352', 33, 1, 'What is the broader significance of Islamic civilization\'s contributions to humanity?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"It only benefited Muslim countries\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"It shaped global knowledge, shaping education, science, governance, and culture that influenced Europe and Asia for centuries\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"It was limited to the medieval period with no lasting impact\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"It primarily advanced military technology\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Islamic civilization\'s contributions — in science, education, governance, and culture — shaped human knowledge globally, influencing European Renaissance, Asian civilizations, and modern scientific thought.', 'The Islamic Golden Age preserved and advanced human knowledge at a critical period in history.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Islamic Civilization\\\",\\\"Global Impact\\\",\\\"Science\\\",\\\"Education\\\",\\\"Governance\\\",\\\"Culture\\\",\\\"Legacy\\\"]\"', 'Islamic History - General Knowledge', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-30 20:44:49', '2026-04-30 20:44:49'),
(1680, '555e666c-b793-48aa-ab04-9eceba9832d8', 145, 4, 'Which of the following is a proper noun?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"city\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"teacher\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Karachi\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"country\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Karachi is the name of a specific city, making it a proper noun. Proper nouns always begin with a capital letter.', 'Proper nouns name a specific person, place, or thing and are capitalised.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"nouns\\\",\\\" proper noun\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '1', 0, 0, 'draft', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:47:13'),
(1681, '5e32e715-92a0-4eeb-bfca-1e4b12e1c821', 145, 4, 'Which of the following is an uncountable noun?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"book\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"child\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"furniture\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"apple\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Furniture is an uncountable noun — it cannot be counted individually and has no plural form.', 'Uncountable nouns have no plural form and always take a singular verb.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"nouns\\\",\\\" uncountable noun\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '1', 0, 0, 'draft', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:49:38'),
(1682, 'c6d97c7b-687c-4eca-88ef-77ef2d151f42', 145, 4, 'What type of noun is \'happiness\'?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Concrete noun\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Proper noun\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Collective noun\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Abstract noun\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'Happiness is an abstract noun — it names a feeling or state that cannot be seen or touched.', 'Abstract nouns name ideas, feelings, or qualities.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"nouns\\\",\\\"abstract noun\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1683, '86e0c419-41ab-4c9a-b307-774359722c3a', 145, 4, 'Which word is a collective noun?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"bird\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"flock\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"stone\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"courage\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Flock is a collective noun that refers to a group of birds treated as a single unit.', 'Collective nouns name groups of people, animals, or things.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"nouns\\\",\\\"collective noun\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1684, 'baa8ba09-dd0b-489f-8b3a-ded78087ff85', 145, 4, 'Which sentence uses a noun as an appositive?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"The teacher explained the rule.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"She loves music.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"My friend Ali, a doctor, arrived late.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"He sat on the chair.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'A doctor\' is an appositive — it renames the subject \'Ali\' and is placed right after it.', 'An appositive renames or explains the noun next to it.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"nouns\\\",\\\"appositive\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1685, 'f11b0a18-0819-4d70-aa45-f6aa8cc90504', 145, 4, 'Which of the following sentences contains an error related to uncountable nouns?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"He gave me useful advice.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"She provided important informations.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The luggage was heavy.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"We received good news.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', '\'Informations\' is incorrect. \'Information\' is an uncountable noun and has no plural form.', 'Words like information, advice, luggage, and news are always singular.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"nouns\\\",\\\"uncountable noun\\\",\\\"common errors\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1686, 'ac11bf2e-7122-4736-8e30-b606e876a7e7', 145, 4, 'Which of the following is a compound noun?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"freedom\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"committee\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"toothpaste\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"honesty\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Toothpaste is a compound noun formed by combining \'tooth\' and \'paste\' into a single noun concept.', 'Compound nouns are formed by joining two or more words.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"nouns\\\",\\\"compound noun\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1687, '7eaf60b1-e5ff-4e48-8f1c-07c81a316fa6', 145, 4, 'In the sentence \'Water is essential for life,\' what type of noun is \'Water\'?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Collective noun\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Countable noun\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Uncountable noun\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Abstract noun\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Water is an uncountable noun. It cannot be counted individually and has no plural form.', 'Can you say \'two waters\' in a general sense? If not, it is uncountable.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"nouns\\\",\\\" uncountable noun\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '1', 0, 0, 'draft', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:46:42'),
(1688, '9582e3b7-4961-47ac-b32d-96ff2be49791', 145, 4, 'Which of the following is a reflexive pronoun?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"him\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"himself\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"his\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"he\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', '\'Himself\' is a reflexive pronoun that refers back to the subject of the sentence.', 'Reflexive pronouns end in -self or -selves.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"pronouns\\\",\\\"reflexive pronoun\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1689, '3fa65d05-976d-44b5-8812-31530ade544e', 145, 4, 'Which pronoun correctly completes: \'_____ is calling?\'', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Whom\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Whose\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Who\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Which\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Use \'who\' here because you can substitute \'he/she\' (He is calling). \'Who\' is the subjective case.', 'If the pronoun is the subject of the verb, use \'who\'.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"pronouns\\\",\\\"who vs whom\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1690, '311731e6-c665-4c1e-a819-cb9a180755bc', 145, 4, 'Which of the following is a demonstrative pronoun?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"anyone\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"each other\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"that\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"whom\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'That\' is a demonstrative pronoun that points to a specific noun.', 'Demonstrative pronouns point to specific things: this, that, these, those.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"pronouns\\\",\\\"demonstrative pronoun\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1691, 'bdacbabe-1bab-42af-9d6f-86ee95125a0e', 145, 4, 'Which sentence uses the correct pronoun case?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Between you and I, this is wrong.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Between you and me, this is wrong.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Between you and he, this is wrong.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Between you and she, this is wrong.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'After a preposition like \'between\', always use the objective case: me, him, her, us, them — not I, he, she, we.', 'Any pronoun following a preposition must be in the objective case.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"pronouns\\\",\\\"objective case\\\",\\\"prepositions\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1692, 'b055ec95-35ff-4055-953c-d5c09d66e21d', 145, 4, 'Which sentence is grammatically correct regarding indefinite pronouns?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Everyone are ready for the test.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Nobody were present.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Each of the students have submitted.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Everyone is ready for the test.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'Indefinite pronouns like \'everyone\', \'nobody\', \'each\', \'either\' are always singular and take a singular verb.', 'Everyone, nobody, each, either, neither — all are singular.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"pronouns\\\",\\\"indefinite pronoun\\\",\\\"subject-verb agreement\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1693, 'f55fdee8-53c0-48ec-8487-af8db4aa8e37', 145, 4, 'Which pronoun correctly completes: \'_____ did you call last night?\'', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Who\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Whose\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Whom\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Which\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Use \'whom\' because you can substitute \'him\' (You called him). \'Whom\' is the objective case.', 'If you can replace with him/her, use \'whom\'.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"pronouns\\\",\\\"who vs whom\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1694, '6312c3d0-cb70-4aa6-8ed5-18d5d4e68e07', 145, 4, 'In \'The students helped each other with homework,\' what type of pronoun is \'each other\'?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Reflexive pronoun\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Reciprocal pronoun\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Indefinite pronoun\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Relative pronoun\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', '\'Each other\' is a reciprocal pronoun — it expresses a mutual relationship between two or more people.', 'Reciprocal pronouns express a mutual action: each other, one another.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"pronouns\\\",\\\"reciprocal pronoun\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1695, 'f4acf937-d46f-4b9e-b573-8c7414c6ee1a', 145, 4, 'What is the comparative degree of \'good\'?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"gooder\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"more good\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"better\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"best\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'Good\' is an irregular adjective. Its comparative form is \'better\', not \'gooder\' or \'more good\'.', 'Good → better → best is an irregular pattern.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"adjectives\\\",\\\"degrees of comparison\\\",\\\"irregular adjectives\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1696, 'd77d6882-87b7-4695-8ebd-28d601483897', 145, 4, 'Which sentence uses a possessive adjective?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"This book is mine.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"My bag is on the table.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"That is her.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Which pen is yours?\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', '\'My\' in \'My bag\' is a possessive adjective — it shows ownership and is always followed by a noun.', 'Possessive adjectives always come before a noun: my, your, his, her, our, their.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"adjectives\\\",\\\"possessive adjective\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1697, 'f64b3292-fa65-4828-a504-21127875ca48', 145, 4, 'Which of the following is a proper adjective?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"tall\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"beautiful\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Pakistani\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"honest\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'Pakistani\' is a proper adjective derived from the proper noun \'Pakistan\'. Proper adjectives are always capitalised.', 'Proper adjectives are derived from proper nouns and are capitalised.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"adjectives\\\",\\\"proper adjective\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1698, '16041cf6-34f0-4c3a-901c-52bb39abd840', 145, 4, 'Which sentence contains a double comparative error?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"She is taller than her sister.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"He is the greatest leader.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"She is more taller than her sister.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"This is the most difficult test.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'More taller\' is a double comparative — using both -er and \'more\' together is grammatically incorrect. The correct form is simply \'taller\'.', 'Never combine -er with \'more\', or -est with \'most\'.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"adjectives\\\",\\\"degrees of comparison\\\",\\\"common errors\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1699, '15acc6db-6a75-4fc5-8592-ca8869936248', 145, 4, 'Which adjective cannot be compared because it is an absolute adjective?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"tall\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"unique\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"cold\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"heavy\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', '\'Unique\' is an absolute adjective — it already expresses a maximum quality. Saying \'more unique\' is incorrect.', 'Words like unique, perfect, dead, and round are absolute — they cannot be compared.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"adjectives\\\",\\\"absolute adjectives\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1700, 'ab16ca9b-fe6b-4682-b08b-0467a05079f7', 145, 4, 'What is the superlative degree of \'bad\'?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"baddest\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"most bad\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"worse\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"worst\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', '\'Bad\' is an irregular adjective: bad → worse → worst. \'Baddest\' and \'most bad\' are both incorrect.', 'Bad → worse → worst follows an irregular pattern.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"adjectives\\\",\\\"irregular adjectives\\\",\\\"degrees of comparison\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1701, '53a15515-fdf9-4b29-adf2-1506c0d7f052', 145, 4, 'Which sentence correctly uses the comparative degree?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"She is more intelligent than anyone in the class.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"She is more intelligent than anyone else in the class.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"She is the most intelligent than others.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"She is more intelligenter than her peers.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'When comparing a person with others in the same group using comparative degree, \'else\' must be added to avoid a logical error. \'Anyone else\' is correct.', 'When the subject is part of the group being compared, add \'else\' after indefinite pronouns.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"adjectives\\\",\\\"degrees of comparison\\\",\\\"common errors\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1702, '7edb304c-6caf-4885-a179-bb5a366bf940', 145, 4, 'Which of the following is a linking verb?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"run\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"write\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"seem\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"jump\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'Seem\' is a linking verb — it connects the subject to a word that describes it and expresses a state of being rather than an action.', 'Linking verbs express a state of being: is, seem, appear, become, feel, remain.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"verbs\\\",\\\"linking verbs\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1703, '6029ee39-3898-4160-b627-dfe584d97282', 145, 4, 'What is the past participle of \'go\'?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"went\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"going\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"gone\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"goed\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The past participle of \'go\' is \'gone\'. The forms are: go → went → gone.', '\'Gone\' is used with have/has/had: \'He has gone home.\'', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"verbs\\\",\\\"irregular verbs\\\",\\\"past participle\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1704, '75974d0b-0814-493b-8171-cbfefd113a3a', 145, 4, 'Which sentence uses an intransitive verb?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"She ate the apple.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"He signed the contract.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Birds fly.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"They built the house.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'Fly\' in \'Birds fly\' is intransitive — it does not require a direct object to complete its meaning.', 'Intransitive verbs do not need a direct object. The sentence is complete without one.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"verbs\\\",\\\"intransitive verbs\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1705, '599c9966-a1c6-4579-a86c-02a575b7bc1c', 145, 4, 'Which sentence is in the passive voice?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"The manager signed the contract.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The contract was signed by the manager.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"She is signing the contract.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"They will sign the contract.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'In passive voice, the subject receives the action. \'The contract was signed by the manager\' follows the formula: object + to be + past participle.', 'Passive voice: subject + to be + past participle.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"verbs\\\",\\\"active voice\\\",\\\"passive voice\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1706, '28eb91cb-3b7f-4723-b605-9cdff457903c', 145, 4, 'Which sentence contains an error in irregular verb usage?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"He has gone to the market.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"She has wrote the letter.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"They had spoken to the manager.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"We have taken the books.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', '\'Has wrote\' is incorrect. The past participle of \'write\' is \'written\'. The correct form is \'She has written the letter.\'', 'Write → wrote → written. Use \'written\' with has/have/had.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"verbs\\\",\\\"irregular verbs\\\",\\\"common errors\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1707, 'f498e7ba-8b4d-45ac-bf88-784d3e73b17c', 145, 4, 'Modal verbs are always followed by which form of the verb?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Past tense\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Present participle\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Base form (infinitive without \'to\')\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Past participle\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Modal verbs (can, could, may, might, shall, should, will, would, must) are always followed by the base form of the verb without \'to\'.', 'Can/could/will/would + base form: \'She can swim\', NOT \'She can swims\'.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"verbs\\\",\\\"modal verbs\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1708, '9933fae2-ee9d-43f3-860e-b3f0b429e454', 145, 4, 'Which sentence correctly uses \'lie\' vs \'lay\'?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"He lied the book on the table.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"She lay down on the sofa yesterday.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"They have lain the carpet yesterday.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"The hen laid an egg last week.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', '\'Lay\' means to place something. Past tense of \'lay\' is \'laid\'. So \'The hen laid an egg\' is correct.', '\'Lay\' (place) → laid → laid. \'Lie\' (recline) → lay → lain.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"verbs\\\",\\\"irregular verbs\\\",\\\"lay vs lie\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1709, '8a96c625-8f15-431e-94a3-4a69a6bc7e51', 145, 4, 'What type of adverb is \'always\' in \'He always arrives on time\'?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Adverb of time\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Adverb of place\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Adverb of degree\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Adverb of frequency\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', '\'Always\' answers the question \'How often?\' — making it an adverb of frequency.', 'Adverbs of frequency answer \'How often?\': always, never, often, sometimes.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"adverbs\\\",\\\"adverb of frequency\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1710, 'b747dac4-eef8-41bb-9c87-ea3c60a53aed', 145, 4, 'Which sentence is correct regarding adverb placement?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"He is never rude.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Never he is rude.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"He never is rude.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"He is rude never.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"1\\\"]\"', 'Adverbs of frequency come after auxiliary verbs and \'be\': \'He is never rude\' is correct.', 'Place frequency adverbs after \'be\' or auxiliary verbs.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"adverbs\\\",\\\"adverb placement\\\",\\\"adverb of frequency\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1711, '6502f93b-9c50-465b-a216-105ee5b09955', 145, 4, 'Which sentence contains a double negative error?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"I can hardly see anything.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"I can\'t hardly see anything.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"I can barely see anything.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"I can scarcely see anything.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', '\'Hardly\' already carries a negative meaning. Combining it with \'can\'t\' creates a double negative. The correct form is \'I can hardly see anything.\'', 'Hardly, scarcely, and barely are already negative — never combine them with \'not\' or \'n\'t\'.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"adverbs\\\",\\\"double negative\\\",\\\"common errors\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1712, 'd37ccfec-fb99-46d3-a8e2-784d8157cea2', 145, 4, 'Which is a conjunctive adverb?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"quickly\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"very\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"however\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"here\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'However\' is a conjunctive adverb — it connects two independent clauses. Other examples: therefore, moreover, consequently, furthermore.', 'Conjunctive adverbs connect clauses: however, therefore, moreover, nevertheless.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"adverbs\\\",\\\"conjunctive adverb\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1713, 'dbfa0950-8543-4063-b3fb-c635553e9a28', 145, 4, 'Which sentence correctly places an adverb of manner?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"She clearly speaks.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"She speaks clearly.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Clearly she speaks fast.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"She speaks clear.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Adverbs of manner come after the verb or after the object: \'She speaks clearly.\' Placing it before the verb (option a) is less natural and changes emphasis.', 'Adverbs of manner usually follow the verb or object.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"adverbs\\\",\\\"adverb of manner\\\",\\\"placement\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1714, '0693bf1f-cfbc-480f-907d-9b6c3bcf15de', 145, 4, 'Which sentence uses \'only\' in the correct position to mean \'she told me nothing but the truth\'?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"She only told me the truth.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Only she told me the truth.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"She told me only the truth.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"She told only me the truth.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Placing \'only\' immediately before \'the truth\' emphasises what she told — that it was nothing but the truth. Other placements change the meaning.', '\'Only\' should be placed immediately before the word it modifies.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"adverbs\\\",\\\"misplaced adverb\\\",\\\"only\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1715, 'd263d5ce-5501-4c38-a36a-64c1dd6353da', 145, 4, 'Which preposition correctly completes: \'The meeting is _____ Monday\'?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"in\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"at\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"on\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"by\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Use \'on\' for days and specific dates: on Monday, on 5th May, on my birthday.', 'ON is used for days and specific dates.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"prepositions\\\",\\\"at on in\\\",\\\"time prepositions\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '6', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1716, '7108cfc8-2c7e-4c52-863e-38f14db5baa8', 145, 4, 'Which preposition correctly completes: \'She has been living here _____ 2019\'?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"for\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"during\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"since\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"by\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'Since\' is used with a specific point in time (2019). \'For\' is used with a duration (three years).', 'Since = specific point in time. For = duration of time.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"prepositions\\\",\\\"since vs for\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '6', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1717, 'e6a9b430-038a-4185-a113-786dd175f561', 145, 4, 'Which sentence uses the correct preposition?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"He is good in mathematics.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"He is good at mathematics.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"He is good on mathematics.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"He is good for mathematics.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The correct expression is \'good at\' — not \'good in\'. This is a fixed preposition collocation.', 'Good at — not good in, good on, or good for.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"prepositions\\\",\\\"common preposition errors\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '6', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1719, '8c8de63d-b70e-48d8-8b30-87c9555d5bf7', 145, 4, 'Which sentence uses the preposition correctly regarding date?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"The accident happened at 5th April.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The accident happened in 5th April.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The accident happened on 5th April.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"The accident happened by 5th April.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Use \'on\' for specific dates. \'On 5th April\' is correct.', 'ON is used for specific calendar dates.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"prepositions\\\",\\\"at on in\\\",\\\"dates\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '6', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1720, '8078717d-36a1-493a-8c05-2be15f2eb283', 145, 4, 'Which preposition correctly completes: \'He is senior _____ me in the department\'?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"than\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"from\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"over\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"to\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'The correct expression is \'senior to\'. \'Senior than\' is a very common but incorrect usage.', 'Senior to, junior to, inferior to, superior to — these words take \'to\' not \'than\'.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"prepositions\\\",\\\"common preposition errors\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '6', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1721, '49cfbf0a-2ff1-4d7b-9789-129244ba3618', 145, 4, 'Which preposition is used for an enclosed space?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"on\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"at\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"in\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"by\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'In\' is used for an enclosed space or area: in the room, in the box, in Pakistan.', 'IN = enclosed space. ON = surface. AT = specific point.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"prepositions\\\",\\\"at on in\\\",\\\"place prepositions\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '6', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1722, 'ef4d7513-9bb2-4540-a95a-2dcd5ab4bebe', 145, 4, 'What does the acronym FANBOYS represent in grammar?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Subordinating conjunctions\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Coordinating conjunctions\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Correlative conjunctions\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Conjunctive adverbs\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'FANBOYS stands for For, And, Nor, But, Or, Yet, So — the seven coordinating conjunctions.', 'FANBOYS = For And Nor But Or Yet So.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"conjunctions\\\",\\\"coordinating conjunctions\\\",\\\"FANBOYS\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '7', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1723, '4ba87196-8a1d-4b2a-9770-49a51540b71f', 145, 4, 'Which of the following is a subordinating conjunction?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"but\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"or\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"although\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"and\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'Although\' is a subordinating conjunction — it introduces a dependent (subordinate) clause.', 'Subordinating conjunctions: because, although, since, unless, while, if, when.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"conjunctions\\\",\\\"subordinating conjunctions\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '7', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1724, '7f53fe46-52f3-4b7a-8f4f-5e5c5d68bb89', 145, 4, 'Which sentence correctly uses a correlative conjunction?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Either he goes, and I go.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Neither Ali or Sana attended.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Not only did she win, but she also broke the record.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Both the teacher or the student agreed.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'Not only … but also\' is a correct correlative pair. \'Either … or\', \'Neither … nor\', and \'Both … and\' are the other correct pairs.', 'Correlative conjunctions work in pairs: not only…but also, either…or, neither…nor.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"conjunctions\\\",\\\"correlative conjunctions\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '7', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1725, '204b08e8-4f59-4dda-ba7b-727ecf65ff2d', 145, 4, 'Which sentence correctly applies the comma rule for coordinating conjunctions?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"He studied hard, and passed the exam.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"He studied hard and, passed the exam.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"He studied hard and passed the exam.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"He, studied hard and passed the exam.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'When \'and\' joins two verbs (not two independent clauses) sharing the same subject, no comma is needed. \'He studied hard and passed the exam\' is one clause with two verbs.', 'Comma before coordinating conjunction only when joining two independent clauses.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"conjunctions\\\",\\\"coordinating conjunctions\\\",\\\"comma usage\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '7', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26');
INSERT INTO `mcqs` (`id`, `uuid`, `topic_id`, `subject_id`, `question`, `question_type`, `options`, `correct_answers`, `explanation`, `hint`, `difficulty_level`, `time_limit_seconds`, `marks`, `negative_marks`, `tags`, `reference_book`, `reference_page`, `is_premium`, `is_verified`, `status`, `created_by`, `approved_by`, `approved_at`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(1726, '04537623-555b-4ac4-9cf2-ab0a94828cad', 145, 4, 'Which sentence correctly uses subject-verb agreement with a correlative conjunction?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Neither the students nor the teacher were present.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Neither the students nor the teacher was present.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Neither the teacher nor the students was present.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Neither the teacher nor the students has been present.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'With neither…nor, the verb agrees with the noun closest to it. \'Teacher\' (singular) is closest, so use \'was\'.', 'Neither…nor: verb agrees with the noun closest to it.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"conjunctions\\\",\\\"correlative conjunctions\\\",\\\"subject-verb agreement\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '7', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1727, '8ae04212-7091-4aaf-ad47-0b559aa8805e', 145, 4, 'In \'No sooner had he left than it started raining,\' what type of conjunction pair is used?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Coordinating conjunction\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Subordinating conjunction\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Correlative conjunction\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Conjunctive adverb\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'No sooner … than\' is a correlative conjunction pair — they always work together.', 'Correlative conjunctions always work in fixed pairs: no sooner…than is one such pair.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"conjunctions\\\",\\\"correlative conjunctions\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '7', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1728, '8b2905e4-6f54-4279-a8c8-cfab28f86fa8', 145, 4, 'Which of the following is an interjection?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"quickly\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Alas\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"because\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"their\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', '\'Alas\' is an interjection expressing sorrow or regret. It has no grammatical role in the sentence.', 'Interjections express emotion: Alas! Bravo! Ouch! Hurray!', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"interjections\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '8', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1729, 'f90ca4de-c8bb-40b1-81a1-67a08c6e2e43', 145, 4, 'Which punctuation mark follows an interjection expressing strong emotion?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Comma (,)\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Full stop (.)\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Exclamation mark (!)\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Semicolon (;)\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Strong emotion is followed by an exclamation mark (!). Mild emotion uses a comma. Example: \'Hurray! We won!\'', 'Strong emotion = ! | Mild emotion = ,', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"interjections\\\",\\\"punctuation\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '8', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1730, 'dc264b27-3d2d-4891-a41b-789949e345f9', 145, 4, 'Which interjection is used to express pain?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Bravo\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Alas\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Ouch\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Hurray\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'Ouch\' expresses pain or discomfort. \'Bravo\' = approval, \'Alas\' = sorrow, \'Hurray\' = joy.', 'Match the interjection to the emotion it expresses.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"interjections\\\",\\\"types of interjections\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '8', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1731, '0f57fbc1-902d-4fde-9b07-73ff9823c830', 145, 4, 'What is the grammatical role of an interjection in a sentence?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"It modifies the verb.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"It joins two clauses.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"It has no grammatical connection to the rest of the sentence.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"It names the subject.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'An interjection has no grammatical connection to the rest of the sentence. It can be removed without affecting the sentence structure.', 'Interjections express emotion only — they play no grammatical role.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"interjections\\\",\\\"definition\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '8', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1732, '89172d6f-40ed-4395-89e2-31806e3d35e7', 145, 4, 'Which article is used before a vowel sound?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"a\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"the\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"an\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"some\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'An\' is used before a vowel sound: an apple, an hour, an honest man.', 'Article selection depends on sound, not spelling.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"determiners\\\",\\\"articles\\\",\\\"a vs an\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '9', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1733, 'f7579a5f-5760-47cf-b253-acfb9c17a30c', 145, 4, 'Which sentence correctly uses the article \'a\' or \'an\'?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"She is an university student.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"He is a honest man.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"She is a university student.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"He is an unique idea.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'University\' begins with a /j/ consonant sound, so \'a\' is correct. \'An university\' is wrong.', 'University starts with a consonant sound /j/ — use \'a\'.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"determiners\\\",\\\"articles\\\",\\\"a vs an\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '9', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1734, '3e4b4654-cfbb-4838-b375-764c31922b4c', 145, 4, 'What is the difference between \'few\' and \'a few\'?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Both have the same meaning.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"\'Few\' is positive; \'a few\' is negative.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"\'Few\' implies scarcity (negative); \'a few\' implies a small but sufficient number (positive).\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"\'A few\' is used only with uncountable nouns.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'Few students passed\' (most failed — negative meaning). \'A few students passed\' (at least some — positive meaning).', 'Few = barely any (negative). A few = some (positive).', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"determiners\\\",\\\"quantifiers\\\",\\\"few vs a few\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '9', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1735, 'd43f4228-8370-4325-87a7-8b04a07294df', 145, 4, 'Which sentence correctly uses the definite article?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"The honesty is the best policy.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Honesty is the best policy.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"An honesty is the best policy.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"A honesty is the best policy.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Abstract nouns used in a general sense take no article. \'Honesty is the best policy\' is correct — no article before \'honesty\'.', 'Abstract nouns used generally take no article.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"determiners\\\",\\\"articles\\\",\\\"abstract nouns\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '9', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1736, '05a5d33a-7dbc-45e4-96df-e976cd150250', 145, 4, 'Which sentence requires the definite article \'the\'?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"She is best student in the class.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"She is a best student in the class.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"She is the best student in the class.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"She is an best student in the class.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Superlative adjectives always require \'the\': the best, the tallest, the most intelligent.', 'Superlatives always use \'the\'.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"determiners\\\",\\\"articles\\\",\\\"superlative\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '9', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1737, '9df1c869-bac5-440d-927b-c466b4b99ec7', 145, 4, 'Which of the following is a distributive determiner?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"some\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"many\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"every\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"several\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'Every\' is a distributive determiner — it refers to members of a group individually. Others include: each, either, neither.', 'Distributive determiners: each, every, either, neither.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"determiners\\\",\\\"distributive determiners\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '9', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1738, '858176ac-b693-4e10-b2eb-0591d5b155d8', 145, 4, 'Which sentence uses \'little\' vs \'a little\' correctly?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"There is little hope \\\\u2014 so we should try.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"There is a little hope \\\\u2014 so we should not try.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"There is a little hope \\\\u2014 so we should keep trying.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"There is little hope \\\\u2014 so we can still succeed.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'A little hope\' has a positive meaning (some hope remains), which logically leads to \'we should keep trying\'.', 'A little = some (positive). Little = barely any (negative).', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"determiners\\\",\\\"quantifiers\\\",\\\"little vs a little\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '9', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1739, '21ce939b-b3a1-4f75-95cf-5791e8e92b21', 145, 4, 'Which sentence correctly uses the article with a unique noun?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"A sun rises in the east.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Sun rises in the east.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The sun rises in the east.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"An sun rises in the east.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Unique things — things of which there is only one — always take \'the\': the sun, the moon, the sky, the Internet.', 'Unique things take \'the\': the sun, the moon, the sky.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"determiners\\\",\\\"articles\\\",\\\"unique nouns\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '9', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 10:37:26', '2026-05-13 10:37:26'),
(1740, '38473425-4503-4834-94c5-0324f618cea2', 144, 4, 'Which sentence is in the Simple Present Tense?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"She was writing a letter.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"She writes a letter every day.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"She will write a letter.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"She has written a letter.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', '\'She writes a letter every day\' describes a habitual action — the defining use of the simple present tense.', 'Simple present describes habits, routines, and general truths.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"simple present\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1741, '9bd7ee35-1477-4c11-936d-bbcba5fa3310', 144, 4, 'Choose the correct form: \'She _____ to school every day.\'', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"go\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"going\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"goes\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"gone\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'With third person singular subjects (he/she/it), add -s or -es to the verb. \'Go\' becomes \'goes\'.', 'He/She/It → add -s or -es to the verb in simple present.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"simple present\\\",\\\"third person singular\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1742, 'a8a55867-39ac-496f-a1f0-a5ed0bfb043c', 144, 4, 'Which time expression is most commonly used with the Simple Present Tense?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"yesterday\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"by next year\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"every day\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"at this moment\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'Every day\' is a classic signal word for the simple present, indicating a habitual or routine action.', 'Signal words for simple present: always, usually, every day, often, never.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"simple present\\\",\\\"signal words\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1743, '58dbf3ec-2ae6-446f-991b-fcdbc17b8e61', 144, 4, 'Which sentence correctly uses simple present for a universal truth?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"The sun was rising in the east.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The sun rises in the east.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The sun has risen in the east.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"The sun is rising in the east.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Universal truths and scientific facts always use the simple present tense regardless of context.', 'Scientific facts and universal truths always use simple present, even in a past context.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"simple present\\\",\\\"universal truth\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1744, '45942985-4100-470a-aaf7-381ecb5a0a70', 144, 4, 'Which sentence contains an error in simple present tense?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"He doesn\'t like spicy food.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"She studies every night.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"He don\'t like spicy food.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Water boils at 100\\\\u00b0C.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'He don\'t like\' is incorrect. With he/she/it, the negative is \'doesn\'t\' + base form: \'He doesn\'t like\'.', 'He/She/It → use \'doesn\'t\' for negation, not \'don\'t\'.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"simple present\\\",\\\"negation\\\",\\\"common errors\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1745, 'ed0b524d-09ba-44eb-8d5b-e5429260fe91', 144, 4, 'Scientists discovered that water _____ at 100°C. Which form is correct?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"boiled\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"had boiled\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"boils\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"was boiling\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Scientific facts use the simple present even when the main clause is in the past. \'Boils\' is correct here.', 'Universal truths and scientific facts do not backshift — always use simple present.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"simple present\\\",\\\"scientific fact\\\",\\\"tense consistency\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1746, 'd9f3f768-781a-478a-9530-0caf7ba8d05f', 144, 4, 'What is the structure of the Present Continuous Tense?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Subject + had + V3\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Subject + will + V\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Subject + is\\\\\\/am\\\\\\/are + V-ing\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Subject + V2\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Present continuous = subject + is/am/are + verb-ing. It describes ongoing actions at the moment of speaking.', 'Present continuous always uses is/am/are + verb-ing.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"present continuous\\\",\\\"structure\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1747, '29aa7874-d48d-498f-97c9-4f7ceb44078f', 144, 4, 'Which sentence is in the Present Continuous Tense?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"She reads every night.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"She is reading a novel right now.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"She has read the novel.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"She read the novel.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', '\'She is reading a novel right now\' uses is + verb-ing, showing an action in progress at this moment.', 'Look for is/am/are + verb-ing to identify present continuous.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"present continuous\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1748, '57f6d2a3-6ab6-42da-a8d3-00f950fef804', 144, 4, 'Which sentence contains an error related to stative verbs?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"She knows the answer.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"I am knowing the answer.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"He wants to leave.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"They believe in honesty.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', '\'Know\' is a stative verb — it expresses a mental state and cannot be used in the continuous form. \'I am knowing\' is incorrect.', 'Stative verbs (know, believe, want, own) cannot be used in continuous tenses.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"present continuous\\\",\\\"stative verbs\\\",\\\"common errors\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1749, '56e96152-08fa-4e4c-875d-36d3fc9b7750', 144, 4, 'Which of the following is a stative verb that CANNOT be used in continuous form?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"run\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"write\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"own\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"sleep\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'Own\' is a stative verb expressing possession. It cannot be used in the continuous form: \'He is owning a car\' is wrong.', 'Possession verbs (own, have, possess, belong) are stative — no continuous form.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"present continuous\\\",\\\"stative verbs\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1750, 'b7a6f4b4-5816-42b8-8779-a0b9150f535d', 144, 4, 'Which sentence correctly uses present continuous to express a future arrangement?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"She will meet the director tomorrow.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"She meets the director tomorrow.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"She is meeting the director tomorrow.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"She has met the director tomorrow.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Present continuous can express a definite planned future arrangement. \'She is meeting the director tomorrow\' implies a fixed plan.', 'Present continuous + future time expression = definite personal arrangement.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"present continuous\\\",\\\"future arrangement\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '2', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1751, 'fe656af3-2d76-41a7-b58c-7a7f1b15f5ab', 144, 4, 'Which sentence is in the Present Perfect Tense?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"She visited Dubai last year.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"She has visited Dubai.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"She visits Dubai often.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"She was visiting Dubai.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', '\'She has visited Dubai\' uses has + past participle, which is the structure of the present perfect tense.', 'Present perfect = has/have + past participle (V3).', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"present perfect\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1752, 'bfa4543b-77ef-41f4-ae34-296ef9303816', 144, 4, 'Which word is the correct signal for Present Perfect Tense?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"yesterday\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"last year\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"already\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"at that time\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'Already\' is a classic signal word for the present perfect. \'Yesterday\' and \'last year\' signal simple past.', 'Present perfect signals: just, already, yet, ever, never, recently, since, for.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"present perfect\\\",\\\"signal words\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1753, '2d6e3e53-08e6-466a-9564-f064e085fea4', 144, 4, 'Which sentence correctly uses \'since\' vs \'for\'?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"I have lived here since ten years.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"I have lived here for 2015.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"I have lived here for ten years.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"I have lived here since a long time.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'For\' is used with a duration (ten years). \'Since\' is used with a specific point in time (since 2015).', 'Since = specific point (since 2015). For = duration (for ten years).', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"present perfect\\\",\\\"since vs for\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1754, '1b0c1f7a-085d-458d-9fff-6e07b839bd60', 144, 4, 'Which sentence contains an error mixing present perfect and simple past?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"I saw him yesterday.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"She has already finished.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"I have seen him yesterday.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"They have just arrived.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'Yesterday\' is a specific completed time — it must use simple past: \'I saw him yesterday\', not \'I have seen him yesterday\'.', 'Specific time expressions (yesterday, last year, in 2010) require simple past, not present perfect.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"present perfect\\\",\\\"simple past\\\",\\\"common errors\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1755, '3e663ce6-6483-427d-ac9d-743d9bf0e7ef', 144, 4, 'Which sentence correctly uses \'yet\' in the present perfect?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"I have yet finished the work.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"I haven\'t finished yet.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"I haven\'t finished already.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"I have finished yet.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', '\'Yet\' is used in negatives and questions: \'I haven\'t finished yet.\' \'Already\' is used in affirmatives.', 'Yet = negatives and questions. Already = affirmatives.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"present perfect\\\",\\\"yet vs already\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1756, 'e87a649f-e9ea-4304-9eaa-cc5203c528f0', 144, 4, 'Which sentence correctly uses the present perfect for an incomplete time period?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"I wrote three reports today.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"I have written three reports today.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"I had written three reports today.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"I was writing three reports today.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', '\'Today\' is an incomplete time period (the day is not yet over), so present perfect is correct: \'I have written three reports today.\'', 'Incomplete time periods (today, this week, this year) take the present perfect.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"present perfect\\\",\\\"incomplete time\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '3', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1757, '64d77bdc-ea7b-46a9-ab2c-58db592bba50', 144, 4, 'What is the structure of the Present Perfect Continuous Tense?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Subject + had + been + V-ing\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Subject + has\\\\\\/have + been + V-ing\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Subject + is\\\\\\/am\\\\\\/are + been + V-ing\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Subject + will + have + V-ing\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Present perfect continuous = has/have + been + verb-ing. It emphasizes the ongoing duration of an action up to now.', 'Present perfect continuous: has/have + been + V-ing.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"present perfect continuous\\\",\\\"structure\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1758, 'e8cda342-efba-460c-abd0-688fa951245a', 144, 4, 'Which sentence correctly uses the Present Perfect Continuous?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"She has worked here since 2018.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"She is working here since 2018.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"She has been working here since 2018.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"She was working here since 2018.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'Has been working since 2018\' shows an action that started in the past and is still continuing — the key use of present perfect continuous.', 'Ongoing action from past to present with since/for → present perfect continuous.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"present perfect continuous\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1759, '75ab6cdd-5ac9-4aa6-b9f7-9ae4eca6af07', 144, 4, 'What is the difference in focus between \'I have written the report\' and \'I have been writing the report\'?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"No difference \\\\u2014 both mean the same.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The first focuses on the result; the second focuses on the duration.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The first is more formal.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"The second is incorrect.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Present perfect focuses on the completed result. Present perfect continuous focuses on the ongoing process and duration.', 'Perfect = result/completion. Perfect continuous = ongoing process/duration.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"present perfect\\\",\\\"present perfect continuous\\\",\\\"comparison\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1760, '689c507a-ebbe-4d97-bfe0-ffe8ce46d9d8', 144, 4, 'Which sentence correctly handles a stative verb in the present perfect continuous context?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"She has been knowing him for years.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"She has been knowing him since childhood.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"She has known him for years.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"She is knowing him for years.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'Know\' is a stative verb — it cannot be used in any continuous form. Even for duration, use present perfect: \'She has known him for years.\'', 'With stative verbs (know, like, love, believe), use present perfect — not present perfect continuous.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"present perfect continuous\\\",\\\"stative verbs\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '4', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1761, 'ad44108c-9ed5-4610-9502-fbba0aeba5e8', 144, 4, 'What is the past form of the verb \'go\'?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"goed\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"gone\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"going\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"went\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', '\'Go\' is an irregular verb. Its simple past form is \'went\'. \'Gone\' is the past participle used with has/have/had.', 'Go → went → gone. Simple past = went.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"simple past\\\",\\\"irregular verbs\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1762, '9e951eec-2dab-412c-9316-c797ef375944', 144, 4, 'Which time expression signals the Simple Past Tense?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"just\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"already\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"yesterday\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"since\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'Yesterday\' is a completed, specific time — the defining signal for the simple past tense.', 'Simple past signals: yesterday, ago, last week, last year, in 2010.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"simple past\\\",\\\"signal words\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1763, '366829c7-8156-48a2-9b41-f0de9a3f0c59', 144, 4, 'Which sentence is correct in the Simple Past Tense?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"She didn\'t went to the market.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"She didn\'t go to the market.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"She doesn\'t went to the market.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"She hasn\'t went to the market.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'After \'did\' in negatives/questions, always use the base form: \'didn\'t go\', not \'didn\'t went\'.', 'Did + NOT + base form (never past form).', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"simple past\\\",\\\"negation\\\",\\\"common errors\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1764, '4803a4f6-b690-4830-bd2b-5011ccb8ef18', 144, 4, 'What is the past form of the verb \'buy\'?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"buyed\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"bought\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"buyed\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"buied\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', '\'Buy\' is irregular. Its past form is \'bought\'. Common pattern: buy→bought, think→thought, catch→caught, teach→taught.', 'Buy → bought. Think → thought. These are irregular past forms.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"simple past\\\",\\\"irregular verbs\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1765, '78d26803-9c00-4b23-b6c7-402215229c62', 144, 4, 'Which sentence contains an error mixing Simple Past and Present Perfect?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"She submitted the report yesterday.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"He has submitted the form yesterday.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"They finished the project last week.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"She went to the market.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', '\'Yesterday\' is a specific past time — present perfect cannot be used with it. Correct: \'He submitted the form yesterday.\'', 'Specific completed time (yesterday, last year) = simple past only.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"simple past\\\",\\\"present perfect\\\",\\\"common errors\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1766, 'b72ea568-be84-4bcc-bf14-d094a6e36900', 144, 4, 'Which pair shows correctly a base form and its simple past?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"speak \\\\u2192 speaked\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"rise \\\\u2192 rose\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"begin \\\\u2192 beginned\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"teach \\\\u2192 teached\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Rise → rose is correct. Speak → spoke, Begin → began, Teach → taught are the correct irregular forms.', 'Rise → rose → risen. These are commonly tested irregular verbs.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"simple past\\\",\\\"irregular verbs\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '5', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1767, '31878f1f-6d00-4b16-8c71-d9bec7573661', 144, 4, 'What is the structure of the Past Continuous Tense?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Subject + had + V3\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Subject + was\\\\\\/were + V-ing\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Subject + is\\\\\\/am\\\\\\/are + V-ing\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Subject + did + V\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Past continuous = was/were + verb-ing. It describes an ongoing action at a specific past time.', 'Past continuous: was/were + verb-ing.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"past continuous\\\",\\\"structure\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '6', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1768, '1a547b51-102d-4bfa-88f5-c68f7fb2be7c', 144, 4, 'Which sentence correctly uses the Past Continuous?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"I cooked dinner when the phone rang.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"I was cooking dinner when the phone rang.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"I had cooked dinner when the phone rang.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"I cook dinner when the phone rang.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'The longer background action (cooking) uses past continuous; the shorter interruption (phone rang) uses simple past.', 'Longer background action = past continuous. Short interruption = simple past.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"past continuous\\\",\\\"interruption\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '6', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1769, 'd02f97f9-d881-440c-975b-11f704048e4c', 144, 4, 'When is \'while\' used versus \'when\' in past continuous sentences?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"\'While\' goes with the short interruption; \'when\' with the ongoing action.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"\'While\' goes with the ongoing background action; \'when\' with the short interruption.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Both are interchangeable.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"\'While\' is only used in simple past.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', '\'While\' introduces the ongoing background action (past continuous). \'When\' introduces the shorter interrupting action (simple past).', 'While + past continuous (ongoing). When + simple past (interruption).', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"past continuous\\\",\\\"while vs when\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '6', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1770, '54371db6-8969-46c9-96c3-09165ea99152', 144, 4, 'Which sentence correctly uses the past continuous for two simultaneous actions?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"While she read, he wrote.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"While she was reading, he was writing.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"While she read, he was writing.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"While she was reading, he wrote.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Two simultaneous ongoing actions in the past → both use past continuous: \'was reading\' and \'was writing\'.', 'Two actions happening at the same time in the past → both use past continuous.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"past continuous\\\",\\\"simultaneous actions\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '6', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1771, 'e8db228a-0736-48df-8594-a5fa5795639f', 144, 4, 'Which sentence contains an error in the past continuous?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"I was studying when she arrived.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"While he was cooking, she was washing dishes.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"I was study when she arrived.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"At 8pm, they were watching TV.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'I was study\' is wrong — the verb must be in -ing form. Correct: \'I was studying when she arrived.\'', 'Past continuous requires was/were + verb-ing. \'Was study\' is incorrect.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"past continuous\\\",\\\"common errors\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '6', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1772, '9662fe4d-c33b-4962-97aa-3874f2570d79', 144, 4, 'What is the structure of the Past Perfect Tense?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Subject + was\\\\\\/were + V-ing\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Subject + had + V3\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Subject + have + V3\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Subject + did + V\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Past perfect = had + past participle (V3). It describes the earlier of two past actions.', 'Past perfect: had + V3. It is the \'past of the past\'.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"past perfect\\\",\\\"structure\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '7', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1773, '37ff9136-f515-4d82-97da-f82a908a69a3', 144, 4, 'Which sentence correctly uses the Past Perfect?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"When I reached the station, the train already left.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"When I reached the station, the train has already left.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"When I reached the station, the train had already left.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"When I reached the station, the train was already leaving.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The train leaving happened before I reached — so it takes the past perfect: \'had already left\'. The later action (reaching) takes simple past.', 'Earlier past action = past perfect (had + V3). Later past action = simple past.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"past perfect\\\",\\\"sequence of events\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '7', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1774, '20fd34cc-209c-4e25-a6a6-38eb78ec84e4', 144, 4, 'Which sentence uses the inverted structure with \'No sooner … than\' correctly?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"No sooner he had left than it started raining.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"No sooner had he left than it started raining.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"No sooner he left than it had started raining.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"No sooner did he leave than it had rained.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'With \'No sooner … than\', the auxiliary \'had\' is inverted before the subject: \'No sooner had he left than …\'', 'No sooner had + subject + V3 … than + simple past.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"past perfect\\\",\\\"no sooner than\\\",\\\"inversion\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '7', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1775, '946984bd-b180-4bae-8b52-361bf67689fb', 144, 4, 'Which signal word most strongly indicates the Past Perfect Tense is needed?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"yesterday\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"by the time\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"currently\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"soon\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', '\'By the time\' indicates an action completed before another past event — the strongest signal for the past perfect.', 'By the time = past perfect in the clause describing the earlier action.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"past perfect\\\",\\\"signal words\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '7', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1776, '837f223e-545a-4682-aaaf-82858efaece6', 144, 4, 'In which sentence is the Past Perfect used correctly in the third conditional?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"If he studied harder, he would have passed.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"If he had studied harder, he would have passed.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"If he has studied harder, he will pass.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"If he studied harder, he will pass.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Third conditional (unreal past): If + past perfect … would have + past participle. \'If he had studied harder, he would have passed.\'', 'Third conditional: If + had + V3 … would + have + V3.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"past perfect\\\",\\\"third conditional\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '7', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1777, 'e873acdc-3642-40e4-81c2-9b709d16df66', 144, 4, 'What is the structure of the Past Perfect Continuous Tense?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Subject + had + been + V-ing\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Subject + has\\\\\\/have + been + V-ing\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Subject + was\\\\\\/were + been + V-ing\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Subject + would + have + V-ing\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"1\\\"]\"', 'Past perfect continuous = had + been + verb-ing. It emphasizes the duration of an action up to a past point.', 'Past perfect continuous: had + been + V-ing.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"past perfect continuous\\\",\\\"structure\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '8', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1778, '3d409768-00cf-4e3a-95aa-86474aaab00d', 144, 4, 'Which sentence correctly uses the Past Perfect Continuous to explain a cause?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"He was tired because he worked all day.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"He was tired because he has been working all day.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"He was tired because he had been working all day.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"He was tired because he was working all day.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'The past state (tiredness) was caused by an ongoing past action. Past perfect continuous: \'had been working\' is correct.', 'Past result caused by an ongoing past action → past perfect continuous.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"past perfect continuous\\\",\\\"cause and effect\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '8', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1779, 'bb8b5746-a011-4b76-a75e-61068096a1f7', 144, 4, 'What does Past Perfect Continuous emphasize compared to Past Perfect?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Completion of the action\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The specific time of the action\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The ongoing duration before a past point\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"The frequency of the action\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Past perfect continuous emphasizes how long an action had been going on before a past moment, not the result.', 'Past perfect continuous = duration. Past perfect = completion.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"past perfect continuous\\\",\\\"past perfect\\\",\\\"comparison\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '8', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1780, '7f6bf1d5-c5a3-4355-b4a2-2eb26a6ece2c', 144, 4, 'Which sentence contains a stative verb error in the Past Perfect Continuous context?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"They had known each other for years before they married.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"They had been knowing each other for years before they married.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"She had been waiting for an hour before he arrived.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"He had been studying all night when she called.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', '\'Know\' is a stative verb — it cannot be used in any continuous form. \'Had been knowing\' is wrong. Correct: \'had known\'.', 'Stative verbs (know, believe, love, own) cannot be used in continuous forms — ever.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"past perfect continuous\\\",\\\"stative verbs\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '8', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1781, 'f870aa42-2d7a-4838-8ef6-4e75ed6adfd2', 144, 4, 'Which structure expresses a spontaneous future decision?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"She is going to answer the phone.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"She will answer the phone.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"She answers the phone.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"She has answered the phone.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', '\'Will\' is used for spontaneous decisions made at the moment of speaking, as opposed to \'going to\' which is for pre-planned intentions.', 'Will = spontaneous decision. Going to = pre-planned intention.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"simple future\\\",\\\"will vs going to\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '9', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1782, 'f84c6068-785d-4e42-a390-77a613b6c642', 144, 4, 'Which sentence uses \'be going to\' correctly for a prediction based on evidence?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"I think she will win.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Look at those clouds \\\\u2014 it is going to rain.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"I will go to the market tomorrow.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"She will be a great leader.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', '\'Going to\' is used for predictions based on visible present evidence (the clouds). \'Will\' is for predictions based on opinion with no evidence.', 'Going to = prediction based on evidence. Will = prediction based on opinion.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"simple future\\\",\\\"will vs going to\\\",\\\"prediction\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '9', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1783, 'cf9aa151-7bde-45d2-bf62-f874cbf5524f', 144, 4, 'Which sentence contains an error in a conditional sentence with future tense?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"If it rains, we will cancel the trip.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"If she studies, she will pass.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"If it will rain, we will cancel the trip.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"If he works hard, he will succeed.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'In conditional and time clauses starting with \'if\', never use \'will\'. Use simple present in the if-clause: \'If it rains, we will cancel the trip.\'', 'If-clause + future → use simple present in the if-clause, not will.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"simple future\\\",\\\"conditionals\\\",\\\"if-clause\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '9', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1784, '54a555d1-3f26-4cd8-91f1-85c8b2b01f81', 144, 4, 'Which tense expresses a scheduled or timetabled future event?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Future continuous\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Future perfect\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Simple present\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Present perfect\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Simple present can express future scheduled/timetabled events: \'The train leaves at 6pm.\' \'The exam starts at 9am.\'', 'Timetabled or scheduled events use simple present for the future.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"simple future\\\",\\\"simple present\\\",\\\"timetables\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '9', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1785, 'a08a4215-f72b-464b-ae56-5b47b7d22f5c', 144, 4, 'Which sentence contains an error in a future time clause?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"When she arrives, I will call you.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"As soon as he leaves, we will start.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Until they will decide, we will wait.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Before she comes, I will prepare.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'After time conjunctions (when, as soon as, before, after, until, unless), never use \'will\'. Use simple present: \'Until they decide, we will wait.\'', 'Time clauses (when, until, before, after, unless) + future → use simple present.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"simple future\\\",\\\"time clauses\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '9', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1786, '7a0c3cde-9c68-4363-b139-51afaf49e5b7', 144, 4, 'What is the structure of the Future Continuous Tense?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Subject + will + have + V3\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Subject + will + be + V-ing\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Subject + is\\\\\\/am\\\\\\/are + going to + V\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Subject + will + have + been + V-ing\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Future continuous = will + be + verb-ing. It describes an action in progress at a specific future time.', 'Future continuous: will + be + V-ing.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"future continuous\\\",\\\"structure\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '10', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1787, '197226f6-e41d-43ef-8591-6dc4ddaf9428', 144, 4, 'Which sentence correctly uses the Future Continuous?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"At 9am tomorrow, I will sit in my exam.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"At 9am tomorrow, I will be sitting in my exam.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"At 9am tomorrow, I will have sat in my exam.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"At 9am tomorrow, I am sitting in my exam.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'A specific future time + an action in progress at that time → future continuous. \'I will be sitting\' is correct.', 'Specific future time + action in progress at that time = future continuous.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"future continuous\\\",\\\"ongoing action\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '10', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1788, 'c989be58-e29f-4590-88e5-0aa41cada0e6', 144, 4, 'What is the key difference in signal words between Future Continuous and Future Perfect?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"\'At\' signals future perfect; \'by\' signals future continuous.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"\'At\' (ongoing at a point) signals future continuous; \'by\' (completed before a point) signals future perfect.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Both use \'by\' as a signal.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Both use \'at\' as a signal.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', '\'At 6pm\' → action in progress → future continuous. \'By 6pm\' → action completed before 6pm → future perfect.', 'At = in progress at that time (continuous). By = completed before that time (perfect).', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"future continuous\\\",\\\"future perfect\\\",\\\"signal words\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '10', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1789, '9cbbd167-dcff-4d3f-9526-f30ba96a070c', 144, 4, 'Which sentence correctly uses Future Continuous to politely ask about plans?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Will you use the car tonight?\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Are you using the car tonight?\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Will you be using the car tonight?\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Did you use the car tonight?\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Future continuous is used to politely ask about someone\'s plans without implying interference: \'Will you be using the car tonight?\'', 'Future continuous = polite way to ask about plans without implying pressure.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"future continuous\\\",\\\"polite inquiry\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '10', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1790, '96dd4801-5661-499e-af16-5b1b7ee39456', 144, 4, 'What is the structure of the Future Perfect Tense?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Subject + will + be + V-ing\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Subject + will + have + V3\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Subject + will + have + been + V-ing\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Subject + had + V3\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Future perfect = will + have + past participle (V3). It describes an action completed before a specific future time.', 'Future perfect: will + have + V3.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"future perfect\\\",\\\"structure\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '11', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1791, 'b7298b4f-086e-4d95-9f0c-c8f3b6c6f8a1', 144, 4, 'Which sentence correctly uses the Future Perfect?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"By next month, she will finish her thesis.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"By next month, she has finished her thesis.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"By next month, she will have finished her thesis.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"By next month, she will be finishing her thesis.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'By next month\' + a completed action → future perfect: \'will have finished\'. The word \'by\' is the strongest signal.', '\'By\' + future time + completed action → future perfect (will + have + V3).', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"future perfect\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '11', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1792, '86491f1f-5a01-459e-b4e0-fdc58da214d5', 144, 4, 'Which word is the strongest signal for the Future Perfect Tense?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"when\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"while\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"by\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"since\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'By\' (e.g., by 6pm, by next year, by the time) is the most reliable signal for the future perfect tense.', '\'By\' + a future time = future perfect tense.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"future perfect\\\",\\\"signal words\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '11', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55');
INSERT INTO `mcqs` (`id`, `uuid`, `topic_id`, `subject_id`, `question`, `question_type`, `options`, `correct_answers`, `explanation`, `hint`, `difficulty_level`, `time_limit_seconds`, `marks`, `negative_marks`, `tags`, `reference_book`, `reference_page`, `is_premium`, `is_verified`, `status`, `created_by`, `approved_by`, `approved_at`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(1793, '0941ae03-ddba-43d3-969b-f1ef799bbb48', 144, 4, 'Which sentence contains an error in the Future Perfect?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"By the time you arrive, I will have finished cooking.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"She will have been complete the course by June.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"They will have submitted the report by Friday.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"By 2030, scientists will have discovered a cure.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', '\'Will have been complete\' is wrong. Future perfect requires will + have + past participle: \'will have completed the course by June.\'', 'Future perfect = will + have + past participle (V3). Never \'been complete\'.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"future perfect\\\",\\\"common errors\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '11', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1794, '34b8da42-1d80-4e35-8c27-6c03ce9ea4f5', 144, 4, 'What is the structure of the Future Perfect Continuous Tense?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Subject + will + have + V3\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Subject + will + be + V-ing\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Subject + will + have + been + V-ing\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Subject + had + been + V-ing\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Future perfect continuous = will + have + been + verb-ing. It emphasizes duration of an action up to a future point.', 'Future perfect continuous: will + have + been + V-ing.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"future perfect continuous\\\",\\\"structure\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '12', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1795, 'c6905568-9024-49d3-b98f-091b651635db', 144, 4, 'Which sentence correctly uses the Future Perfect Continuous?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"By next year, I will be working here for five years.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"By next year, I will have been working here for five years.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"By next year, I will have worked here for five years.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"By next year, I have been working here for five years.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Future perfect continuous emphasizes how long an action will have been ongoing by a future point: \'will have been working for five years\'.', 'By + future time + for + duration = future perfect continuous.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"future perfect continuous\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '12', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1796, '2ae52b37-d1b8-4893-a578-f5665045484d', 144, 4, 'What is the difference between \'By June, she will have written the book\' and \'By June, she will have been writing the book for eight months\'?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"No difference \\\\u2014 both are future perfect.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The first focuses on completion; the second focuses on duration of the ongoing process.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The first is incorrect.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"The second focuses on the result.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Future perfect = book will be done (result/completion). Future perfect continuous = how long she will have been writing (duration/process).', 'Perfect = result. Perfect continuous = duration of ongoing process.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"future perfect\\\",\\\"future perfect continuous\\\",\\\"comparison\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '12', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1797, 'e2742f1b-9407-4d4a-8939-7a8973040fd9', 144, 4, 'Which sentence incorrectly uses a stative verb in the Future Perfect Continuous?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"By then, she will have been working here for a decade.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"She will have known him for a decade by then.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"She will have been knowing him for a decade by then.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"By 2030, they will have been building the dam for ten years.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'Know\' is stative — it cannot be in any continuous form. Use future perfect instead: \'She will have known him for a decade by then.\'', 'Stative verbs cannot be in continuous form in any tense.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"future perfect continuous\\\",\\\"stative verbs\\\",\\\"common errors\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '12', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1798, 'ea4e7d36-c3ce-4b92-a08e-021f246fb2e9', 144, 4, 'Which sentence has an unnecessary tense shift?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"She walked into the room and sat down.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"She walked into the room and sits down.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"She walks into the room and sits down.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"She will walk in and sit down.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Both actions are in the same time frame. Mixing \'walked\' (past) and \'sits\' (present) is an unnecessary tense shift.', 'Sequential actions in the same time frame must use the same tense.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"tense consistency\\\",\\\"tense shift\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '13', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1799, '82f514c3-3e02-41a2-85e8-f8cc124f1bdb', 144, 4, 'In reported speech, \'She said, I am tired\' becomes:', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"She said that she is tired.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"She said that she was tired.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"She said that she has been tired.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"She said that she will be tired.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'In reported speech with a past reporting verb, the present simple shifts to simple past: \'am\' → \'was\'.', 'Reported speech backshifting: simple present → simple past.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"tense consistency\\\",\\\"reported speech\\\",\\\"backshifting\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '13', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1800, '4daa9f56-a54d-4338-a396-fec221887740', 144, 4, 'Which backshift is correct for reported speech: He said, \'I have finished the work\'?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"He said that he has finished the work.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"He said that he had finished the work.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"He said that he finished the work.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"He said that he will finish the work.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Present perfect → past perfect in reported speech: \'I have finished\' → \'he had finished\'.', 'Present perfect → past perfect in indirect speech.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"tense consistency\\\",\\\"reported speech\\\",\\\"backshifting\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '13', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1801, 'add8a876-cadf-4a75-96f4-4db8f757a074', 144, 4, 'Which sentence correctly avoids backshifting for a universal truth?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"The teacher said that the earth revolved around the sun.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The teacher said that the earth revolves around the sun.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The teacher said that the earth is revolving around the sun.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"The teacher said that the earth had revolved around the sun.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'Universal truths and scientific facts do not backshift in reported speech. \'Revolves\' remains in the present tense.', 'Scientific facts and universal truths stay in simple present — even in indirect speech.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"tense consistency\\\",\\\"reported speech\\\",\\\"universal truth\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '13', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1802, '3a151433-efcd-4811-802d-29a3f2050f16', 144, 4, 'Which conditional pattern is correct for a real future possibility?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"If she studied harder, she would pass.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"If she had studied harder, she would have passed.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"If she studies harder, she will pass.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"If she will study harder, she will pass.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'First conditional (real future): If + simple present … will + base form. \'If she studies, she will pass.\'', 'First conditional: if + simple present + will + base form.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"tense consistency\\\",\\\"conditionals\\\",\\\"first conditional\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '13', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1803, '94e035de-8eea-4f10-b6f7-fe457cebec5f', 144, 4, 'Which sentence correctly uses \'would rather\' with tense consistency?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"I would rather she stays home.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"I would rather she stay home.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"I would rather she stayed home.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"I would rather she will stay home.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'After \'would rather\' referring to another person\'s action, use the simple past (subjunctive): \'I would rather she stayed home.\'', 'Would rather + subject + simple past (subjunctive mood).', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"tense consistency\\\",\\\"would rather\\\",\\\"subjunctive\\\",\\\"tenses\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '13', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1804, 'a68be5ef-168b-4997-9785-409c081a484b', 144, 4, 'How many tenses are there in English grammar?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"9\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"10\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"12\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"16\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'English has 12 tenses: 4 aspects (Simple, Continuous, Perfect, Perfect Continuous) × 3 time frames (Present, Past, Future).', '3 time frames × 4 aspects = 12 tenses.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"tenses\\\",\\\"overview\\\",\\\"general\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1805, '52ff4d88-b831-4591-b74a-d1683512a007', 144, 4, 'Which tense uses \'had + been + V-ing\'?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Present Perfect Continuous\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Past Perfect Continuous\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Future Perfect Continuous\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Past Continuous\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', '\'Had + been + V-ing\' is the structure of the Past Perfect Continuous Tense.', 'Had = past perfect. Been + V-ing = continuous aspect.', 'easy', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"tenses\\\",\\\"structure identification\\\",\\\"general\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '8', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1806, 'f0d4726e-8f02-41c1-b631-24485601dc8c', 144, 4, 'Identify the tense: \'By the time she arrives, I will have prepared everything.\'', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Future Continuous\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Future Perfect Continuous\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Future Perfect\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Simple Future\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', '\'Will have prepared\' = will + have + past participle → Future Perfect Tense. Signalled by \'by the time\'.', 'Will + have + V3 = Future Perfect. \'By the time\' is a key signal.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"tenses\\\",\\\"identification\\\",\\\"future perfect\\\",\\\"general\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '11', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1807, '0f506146-7e22-4b38-8cd8-9a519cf279c0', 144, 4, 'Which tense is used to describe an action that will have been ongoing for a period up to a future point?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Future Perfect\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Future Continuous\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"Future Perfect Continuous\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"Present Perfect Continuous\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"3\\\"]\"', 'Future Perfect Continuous (will have been + V-ing) emphasizes the duration of an action that will still be ongoing up to a future point.', 'Duration up to a future point → Future Perfect Continuous.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"tenses\\\",\\\"future perfect continuous\\\",\\\"identification\\\",\\\"general\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '12', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1808, '729d5070-fd85-4694-9710-b7892321eb47', 144, 4, 'Which sentence uses the WRONG tense for the conditional?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"If you heat water to 100\\\\u00b0C, it boils.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"If she had applied, she would have got the job.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"If I had more time, I would learn a language.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"If she would study, she will pass.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"4\\\"]\"', 'In real/possible conditions (first conditional), the if-clause takes simple present — not \'would\'. \'If she studies, she will pass\' is correct.', 'Never use \'would\' in the if-clause of a first conditional.', 'hard', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"tenses\\\",\\\"conditionals\\\",\\\"tense consistency\\\",\\\"general\\\"]\"', 'English Grammar Guide', '13', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 11:42:55', '2026-05-13 11:42:55'),
(1809, 'a92cd4a8-a8f7-4e7c-9f49-5ff1e9974534', 143, 4, 'Which sentence is in active voice?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"The work was completed by Ali.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"Ali completed the work.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"The work is being completed.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"The work has been completed.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'In active voice, the subject performs the action.', 'Identify the doer of the action.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Introduction to Voice\\\"]\"', 'N/A', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 15:28:17', '2026-05-13 15:28:17'),
(1810, 'c0aebdac-14b8-4e92-ba7d-fa7cd88a705c', 143, 4, 'Which sentence is in passive voice?', 'single', '\"{\\\"1\\\":\\\"Sara wrote a letter.\\\",\\\"2\\\":\\\"The letter was written by Sara.\\\",\\\"3\\\":\\\"They cleaned the room.\\\",\\\"4\\\":\\\"He repairs cars.\\\"}\"', '\"[\\\"2\\\"]\"', 'In passive voice, the subject receives the action.', 'Look for a form of \'be\' + past participle.', 'medium', NULL, 1, 0, '\"[\\\"Introduction to Voice\\\"]\"', 'N/A', '1', 0, 0, 'published', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 15:28:17', '2026-05-13 15:28:17'),
